  {"a":"aurora","b":"aatrox","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Aatrox's Q sweetspot rhythm plus Infernal Chains at 3 is his window to run you down — never sit in the slow zone of his W with your Q (Twofold Hex) and W leap both on cooldown, or he snaps you back into a sweetspot Q knockup and drains the trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your peak: drop the rift on him so its damage/slow zones him, and W into the spirit realm so you go untargetable to him from outside — he can't connect his R-empowered sweetspot Q while you exorcise spirits off him and heal the chip back via Spirit Abjuration."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first bruiser item (Eclipse-style) reclaims the lane — once Aatrox can hold an extended trade, his Q-sweetspot healing and Deathbringer drain out-sustain your Twofold Hex poke, so stop standing to trade him."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items it's a skirmish coinflip: your Q burst plus W-reset roams vs his combat-stat R all-in, so catch him with max-range Q and let your team body him in the 5v5 instead of dueling his drain stats."}],"wants":{"you":["Fire Twofold Hex out then recast the pull for the double-hit while Spirit Abjuration exorcises spirits off him and heals your poke back","Reach 6 and fight inside Between Worlds — W into the spirit realm so you go untargetable to him from outside and his R-empowered sweetspot Q can't connect","Use The Weirding's backward hop and the W leap's invisibility to slip out of his Infernal Chains slow zone before it snaps you back into a sweetspot Q"],"foe":["Land all three Q sweetspots and lock you with Infernal Chains so the chains snap you back into the knockup for a long drain trade","Bait out your W leap, then all-in with R combat stats while your only repositioning tool is down","Stack Q-sweetspot and Deathbringer healing through your poke and outscale you into a 2-item drain bruiser"]},"early":"Level 1 you're both low-threat — he has no sweetspot rhythm yet and you only have Twofold Hex with no W leap, so just last-hit and learn his Q angles. From 2 you can open the poke war: fire Twofold Hex out, recast the pull for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the chip back. But the moment he hits 3 with Q1-Q2-Q3 plus Infernal Chains online he out-trades you flat — do NOT stand in his W slow zone where it snaps you back into a sweetspot Q, and never burn your W leap to chase a kill before 6, because once it's down he chains you and runs you over.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a genuine coinflip: your poke, Spirit Abjuration sustain, and W cooldown line up, but so does his drain trade, so only commit when you can hop a Q with The Weirding and disengage before Infernal Chains snaps you back. Level 6 is your window to seize — drop Between Worlds so the rift damages and slows him, then W into the spirit realm so you go untargetable to him from outside while you chip him through his R-empowered combo. Land a Q burst into a takedown here and the W reset lets you snowball before his first item comes online.","late":"Once he finishes his first bruiser item (Eclipse-class) his Q-sweetspot healing and Deathbringer drain out-sustain your poke and the lane tilts back to him, so stop trading him straight. He's a drain bruiser with a teamfight R; you're a skirmish-mage who lives on W-reset roams. Use Between Worlds' wall-walk and your W invisibility to fight on YOUR terms, catch him with a max-range Twofold Hex before he can extend the trade, and let your team body him in the 5v5 rather than feeding his combat-stat all-in 1v1.","whys":["Neither of you wants level 1 — he has no Q sweetspot rhythm and you have only Twofold Hex with no W leap, so just trade last-hits.","You get Twofold Hex poke and Spirit Abjuration sustain online, but his level-2 Q sweetspot still threatens a knockup, so it stays even.","At 3 his full Q-sweetspot combo and Infernal Chains out-trade your poke — the chains snap you back and he drains you faster than Spirit Abjuration heals it.","Your poke-and-disengage with The Weirding meets his drain trade — fight only when you can hop a Q and leave before the chains, so it's genuinely even.","Between Worlds lets you W untargetable to him from outside while the rift zones him, so you dodge his R-empowered sweetspot Q and exorcise-heal through his all-in.","His first bruiser item plus Q-sweetspot and Deathbringer healing out-sustains your Twofold Hex poke once he can hold an extended trade.","At 2+ items it's a skirmish coinflip — your W-reset roams and Q burst vs his combat-stat R all-in, so group instead of dueling his drain stats."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"akali","win":["Skill","Akali","Akali","Skill","Skill","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Akali has only her Q and no Twilight Shroud to vanish into yet, so open with Twofold Hex, recast it to pull the curse back through her for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the trade back before she can answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aurora's R, Between Worlds, is the level-6 swing: drop the rift and you become untargetable to Akali from outside it, so her R two-part dash and execute fizzles and she cannot all-in you the way she does most squishies."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Akali's first AP item (Hextech Rocketbelt/Riftmaker) is her real spike — she sits in W shroud untargetable, dashes in with E shuriken, and bursts you before Spirit Abjuration can heal, while your Q poke whiffs into the smoke."},{"when":"Late","text":"Both of you are item-scaling assassins trading untargetability windows — your R rift versus her W shroud — so it comes down to who lands the first clean Q-curse or E-shuriken engage rather than raw scaling."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level-1 poke race with Twofold Hex and the recast pull while Akali has only Q and no shroud to disappear into","Save R, Between Worlds, as your level-6 trump card — the rift makes you untargetable to her from outside, so her R dash-execute simply cannot land on you","Use E, The Weirding, to slow-and-hop backward out of her E shuriken range, kiting the trade instead of standing in her energy poke"],"foe":["Drop W Twilight Shroud mid-trade to go untargetable, breaking your Q-curse lock-on and resetting the poke war on her terms","Hit her first AP item so the W-shroud into E-shuriken burst kills you before Spirit Abjuration heals the trade back","Bait your W leap or R, then E-shuriken in and execute you with R the instant your untargetability window is on cooldown"]},"early":"Level 1 is genuinely yours: Akali has only her Q and no Twilight Shroud to hide in, so curse her with Twofold Hex, recast it to drag the curse back through her for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the trade back while she has no untargetability to answer with. Once she can put a point in W the lane flips to a coin-flip — she drops the shroud to break your Q's lock-on and your missile sails through empty smoke. Last-hit at max Q range, never walk up to auto into her energy poke, and accept that the early levels even out fast once that shroud is online.","mid":"This is the stretch you have to survive. Once Akali has her E shuriken and an AP item, she dictates the trades — she sits in W shroud untargetable, dashes in with E, and your Q/E poke can't lock onto her through the smoke. Hold your W leap and your R rift as escape buttons, not engage tools: the moment your untargetability window is down she can E-in, R-dash, and execute you. Keep your back to your turret, ward your flanks for her roams, and only contest CS you can grab without stepping inside shroud-and-dash range. Note her R is also a powerful gank-confirm, so she may look to roam rather than out-trade you straight up.","late":"By the time you both have items the matchup levels back out — your R, Between Worlds, makes you untargetable to her from outside the rift, the direct mirror to her W shroud, and whoever lands the first clean engage wins the skirmish. You are not hard-outscaled here the way you are versus a Mordekaiser or Olaf; it's an even assassin-versus-skirmisher trade. Use your R wall-walk to roam and make picks elsewhere rather than forcing the 1v1, and in fights save your W reset to peel her dive off your carries instead of dueling her into the shroud.","whys":["Akali has only her Q and no W Twilight Shroud at level 1, so your Twofold Hex poke and recast pull land clean and Spirit Abjuration heals the raw trade in your favour.","Once her W shroud can be leveled she goes untargetable to break your Q's lock-on in the smoke, so the poke war evens out and you trade hex-for-energy.","With Q, E and shroud all online it's a pure skill matchup — you poke-and-hop with E, she pokes-and-vanishes with W, and neither lands a clean commit.","Her E shuriken dash plus first-item power lets her engage on her terms while your slower Q poke can't punish a shroud she re-enters at will.","Akali's first AP item sharpens the W-shroud into E-shuriken burst faster than your poke ramps, so she out-DPSes your trade window once she has gold.","With items up her R two-part dash and execute can kill you the instant your W leap or R rift is on cooldown — her clearest spike in the lane.","By now you're both item-scaling assassins trading untargetability — your R rift answers her shroud evenly, so the fight goes to whoever lands the first clean engage, not to raw scaling."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"akshan","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Before Akshan has Heroic Swing charges or a Dirty Fighting mark stacked, you can land Twofold Hex, recast it for the curse-pull second hit, and walk off with a Spirit Abjuration heal — your one clean early window."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once Akshan has Avengerang (hits out AND back) plus Heroic Swing, he hit-and-runs your single-target Q poke and chunks you with the mark-detonation auto every time you step up to CS."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Comeuppance is a channeled ranged execute that scales with your missing HP — after his Q double-hit softens you, it deletes you from screen-edge and your W leap can't dodge a locked channel."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Luden's/Malignance online: your Q-recast burst finally one-shots his squishy lethality build, and three stacked Spirit Abjuration heals out-sustain his Avengerang chip in any extended trade."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q (Twofold Hex) and recast it for the curse-pull second hit so two Spirit Abjuration spirits drift back and fund the trade","Save W (Across the Veil) to leap his Heroic Swing re-entry or break his Comeuppance line of sight, never to engage a ranged kiter pre-6","Farm to 2+ items where Luden's burst lets a Q-pull + E combo delete his no-defense lethality build before his poke matters"],"foe":["Land Avengerang's return hit and proc the Dirty Fighting mark with an auto so his poke out-trades your single Q","Use Going Rogue camouflage to disengage your E-poke, roam mid/bot, and return to punish your shoved wave","Channel Comeuppance for the missing-HP execute while your W and E are down — the ranged execute ignores your leap"]},"early":"Level 1 is your one early gift: before Akshan has a Heroic Swing charge or a stacked Dirty Fighting mark, fire Twofold Hex, recast it for the curse-pull second hit, and let two Spirit Abjuration spirits heal you back — take that trade and respect everything after. The moment he hits 2 and 3, Avengerang pokes on both the throw and the return while his mark-detonation auto adds burst, and Going Rogue camouflage lets him reset any trade he loses, so stop walking up. Last-hit at max Q range, sidestep his boomerang line, and do NOT burn W or E chasing — you need W to leap his swing-in and E to disengage-poke.","mid":"This is his window, not yours. Akshan's Avengerang double-hit plus Heroic Swing lets him poke-and-reposition faster than your spirit heal ticks up, and the mark detonation chunks you off every wave you over-extend on. Don't enter a poke war — your E hops you back after a slow but won't out-trade his hit-and-run, and if you waste W as an engage his next swing catches you with nothing to dodge with. At 6 his Comeuppance is a channeled ranged execute that scales with your missing HP, so the more his Q has chipped you the harder it bites; your R can zone the rift and turn you untargetable to break his channel, but it's an escape here, not a pick — play for waves and farm.","late":"You finally flip it at 2+ items. Once Luden's/Malignance lands, your Q-recast burst goes from poke to one-shot, and Akshan stacks lethality with no defensive items — a clean Twofold Hex pull plus E and a W reposition deletes him before his boomerang matters. Three stacked Spirit Abjuration heals now out-sustain his Avengerang chip in any extended trade. Use Between Worlds to drop the rift, walk a wall, and go untargetable to his swing or Comeuppance, then punish — but never face-check his Going Rogue camouflage near objectives, because he'll scout you, pick you when you're alone, and revive a fallen ally off the kill.","whys":["At level 1 he has no Heroic Swing charge and no stacked mark — land Twofold Hex, recast the curse-pull, and two Spirit Abjuration spirits heal you for a free trade.","Avengerang pokes on the throw AND the return and his mark-detonation auto adds burst, while Going Rogue camouflage lets him reset any trade he loses — concede the step-up.","With his boomerang and Heroic Swing online he hit-and-runs your single-target poke and chunks your CS faster than your spirit heal recovers it.","His swing-and-poke kite beats your tempo: spend W as an engage and his Heroic Swing re-entry catches you with no leap left to dodge.","Comeuppance is a channeled ranged execute scaling with your missing HP; after his Q softens you it deletes you, and your W leap can't escape a locked channel.","His first lethality item sharpens the Avengerang-and-mark burst that your three-stack spirit sustain still can't out-DPS in lane.","At 2+ items your Luden's Q-recast one-shots his no-defense lethality build and stacked Spirit Abjuration heals out-last his chip — the duel is finally yours."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"ambessa","win":["Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa","Skill","Skill","Ambessa","Ambessa"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke war opens: fire Twofold Hex, recast to drag the curse back through her for the double hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the chip so her early dash-trades net nothing."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your best window — Q cooldown, passive healing, and Across the Veil all line up so you out-poke and out-space her before either of you has an ult."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Lane flips: Between Worlds is your escape, not a kill button here — when she dashes in and starts her chain-CC + W damage, pop R to go untargetable and walk out rather than trading ults straight up."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once her first bruiser item and leveled dashes come online, one dash combo chains CC onto your squishy mage body while your W and R are down and she wins the straight duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Twofold Hex and recast it to pull the curse back through her for the second hit, then let Spirit Abjuration heal the trade before she dashes in","Save Across the Veil as a dash-dodge/reset, not just a poke tool — its takedown reset snowballs the pre-6 war, but you need it up when she commits","Hold Between Worlds for her all-in so you go untargetable through her chain-CC and W damage instead of trading ults head-on"],"foe":["Weave her dashes around your Q missile and E blast so your poke whiffs and you burn cooldowns for nothing","Wait out Across the Veil, then dash in and land chain CC to lock your squishy body before dumping W damage","Drag the lane to 2+ items where her bruiser stats and CC chain out-duel your mage once your W and R are on cooldown"]},"early":"Level 1 you are a single-spell mage with no escape up yet, so concede it — last-hit at the tip of Twofold Hex and never step into her dash range. From level 2-3 start the poke war: fire Q, recast it to drag the curse back through her for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the chip so her dash-trades go nowhere. The danger is her mobility — she weaves dashes around your Q missile and your E blast, so do not blow The Weirding as your only disengage early, because once it is down she can dash in and chain-CC you with no answer left.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your best window: your Q cooldown, passive healing, and Across the Veil line up so you control spacing and out-poke her before either of you has an ult to swing it. Bait her dash, E-blast and hop back, then Q-recast through her — and keep Across the Veil for the dodge, not just the poke. At 6 the lane flips: Between Worlds is your lifeline, not your kill button here. When she dashes in and opens her chain-CC plus W damage, pop R to go untargetable and walk out, because trade ults straight up and her CC lands while your W is down and she wins it.","late":"This is her half of the matchup. Once her first bruiser item and leveled dashes come online, one dash combo chains CC onto you and her stats win the straight duel — you are a squishy mage and your only outs are W and R on cooldown. Never get caught with Across the Veil down; play for poke and side-lane pick-offs where her dashes or CC are spent, and lean on your team to peel her engage. If you let the lane go even to 2+ items, she takes over the duel.","whys":["You are a no-escape single-spell mage at level 1, but Ambessa's combo is also weak before her dashes are leveled — deny her CS and set your spacing without stepping into dash range.","Even skirmish: your Twofold Hex out-and-recast poke trades with her early dash-pokes, and Spirit Abjuration heals enough that neither side wins the exchange yet.","Her dash mobility weaves around your Q missile and E blast and closes the gap, so once The Weirding is down she dictates the trade and can chain-CC you.","Levels 4-5 your Q cooldown, passive healing, and Across the Veil all line up — you out-poke and out-space her in the only window before ultimates swing it.","Between Worlds keeps you alive but Ambessa owns the all-in: her dash-in chain-CC plus W damage lands while your W is on cooldown and wins the straight ult trade.","Her first bruiser item plus leveled dashes turns one combo into a kill before Across the Veil resets — she punishes any caught positioning hard.","At 2+ items her bruiser stats and CC chain out-duel your squishy body; once your W and R are down she locks you and wins every straight fight."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"camille","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Camille"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q (Twofold Hex) plus E (The Weirding) online you open the poke war: curse her, recast Q to pull it back for the second hit, and E to slow-and-hop before her melee kit can close the gap."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds zones her off the all-in and lets you phase through a wall to dodge her E hookshot; W resets on takedown, so your cleanest kill window before her Trinity Force spike snowballs."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-pull combo so one rotation bursts her before she lands her E-stun into Q-W true-damage chunk."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Camille has Trinity Force plus a bruiser item her R (Hextech Ultimatum) walls you into a 1v1 and her E-stun connects while your W leap is down — this is her window."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the poke war with Q curse-pulls and E slows while your passive heals the spirits back off every spell you land","Reach 6 and use Between Worlds to zone her engage or phase through a wall to dodge her E hookshot, then snowball off the W takedown reset","Burst her with your Luden's-spike Q combo and close the game before her Trinity Force and bruiser items come online"],"foe":["Land her E hookshot stun the instant your W leap is on cooldown to lock you for the E-Q-W combo","Stick to you for the Q true-damage proc and W true-damage cone heal to out-trade your poke up close","Survive lane and use R (Hextech Ultimatum) to wall you into a 1v1 once her items out-scale your kit"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you are a single-spell mage with no leap yet and she has her E wall-dash, so don't get caught stepping up for a Q. Once you have Q plus E at levels 2-3 you take over: fire Q (Twofold Hex) to curse her, recast to pull the curse back for the second hit, and E (The Weirding) to slow and hop away before she can close. Your passive, Spirit Abjuration, heals you off every spell that lands, so you win the poke exchange outright as long as you never let her E hookshot stun connect — that stun is her only way to flip a trade this early.","mid":"This is your lane. At 4-5 your poke, passive sustain, and W cooldown line up so you control spacing and chip her down off CS. At 6, Between Worlds is the difference-maker — drop the rift to zone her off any engage, or walk through a wall to dodge her E hookshot, and remember W resets on takedown so one kill snowballs into the next. Bait her E, leap away with W when she commits, then Q-pull burst her while she's stuck on the cooldown. Don't sit in her W cone trading autos — keep it a ranged poke war where her true damage can't reach you.","late":"Camille is a hard scaler and this is where she reclaims it. Once she has Trinity Force and a bruiser item her R (Hextech Ultimatum) drops a wall around you, cuts off your W escape, and forces the 1v1 her true-damage Q proc and W cone win. You stay a squishy mage the moment your leap is down. Win on the lead you built early-mid — group, take towers, and convert your poke advantage into objectives before her items come online. Never get caught alone in side lane after ~2 items, because her R-isolate into E-stun is built to delete exactly your kit.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you are a no-leap single-spell mage and she has only her E wall-dash, so neither can commit; deny her last-hits and set up your spell levels.","Q plus E come online and her melee kit has no answer to ranged curse-pulls — start chipping her down while your passive heals every spell back.","With Q-pull burst and E disengage you out-trade her up close; your passive sustains the war while she has only her E stun to punish a step-up.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all peak at 4-5 — you control spacing and zone her off CS before her items matter.","Between Worlds zones her engage and lets you phase through walls to dodge her E hookshot, and the W-reset-on-takedown turns one kill into a snowball.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-pull combo so you delete her before she lands E into her Q-W true-damage chunk — force the all-in now.","She out-scales hard: her R walls you into a 1v1, cuts off your W escape, and her true-damage Q proc and W cone win the duel once her Trinity Force and bruiser items come online."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once your Q (Twofold Hex) curse plus its pull-back recast is online, you out-poke her single Noxious Blast before her poison ramps — her Twin Fang has nothing to feed on yet."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Across the Veil into spirit mode lets you blink behind her and Between Worlds drops you untargetable to her, so Petrifying Gaze can't catch your face — then W resets on the kill."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance burst behind your Q-out, Q-recast double-hit two-shots her squishy frame before her poison can stack Twin Fang to lethal — your last clean kill window."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Cassiopeia's whole identity: with two items her stacked Noxious Blast/Miasma poison and Twin Fang spam out-sustain your burst, and her passive move speed kites you out of Q range."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the early poke war with Q-out into Q-recast double-hits while your passive Spirit Abjuration heals back the poison chip she lands","Use your level-6 spike to W behind her and pop Between Worlds untargetable so Petrifying Gaze whiffs, then W-reset the kill","Snowball the lead and end before her two-item poison spike, because you can't out-sustain her ramped Twin Fang DPS"],"foe":["Stack poison with Noxious Blast (Q) and Miasma (E), then spam Twin Fang (W) on poisoned targets to out-DPS your burst-and-heal trades","Hold Miasma (E) to ground you the instant you commit, stopping your Across the Veil leap so you can't reposition or disengage","Survive your early-and-6 windows to two items, where her ramped poison and passive move speed reclaim the kite and the lane"]},"early":"Her early chip is just Noxious Blast (Q) — Twin Fang only spikes once she has poison ramping and items to pay for the mana, so right now your passive Spirit Abjuration heals through her chip and you win the poke war. Trade with Q-out, then recast Twofold Hex to drag the curse back through her for the second hit, and use E (The Weirding) to slow her and hop yourself backward before she can land a follow-up. Do not facetank her at point-blank: her boots-free passive move speed lets her walk with you, so poke at max range and let your spirits drift home and heal.","mid":"This is your takeover. Your Q double-hit plus E poke out-trades her ramping poison while your passive sustain eats the chip she lands. The whole lane is her Miasma (E) — she wants it ready to ground you the moment you commit, killing your Across the Veil leap so you can't get on her or get out. Bait the Miasma first; once it's down, W behind her, Q-recast for the burst, and use Between Worlds so you're untargetable to her — Petrifying Gaze only petrifies enemies facing her, and it can't lock something it can't target. At 6 your W resets on the takedown and you snowball.","late":"You own every window up to your first item, but Cassiopeia is a brutal scaler — at two-plus items her stacked Noxious Blast and Miasma poison plus rapid-fire Twin Fang out-DPS your burst, and her passive move speed keeps her spacing just outside your Q. Once her poison ramps fully she shrugs off your combo and chips you down faster than Spirit Abjuration can heal, and a single Miasma ground deletes your escape. Close the lane on your level-6 and first-item spikes: force the all-in while Miasma is still her only real answer, and end the game before her two-item DPS makes the duel unwinnable.","whys":["She has passive move speed but only Noxious Blast at level 1 — your passive sustain matches her chip while neither of you can hard-commit.","Your Q curse plus its pull-back recast lets you double-hit and trade up before her Twin Fang has stacked poison to feed on.","With the Q-recast and E online, your double-hit poke out-damages her ramping poison and your healing eats what she lands.","Your poke, passive heal, and W tempo line up — you control every trade while her DPS still needs items to come online.","Across the Veil blinks you behind her and Between Worlds makes you untargetable, so Petrifying Gaze whiffs and W resets the kill.","Luden's-class burst plus the Q-recast two-shots her squishy frame before her poison stacks lethal — your last clean kill window.","Cassiopeia out-scales hard: at two items her stacked poison and Twin Fang spam out-DPS your burst and her move speed kites you — play the lead you already built."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"chogath","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Cho'Gath"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Open the poke war the moment you have Q (Twofold Hex) plus E (The Weirding) — chip Cho'Gath's HP and heal the return fire with Spirit Abjuration before any Feast stacks pad his bar."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your snowball window: drop the rift and step out of it and he can't target you, so his Rupture and Feral Scream are wasted unless he walks in after you — burst him and chase the W reset on a kill."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's or Malignance sharpens the Q-recast double-hit — force trades on his Rupture and Feral Scream cooldowns and end the lane before his Feast HP balloons past your burst."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Feast becomes a true-damage percent-HP execute that ignores your Spirit Abjuration sustain entirely — once he has tank items and stacks, respect the Rupture-into-silence and stop committing all-ins."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the Q (Twofold Hex) / E (The Weirding) poke war and heal the trade with Spirit Abjuration before Feast stacks balloon his HP bar","Sidestep his Rupture with W (Across the Veil), then recast Q to pull the curse back through him for the second hit while his silence is wasted","Snowball levels 2 through 6 and close the lane before his Feast HP and Feast-execute R make him unkillable"],"foe":["Land Q (Rupture) knockup into W (Feral Scream) silence to lock out your W escape and burst you while your spells are down","Farm safely, dodge the Q-recast poke, and stack Feast on minions and monsters to push his HP past your burst threshold","Reach 2+ items so the true-damage Feast execute and tank stats shrug off everything you can throw at him"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you're a one-spell mage with no escape until W, and Cho'Gath just wants to last-hit and dodge a Q (Twofold Hex), so don't overcommit before your kit is online. From level 2 you take over: poke with Q and recast it to drag the curse back through him for a second hit, weave in E (The Weirding) to chip and slow as it hops you back to safety, and let Spirit Abjuration heal you through the return trade. The one thing to respect is his Q (Rupture) — it's a delayed ground knockup, so sidestep it and his W (Feral Scream) silence has nothing to chain off. Every time those two are on cooldown, walk up and punish.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your window — poke, passive healing, and your W cooldown all line up while his HP bar is still small enough for your burst to bite. Keep landing Q recasts and E pokes, and bait his Rupture with a W (Across the Veil) leap before you commit. At 6, Between Worlds is the difference-maker: drop the rift and step outside it and he can't target you, so his Rupture and Feral Scream are wasted unless he follows you in — burst him down and grab the W reset if you take the kill. Just don't dawdle inside the rift with him, because once he's in there with you the untargetability is gone. This is the stretch where you build the lead that has to carry the lane.","late":"This is where Cho'Gath reclaims the lane. Once he has 2+ items and a few Feast (R) stacks of bonus HP, his ultimate is a true-damage percent-HP execute that ignores your Spirit Abjuration sustain completely — you can't poke or heal through it. A clean Rupture-into-Feral Scream catches you with your W down, and the Feast finishes you before you can leap out. Stop diving him, use your R rift to escape and zone rather than to all-in, and cash in the lead you built at 2-6. If the game drags long he simply out-tanks you, so your job was to have ended it before this point.","whys":["At level 1 you're a low-threat one-spell mage with no escape until W, but Cho'Gath only wants to last-hit and not eat a Twofold Hex — neither of you owns it.","With Q (Twofold Hex) and E (The Weirding) online you open the poke war and W-dodge his Rupture knockup, chipping his HP before Feast stacks pad it.","The Q-recast double-hit and E slow out-trade an immobile Cho'Gath, and Spirit Abjuration heals you back faster than he can punish.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all peak here while his HP bar is still small enough for your burst to matter.","Between Worlds makes you untargetable to him from outside the rift, so his Rupture and Feral Scream are wasted unless he chases you in — burst and grab the W reset on a kill.","Your Luden's or Malignance spike sharpens the Q-recast burst — force all-ins on his Rupture and Feral Scream cooldowns before his Feast HP scales out of reach.","His Feast becomes a true-damage percent-HP execute that ignores your sustain, and his Feast HP and tank items shrug off your poke — he owns the late duel."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"darius","win":["Aurora","Skill","Darius","Darius","Aurora","Darius","Darius"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Darius owns the early all-in: his E (Apprehend) pull yanks you out of position and his Decimate sweet-spot plus Hemorrhage bleed shreds you before your Q poke or passive heal can pay off."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your power window. Across the Veil leaps his 26s Apprehend and Between Worlds slows him and teleports you across the rift, so you poke him low and leave before Noxian Guillotine is in its 460-unit range."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Twofold Hex recast burst. Chunk him from outside E-pull range and let your passive heal off the spirits while he eats poke he can't trade back."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Respect his Hemorrhage execute in skirmishes: one E into your team stacks bleed fast, and his R refreshes on every kill, so don't get caught with Across the Veil down."}],"wants":{"you":["Stay outside his E (Apprehend) range and poke with Twofold Hex, then recast it to pull the curse back for the second hit while your passive heals the bleed chip","Bait his E, and the instant it whiffs use Across the Veil to leap clear so his Decimate sweet-spot misses","Reach 6 even, then use the Between Worlds slow zone and its side-to-side teleport to break his all-in before Hemorrhage reaches five stacks on you"],"foe":["Land E (Apprehend) to pull you in, then Decimate sweet-spot plus Hemorrhage stacks for a free all-in trade","Stack five Hemorrhage bleeds to empower his Decimate and chunk you faster than your passive spirits can heal","Catch you with Across the Veil on cooldown so his Hemorrhage-execute Noxian Guillotine confirms the kill"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Darius and you cannot fight him here. His E (Apprehend) pull drags you into Decimate sweet-spot range, and Hemorrhage's bleed out-damages your passive spirit-heal in any extended trade before your Q poke matters. Do NOT step up to last-hit inside E range. Take the slow push and farm with Twofold Hex from max distance. The trap is throwing a Q to poke, eating an E for it, and getting Decimate-sweetspotted plus bled before Across the Veil is even leveled to escape.","mid":"Levels 4-5 even out as your Q cooldown drops and your passive spirits let you chip the bleed back, but 6 is where you flip the lane. Between Worlds turns you untargetable to enemies outside the rift and lets you walk through walls, so when he commits an all-in you simply rift out before Noxian Guillotine can confirm. Poke him with Twofold Hex (fire, then recast to pull the curse back through him for the second hit), let the bleed-vs-heal math favor you, and if he E-pulls, leap out with Across the Veil. Every takedown resets that W, so a clean kill snowballs hard.","late":"Your first item (Luden's/Malignance) turns the lane into a range war he can't win. Burst him from outside E-pull range and he has no way to close the gap on you. The danger is roams and ganks: his E into your team during a skirmish stacks Hemorrhage fast and bypasses your spacing, and his Noxian Guillotine refreshes on every kill to chain through fights. Group with vision, never face-check for his pull, and save Between Worlds and Across the Veil to disengage the moment he commits.","whys":["Darius is a level-1 monster and you are a single-target mage with no escape leveled yet. His E pull plus Decimate sweet-spot out-trades anything you can throw.","Once E is online, any step into Apprehend range ends with a Decimate sweet-spot and a Hemorrhage stack your passive heal can't keep up with.","His bleed math beats your passive spirits in extended trades. Your Q poke just bait-feeds him an E-pull all-in, so concede CS and hold range.","Levels 4-5 are a coin-flip on spacing: your shorter Q cooldown and passive sustain let you chip the bleed back, but one mistimed step into his E still kills you.","Between Worlds slows him and teleports you across the rift while Across the Veil leaps his 26s Apprehend, so this is the window where Guillotine never reaches 460 units and you poke him out safely.","Your Luden's/Malignance Twofold Hex burst chunks him from outside E range, but he's still a Hemorrhage-execute threat in any skirmish, so the lane stays trade-of-poke-versus-pull.","You out-range his lane, but his E into a teammate plus the Guillotine reset still swings teamfights. Your rift keeps you alive but doesn't carry the fight by itself."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"drmundo","win":["Skill","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo","Skill","Skill","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Mundo can only throw cleavers (Q) level 1 and has no escape — fire Twofold Hex (Q) and recast it to drag the curse back through him for a second hit while he's the weakest body on the map."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Q cleaver percent-HP chip plus his passive (which heals him for a chunk every few seconds) out-sustains your Spirit Abjuration heals and lets him shove you off the wave — his strongest lane window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds slows him and teleports you across the rift, so you leave Heart Zapper's 325-unit burst and he heals nothing — your one clean all-in before Maximum Dosage."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Maximum Dosage (R) regens most of a health bar over its duration, so even a flawless Twofold Hex poke war stalls into a kill you simply can't close."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his cleaver (Q) onto minions, then Twofold Hex out and recast the curse back through him while his Q is down","Use the Between Worlds rift slow at 6 to leave Heart Zapper's 325 units before it bursts, so he heals none of it","Roam off your wave with Across the Veil (W) invisibility and E disengage — snowball before his second item heals through your burst"],"foe":["Land cleaver (Q) percent-HP poke and let his passive regen win the war of attrition","Drag the lane past two items so Maximum Dosage (R) makes him effectively unkillable to a lone mage","Walk you down with the cleaver slow whenever your Across the Veil (W) leap is on cooldown"]},"early":"Mundo can only throw cleavers (Q) at level 1 and has no escape, so step up and chunk him with a Twofold Hex (Q) — fire it through him, then recast to drag the curse back for a second hit while your Spirit Abjuration spirits heal you through his return poke. The problem starts once his Q and passive are both online: the cleaver's percent-HP chip plus his passive heal (a sizable tick every few seconds) out-sustains your poke, and a whiffed cleaver is the only real mistake you can tax. Last-hit at Q range, never eat free cleaver poke, and don't burn your Across the Veil (W) leap dodging a single cleaver when you'll want it for a committed trade.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are his window, not yours — his passive regen plus cleaver outheals your spirit sustain, and he can shove the wave in and walk you down with the cleaver slow whenever your Across the Veil (W) is on cooldown. Hold your real trades for 6: Between Worlds (R) makes you untargetable to him mid-fight so his cleaver and E bonus damage whiff, and that's the one all-in his sustain can't bail him out of yet. Bait the cleaver onto the wave, poke with Twofold Hex and E-hop back to safety, then commit your Q combo plus the W leap the instant his cleaver is down — your only clean kill pressure lives on his Q cooldown.","late":"This is where the lane settles into a stalemate: Maximum Dosage (R) regens most of a health bar over its channel, so your Twofold Hex burst and poke war simply can't kill a Mundo who plays the long fight. You don't lose the 1v1 outright — Across the Veil and Between Worlds keep you slippery enough to walk away — but you can't finish him, and his percent-HP cleaver scales hard into your squishy mage health pool. Stop dueling him: use W invisibility and E disengage to roam and cash your poke priority elsewhere, and leave the drain tank for your team's anti-heal or true damage rather than feeding him a fight he can't lose.","whys":["Mundo is the weakest level-1 here — one cleaver, no dash — so a Twofold Hex (Q) cast-and-recast double-hit chunks him for free before his regen matters.","He gets his cleaver but you get your Q plus Spirit Abjuration sustain — neither can hard-commit, so first-blood pressure hinges on who whiffs a cleaver dodge.","With cleaver and passive heal both online his percent-HP chip out-sustains your spirit heals and he can shove you off the wave.","Levels 3-5 his heal-through-trades plus cleaver slow let him walk you down the moment your Across the Veil (W) leap is down.","Between Worlds rifts you out of Heart Zapper's 325-unit burst, so it heals him nothing — your clean all-in before Maximum Dosage.","His first-item sustain out-heals your early item poke spike, so the war of attrition tilts back toward Mundo.","Maximum Dosage (R) regens most of a health bar so you can't close the kill, but your W/R escape means he can't catch you either — a stalemate."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"fiora","win":["Aurora","Skill","Fiora","Fiora","Aurora","Fiora","Fiora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Fiora Q-dashes onto you to proc a vital, and with only one spell and no W leap yet you have no answer — eat the percent-HP true damage and farm at range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one real window — the rift slow plus the cross-zone teleport lets you break her vital chain and set up an all-in if her Flash and 24s Riposte are down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance poke spike — chip her from max Q range and recast-pull so she never lands a clean vital before her dash comes back up."},{"when":"1st item (her)","text":"Fiora's first item (Eclipse/Shojin) is her kill threshold — if she Riposte-stuns your E or Q cast in the all-in, your W escape can't save you before her vitals finish you."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with the Q missile and recast-pull plus E from max range so her dash never closes onto a vital for free","Bank your W leap as a panic escape, not a trade tool — only hop after she has burned her Q-dash","Hit Level 6 even and use the Between Worlds rift slow and cross-zone teleport to break her vital chain early"],"foe":["Riposte your E or Q damage cast to stun you, then dash in and finish before your spirit-heal sustains you back","Q-dash onto a vital every time your spells are down and proc percent-max-HP true damage you can't out-trade","Reach 2 items and side-lane 1v1 you where her sustained vital DPS beats your cooldown-gated Q burst"]},"early":"Fiora owns these levels and you have to accept it. At Level 1 you are a single-spell mage with no W leap, so do not contest a last hit she can Q-dash onto — eat the vital, farm at range, and never trade autos. Your passive spirit-heal sustains the chip war, but it does nothing against her percent-HP vitals plus true damage, so the moment you throw Q to last-hit she dashes in and procs a vital before your recast-pull lands. Keep W up purely as a panic button, never as a trade opener, until you have E at 3.","mid":"This is your only foothold. Once Q poke, E slow-and-hop, and passive healing line up, you can finally pressure with the Q missile and its recast-pull from a range her Q-dash can't punish for free — but the cardinal rule is never lead with a damage cast into her, because Riposte will parry your E or Q, stun you, and delete you while your W escape is on cooldown. At 6, Between Worlds is your equalizer: the rift slow plus going untargetable to her lets you zone her off your vitals, and if her Flash is down you can W-reset off a takedown. Bait the Riposte first, then commit.","late":"You lose the long game outright. Once Fiora has two items she side-lanes and 1v1s you, and her sustained vital DPS shreds you faster than your cooldown-gated Q burst and spirit-heal can answer — a single parried E or Q in the duel is a death sentence. Your job is to have already snowballed off your mid-game R windows; if the game goes even into the split, do not take the 1v1 — group and make her parry into multiple targets, where Riposte only catches one cast and her vitals only stick to one body.","whys":["You are a one-spell mage with no W leap yet while she Q-dashes onto a vital and procs true damage — you cannot trade.","She gets Q-dash spacing and vital pressure online before your E, so any spell you throw to farm invites a free vital proc.","With Q, E, and passive sustain you can finally poke at max range, but lead with a damage cast and Riposte stuns you — a coin-flip you keep even at best.","Her Eclipse/early-item vital DPS plus Q mobility out-trades your pre-6 poke; without R you have no safe all-in answer.","The Between Worlds rift slow and its cross-zone teleport are your one equalizer — you break her vital chain and commit while her 24s Riposte is down.","Her first-item spike plus a Riposte on your E or Q lets her all-in through your poke faster than your burst can kill her.","Two-item Fiora side-lanes and out-duels you — her sustained vital true damage beats your cooldown-gated burst and one parried cast ends you."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"galio","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-out, Q-recast back through Galio plus an E blast chips him while your passive heals the return — his Winds of War tornados are slow to converge, so you can stand outside the overlap and still poke."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your poke peak: passive spirit-healing and W's short cooldown let you win the river trade war before his Shield of Durand damage reduction and MR items come online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Both spike — the Between Worlds rift zones and Across the Veil turns you invisible, but Hero's Entrance is a 180s global knock-up and Justice Punch (11s) pins you for the taunt, so commit on cooldown, not blindly."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Abyssal Mask and Force of Nature stack his MR while Shield of Durand cuts magic damage further — your Q burst stops killing and the lane tilts to the unkillable tank."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level 2-5 poke war with Q-recast and E while your passive heals you — punish Galio before he buys MR or Shield of Durand softens your burst","Use W to leap clear of his Justice Punch dash and the Shield of Durand taunt radius so his engage whiffs and you free-poke the channel","Snowball a roam or kill lead before stacked MR turns your AP burst into chip damage"],"foe":["Stack magic resist (Abyssal Mask, Force of Nature) and channel Shield of Durand so Aurora's AP poke and Q burst stop hurting","Land Winds of War zones and follow Justice Punch into the Shield of Durand taunt to lock her for a full combo","Soak the lane even, then use Hero's Entrance to knock up and take over other lanes, scaling into a frontline teamfight tank"]},"early":"Galio is squishiest before he stacks MR, so the first three levels are your window to open the poke war. Lead with Q, recast Twofold Hex to drag the curse back through him for the second hit, and weave E for the slow-and-hop — your passive exorcises spirits off him and heals you through any return damage. Respect his Winds of War (the two tornados deal damage and slow where they converge) and his Colossal Smash empowered auto, but both are slow and telegraphed, so stand outside the tornado overlap and you out-poke him cleanly.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your real peak — your Q cooldown, passive healing, and W reset line up so you out-trade him before his MR and Shield of Durand matter. Keep chipping with Q-recast and E, and stay mobile: his only hard engage is Justice Punch into the Shield of Durand taunt, so hold W to leap out of the dash or the taunt radius and then free-poke his channel. At 6 it stays even — your Between Worlds rift and untargetable W zone hard, but his Hero's Entrance global and his taunt punish a blind commit, so all-in on cooldown windows, not coinflips.","late":"This is where Galio reclaims it. Every MR item he buys — Abyssal Mask, Force of Nature — directly blunts your AP, and Shield of Durand's magic damage reduction makes him near-unkillable in a straight fight, so the burst that one-shot him at level 5 just chips him by 2+ items. Your job is to have already converted the early-mid lead: roam with your W speed, snowball a side lane, and end before his MR stacking and Hero's Entrance global turn him into an unkillable teamfight anchor.","whys":["Both are low-threat at level 1 — neither his single Winds of War nor your lone Q decides a trade, so it's a clean farm stage decided by who hits skillshots.","Your Q-recast plus E poke comes online and his pre-MR HP can't sustain it while your passive heals you back — you start owning the trade.","With Q, E and passive sustain stacked you win the poke war outright; his slow-converging Winds of War tornados are easy to side-step.","Your power peak: poke, passive healing and W's reset align so you control every river trade before his Shield of Durand reduction or MR items exist.","Both spike hard — the Across the Veil invisibility and the Between Worlds rift zone, but Hero's Entrance and an 11s Justice Punch into the taunt answer your all-in, so 6 is a skill-matched commit.","His first MR item plus Shield of Durand's magic reduction already start blunting your burst, tipping the trade war his way as he buys defense.","Stacked MR (Abyssal, Force of Nature) plus the Shield of Durand taunt shrug off your AP — he out-scales you into a frontline teamfight tank."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"gangplank","win":["Skill","Gangplank","Gangplank","Skill","Skill","Gangplank","Gangplank"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Pure poke war and genuinely even: your Q out-and-recast double-hit and Spirit Abjuration heal trade against his Parrrley harass and barrel chip. Shoot or step on his barrels before they detonate so a chain never out-damages your two-hit Q."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"You edge ahead pre-ult: E's slow-then-backhop lets you land Q poke and disengage while your spirit-heal stacks sustain you. Punish him every time he walks up to arm or detonate a barrel."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your clearest window. The rift slow plus its cross-zone teleport lets you all-in through his barrel burst — do it while Remove Scurvy (22s at rank 1) is down, or he cleanses the slow and heals."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Gangplank's window. Crit-empowered barrel chains and global Cannon Barrage out-DPS your poke, and Remove Scurvy cleanses your E-slow so you can't kite him. Close the lane before he gets here."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade evenly levels 1-3 by landing the Q recast double-hit while Spirit Abjuration heals you through his Parrrley and barrel chip","Hit 6 and convert the rift slow plus the cross-zone teleport into an all-in while his 22s Remove Scurvy is still down","End the lane on your first-item Luden's/Malignance spike before crit barrels and global R take over"],"foe":["Detonate barrel chains and Parrrley harass faster than your spirit-heal restores it","Hold Remove Scurvy to cleanse your E-slow so he can't be kited or chunked on the all-in","Stall to 2+ items where crit barrels and global Cannon Barrage reclaim the lane and pressure the whole map"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are a straight poke war and it is genuinely even. Fire Q and recast it to drag the curse back for the double-hit, and let Spirit Abjuration's drifting spirits heal you through his Parrrley harass and barrel chip. The whole lane hinges on barrels: shoot or step on the ones he plants before they detonate, because a full armed chain out-damages your poke if you let it cook. Don't burn W to chase a single barrel detonation — Across the Veil is your only escape once it's down.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your window to take over. E's slow-then-backhop sets up Q poke while your spirit-heal stacks keep you topped off, and this all lands before either of you has an ult — so punish him every time he steps up to arm or detonate a barrel. At 6, Between Worlds is your real spike: drop the rift to slow him, go untargetable in spirit mode to dodge his barrel burst, and all-in — the W reset on the takedown is your snowball. Just respect that Remove Scurvy can cleanse your E-slow, so commit when it's on cooldown.","late":"This is where Gangplank reclaims it and you have to be honest about it. Once he hits 2+ items his crit-empowered barrel chains and global Cannon Barrage out-DPS your poke, and Remove Scurvy cleanses your E-slow so you simply can't kite him anymore. Your first-item Luden's/Malignance spike is your last clean window to convert a lead — take it. If the game goes long he out-scales you and starts pressing the map with his global ult, so close before two items or accept a coinflip teamfight lane.","whys":["Both are low-threat single-spell pokers at level 1 — your Q missile and his Parrrley trade evenly, neither commits.","Q recast double-hit plus Spirit Abjuration's heal answers his early barrel chip and Parrrley harass exactly — it stays a wash.","Your E slow-and-backhop comes online and your spirit-heal stacks let you out-sustain his chip — you edge the pre-ult trades.","Your poke, E disengage, and stacked healing all land before ultimates — punish him every time he steps to arm a barrel.","Between Worlds slows him and rifts you through his barrels, and a 22s Remove Scurvy left down is what makes the all-in stick.","Once his first item lands, armed barrels and crit start out-trading your poke and Remove Scurvy cleanses your slow — the lane tilts to him.","He out-scales hard — crit barrel chains and global Cannon Barrage out-DPS you and his W cleanse stops you kiting, so close early."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"gnar","win":["Skill","Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Skill","Gnar","Gnar"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-curse then E-blast-and-hop wins the poke race once mini-Gnar has thrown his boomerang and has to walk up to retrieve it for the empowered second hit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds slows Gnar in the rift and teleports you across it, and GNAR! only stuns if it throws you into a wall — hold open ground and it is just a slow."},{"when":"Mega rage","text":"Full bar means his next form is mega-Gnar: a Wallop bonk plus a GNAR! throw can chain-CC and burst you while your W leap is down — back off until the rage bar drains."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Liandry's sharpens the Q-recast burst so you one-combo a low-armor mini-Gnar before his rage fills and he transforms."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade only in his mini-Gnar form: land Q-curse, recast it back through him for the second hit, then E-hop out before his thrown boomerang returns to his hand","Watch his rage bar and commit your all-in only while it is low, so no mega Wallop or GNAR! answers the moment you step up","Use W's brief invisibility and the R rift to dodge the mega GNAR! wall-stun, then punish the long mega-form ability cooldowns"],"foe":["Kite your poke with mini-Gnar boomerang and hops, walking up to retrieve the boomerang so the return throw double-hits","Build rage to mega off cooldown, then chain Wallop into a GNAR! wall-stun while your W leap is unavailable","Stack rage next to his tower or a wall so GNAR! pins you into terrain and his team collapses on the stun"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are a boomerang-versus-curse poke race, and it is close — mini-Gnar's Q out-ranges my Q and the returning boomerang double-dips if he stands in its path, so I last-hit at max range and never walk up into a free hop+boomerang catch. Once I hit 3 I have Q-curse plus E, and my passive starts pulling spirits off him to heal the chip, so exchanges tip my way: land Q, recast it back through him for the second hit, then E-blast-and-hop before his boomerang comes back to his hand. The one hard rule early is his rage bar — if it is filling toward gold, do not step up, because transforming into mega-Gnar erases the trade I'm trying to win.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are yours if you respect the rage bar. Pre-6 run the poke pattern around his transform timer: trade hard while he's mini and his rage is low, then disengage with E the instant the bar goes gold. At 6, Between Worlds is the trump card — the rift slows him and teleports you across it, and GNAR! only stuns enemies it throws into a wall, so holding open ground turns his commit into a knock-back. The real kill window is a low-rage mini-Gnar at 6: Q-recast burst while his 22s Hop is down lets you snowball before he ever reaches mega form.","late":"Late game flattens back to even, which is why this is a coinflip lane and not a free one. Once he has a few items, mega-Gnar in a teamfight brings Wallop plus a GNAR! knockback-stun that can land while my W leap is on cooldown, and a single stun is enough to delete a squishy mage — so my job is to stay on the edge, throw Q pokes from max range, and only commit my leap when his rage is empty. I don't out-scale him; I out-tempo him. If I banked a level-6 lead I press it around mid-game objectives, and in fights I save W and R purely to dodge the mega stun rather than to chase a kill.","whys":["Mini-Gnar's boomerang out-ranges my Q and double-dips on the return, and I have no escape online yet — last-hit at range, don't trade into a free hop+boomerang catch.","Still a wash: his hop kites my poke and I lack burst pre-3, so I bank CS and watch the rage bar rather than force anything.","Q-curse plus E-hop comes online and my passive heals the chip, so I win the mini-Gnar poke war once his boomerang is mid-flight and out of his hand.","I control trades while he's mini and low-rage, but the moment the bar fills, a mega Wallop-into-GNAR! flips the exchange — so it swings entirely on his rage timer.","Between Worlds slows Gnar in the rift and GNAR! only stuns into terrain, so open ground turns his ultimate into a slow — your cleanest all-in on a low-rage Gnar.","Luden's/Liandry's sharpens the Q-recast burst so I one-combo a low-armor mini-Gnar before his rage fills and he transforms to answer.","Even again — itemized mega-Gnar's GNAR! stun lands while my W is down and bursts a squishy mage, so I poke and dodge from the edge instead of dueling."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"gragas","win":["Aurora","Skill","Gragas","Gragas","Aurora","Gragas","Gragas"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"His E Body Slam comes online and closes the gap your poke depends on — the dash collides and STUNS, so he can lock you down before your Q-recast curse-pull lands, then his W-empowered attack and Happy Hour healing win the trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Explosive Cask (100s) ends your all-in: the knockback interrupts your W-leap commit and displaces you clean out of your own rift, so the zone converts nothing and he can even cask you into his tower."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance is your one real window — burst him with Q-recast + E before his W damage-reduction is sampled, and use your E backward-hop plus R rift to zone the wave and disengage."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"He out-brawls you: his W damage-reduction blunts your Q-recast burst and his Happy Hour passive heals through the chip your spirit passive needs, so the AP duel goes to the tankier body with the stun."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q on his approach and recast to curse-pull him before his E Body Slam dash can reach and stun you","Hold your W-leap to dodge his E dash, not to engage — once he stuns you with no W up, you eat his full W-empowered follow-up","Stall to your first item and force the poke war before his W damage-reduction and Happy Hour sustain fully outscale your spirit healing"],"foe":["Body Slam E onto you the instant your W-leap is on cooldown, landing the collision stun while you have no escape","Sample W for damage-reduction, eat your Q poke, then trade back with the W-empowered attack while Happy Hour heals the chip","Land R Explosive Cask to interrupt your W commit or knock you clean out of your own R rift"]},"early":"Gragas owns the early lane because his E Body Slam closes the exact gap your poke needs — the dash collides and stuns, so he can lock you down faster than you can curse-pull with Q-recast, and his Happy Hour passive heals the chip your spirit passive was supposed to win you. Don't throw a Q he can just dash through; last-hit at max range and keep your W-leap in reserve as a dodge for his E, never as an engage. If he lands the Body Slam stun and you've already burned W, you're a squishy mage eating his W-empowered attack and full follow-up with no exit.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your one even patch — your Q cooldown drops and your spirit-passive sustain stacks, so you can win short poke trades if you respect his 14s Body Slam. But at 6 his R flips it back: the Explosive Cask knockback interrupts your W commit and can punt you clean out of your own rift, so the zone converts nothing while his ult plus a Drunken Rage auto out-trades you. Only commit when Body Slam and his 100s cask are both down.","late":"Your first-item spike (Luden's/Malignance) is the one window you genuinely own — burst him with Q-recast and E before his W damage-reduction is sampled, and use your E backward-hop and R rift to zone the wave and stay safe. But it doesn't last: at two items his W blunts your combo and his Happy Hour passive heals through your spirit poke, so the AP brawl goes to the tankier body with a stun. Convert that single item window into a lead and roam, or this lane just out-sustains you all game.","whys":["He's a strong level-1 brawler and you're a single-combo mage with no hard escape — concede it and deny his last-hits at max Q range.","His E Body Slam comes online and the dash STUNS on collision, locking you before your Q-pull lands — don't step into dash range.","His Happy Hour passive out-sustains the chip your spirit passive needs, and his E stun punishes any commit — keep farming at max Q range.","Your Q cooldown and spirit healing line up, so short trades go even if you bait his E first — this is your only level patch.","His R Explosive Cask knockback interrupts your W-leap and punts you out of your own R rift, so his ult all-in beats yours.","Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst — kill him before his W damage-reduction is sampled, then E-hop and zone with R.","At two items his W blunts your combo and his Happy Hour passive heals through your poke — the tankier AP body with a stun reclaims the brawl."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"garen","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Garen's Decisive Strike (Q) is a move-speed burst plus a silence — if you're silenced you can't fire your Q missile or W out, so he closes the gap and lands the empowered, slowing strike on you. This is his cleanest walk-up window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Demacian Justice (R) is a flat missing-HP true-damage execute. Once your Spirit Abjuration heal can't keep you topped, a Q-E shove into R deletes you — and your W blink only saves you if you take it BEFORE you dip into execute range, not after."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-recast double-hit and E poke so your stacked Spirit Abjuration sustain finally out-trades his Perseverance regen and Courage (W) damage-reduction — the lane flattens into a coinflip here."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With two AP items your Q-out, Q-recast-pull-into-E burst out-chunks anything Perseverance can regen between trades — and chip alone stops it ticking. Between Worlds slows him and teleports you across the rift, so his 8s Decisive Strike silence never catches you standing still."}],"wants":{"you":["Last-hit at max Q-missile range and never sit inside Decisive Strike (Q) range while your W is down — being silenced there means no Q, no W out, and a free empowered strike on you","Bait his Q-walkup-then-disengage with a single Q poke, then catch the recovery with E (slow + backward hop) and a Q-recast pull as he peels off, chipping him without standing in silence range","Stack Spirit Abjuration heals off safe poke and survive to your 1st-2nd item spike, where your burst finally beats his Courage (W) reduction and Perseverance regen"],"foe":["Land Decisive Strike (Q) to silence you out of casting Q or W, then ride the move-speed buff in for the empowered strike","Pop Courage (W) before you commit your combo, soaking your Q-recast burst with the damage reduction and shrugging your E-slow with the tenacity","Push your HP to a missing-HP threshold so Demacian Justice (R) executes through your remaining health, then break vision to reset Perseverance regen and reload"]},"early":"Garen owns these levels and you have to respect it. Decisive Strike (Q) is the problem: the silence means that if he catches you in range you simply can't fire your Q missile or W out — so he eats your spell, rides the move-speed buff into your face, and lands the empowered, slowing strike. Do not step inside Q range to throw poke. Last-hit at the very tip of your Q missile, take a little chip, and let Spirit Abjuration heal you back to even. You can't out-trade him standing still at level 1 as a single-spell mage, so the whole early game is spacing and farm — keep W held as your escape, not your engage.","mid":"Still his window. At 6 Demacian Justice (R) is a flat missing-HP true execute, so the instant your Spirit Abjuration heal stops keeping you full, a Q-E shove into R can delete you — and W only saves you if you blink out BEFORE you drop into execute range, never reactively once he's already pressing R. The way to survive is the bait: throw one Q poke to draw his Q-walkup, then catch the disengage frames with your E (slow plus backward hop) and a Q-recast pull as he spins off, chipping him without ever eating the silence. Trade in single touches, not commitments, and treat W purely as the panic button for his all-in.","late":"This is where you take it back. With two AP items your Q-out, Q-recast-pull-into-E burst chunks harder than his Perseverance passive can regen between trades, and Courage (W) only blunts one combo, not a sustained poke war. Between Worlds (R) lets you zone the lane or walk a wall onto him untargetable, and his short Q-E-then-disengage pattern has no answer to a poke fight he's now losing. Keep your distance, never get silenced onto, and farm to the spike: a fed Garen can still flash-R execute you out of nowhere, but an even-or-ahead Aurora out-pokes and out-positions him for the rest of the game.","whys":["Decisive Strike (Q) silences and move-speed-buffs Garen into you, and at level 1 you're a single-spell mage with no W escape unlocked yet — concede the trade and last-hit safe.","With Q-E online he can silence you out of casting, then walk you down with the speed buff; you don't have your full combo or W-reset yet to punish him, so just farm at range.","His Q move-speed closes the gap and Courage (W) damage-reduction soaks your poke — without your stacked Spirit Abjuration sustain and item spike you lose every committed trade here.","His Courage (W) reduction plus Perseverance regen out-sustains your pre-item Q-E chip, and the Q silence shuts off your W the instant you'd want to disengage.","Demacian Justice (R) is a missing-HP true execute — once you dip into threshold range a Q-E-R kills you outright, and your W only escapes it if taken before the execute window, so this is his peak.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike lets the Q-recast double-hit and stacked Spirit Abjuration finally out-trade his W reduction and Perseverance regen — neither of you cleanly owns the lane now.","With two AP items your Q-pull-into-E burst out-chunks his Perseverance regen between trades and Between Worlds (R) zones his short disengage — you reclaim the duel and out-poke him for good."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"graves","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Graves"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q-missile-into-E poke war comes online and your passive spirits heal the chip right back — Graves has no lane lifesteal to answer the bleed."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds zones his footing and turns you untargetable to his shotgun burst from outside the rift, while W resets on the takedown — your cleanest all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Ludens/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-curse recast so one pull-back combo deletes a tank-ADC Graves before his armor stacking matters."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Graves' window: tank-ADC items and stacked True Grit out-DPS your poke point-blank, and Quickdraw closes the instant W is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the Q-missile and E poke war at max range so his shotgun pellets never land full and your passive spirits heal every trade","Hit Level 6 and drop the R rift to zone his footing, walk it untargetable through his burst, then W-reset on the kill","Force the kill on your item spike before his tank-ADC build comes online and the point-blank duel flips at 2+ items"],"foe":["E-dash in and unload both point-blank shotgun autos for full pellets before your passive spirits heal the trade back","Land Smoke Screen (W, 26s) on you to nearsight your spacing and break line of sight when you try to curse-recast","Stack True Grit armor off his E and scale to 2+ items where his shotgun burst out-DPSes your poke"]},"early":"Graves only hurts at point-blank — both shotgun autos need to be near-touching to land all their pellets, so the whole early game is keeping your Q missile and E poke at max range where he can't close. Level 1 respect his two-auto burst and don't walk up to trade autos; once you have Q plus E at 2-3 you open the poke war his kit can't sustain, since he has no lifesteal in lane and your passive spirits heal the chip right back. Don't waste W chasing — save the leap, because if he E-dashes onto you and stacks his True Grit armor, that blink is your only out.","mid":"This is your window. Curse him with the Q missile, recast it to pull the curse back through him for the second hit, and E-poke to slow-and-hop backward before his shotgun range matters — your passive spirit sustain wins every extended trade. At 6, drop the R rift to zone his footing and walk through it untargetable when he tries to burst you from outside, then commit the W leap; the takedown resets W and you snowball. Watch his W smoke — it nearsights you and breaks vision, so don't blindly chase your curse-recast into it; trade through it or wait it out.","late":"Hold your lead, because 2+ items is where Graves reclaims this. He builds tanky for an ADC and his point-blank shotgun burst out-DPSes your poke once his items and True Grit armor scale — if he E-dashes in and lands both autos full while your W is on cooldown, you are a squishy mage with no second escape. Close the game on your mid-phase spike: end before his items come online, save W for his all-in, and never get caught facechecking when your blink is down.","whys":["New Destiny fires 4 bullets that cannot pass through units, so last-hit from behind your own minions — step into the open and his two-auto point-blank burst chunks you at Level 1.","Q plus E lets you open the poke war from range, and Graves has no lane lifesteal to heal the chip while your passive spirits heal yours for free.","Your Q-curse recast double-hit out-trades him while your passive heals it back — he has to dash in to answer, and you keep W to punish that commit.","Your poke, spirit sustain and the 15s Weirding control spacing, and your minions swallow the bullets he needs.","Between Worlds zones his footing and turns you untargetable to his burst from outside the rift, and the takedown resets W so you snowball.","Your Ludens/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-curse pull burst so one combo deletes a tank-ADC Graves before his armor stacking matters — force the all-in here.","He out-scales: tank-ADC items, stacked True Grit and point-blank shotgun DPS burst you the moment W is down, so play safe once his items land."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"gwen","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Gwen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q missile + E slow are both online while Gwen has barely ranked Hallowed Mist (W) — open the poke war now, before she has a full cloud to vanish into."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds (R) slows and zones her off the wave while Across the Veil turns you invisible — your cleanest all-in, before her Riftmaker/Nashor's spike arrives."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst; force kills now while Gwen's Snip Snip! (Q) true damage and Riftmaker healing are still missing."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Gwen's window flips it: with Riftmaker + Nashor's her Q true-damage snips and refreshing E dash out-DPS your squishy mage body — stop dueling and play for picks."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with the Q missile then recast-pull for the second hit while Spirit Abjuration spirits drift back and heal you to full","Catch Gwen the instant she steps outside Hallowed Mist (W) and burst her with Q-pull + E before she re-clouds","Cash in your Level 6 R zone and first-item burst for a kill before her Q true-damage scaling arrives"],"foe":["Drop Hallowed Mist (W) and sit inside it, going untargetable to your Q/E pokes thrown from outside the cloud","Farm safely under Mist and refuse trades, stalling until Riftmaker/Nashor's come online","Reach 2+ items where her Snip Snip! (Q) true damage and self-refunding E dash shred your low mage HP"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you have one spell ranked and no escape yet, and Gwen is a melee with barely any Hallowed Mist, so just last-hit. From level 2-3 you take over: fire Q to curse her, recast it to pull the curse back for the second hit, and weave E to slow and disengage, all while Spirit Abjuration spirits drift back to heal you through the trade. The key read is her W, Hallowed Mist — the moment she drops it she's untargetable to anything outside the cloud, so land your Q/E BEFORE she casts it, or step inside the cloud with her so your spells can still hit.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your peak. Your Q-pull burst plus E slow and your passive sustain out-trade her, and she can't all-in you without abandoning Mist's safety. At 6, Between Worlds slows and zones her off the wave while Across the Veil turns you invisible on landing — commit your hardest all-in here, and remember Skip 'n Slash refunds part of its 13s cooldown every time she hits something, so it is rarely truly down. Bait her E dash, land your E slow as she commits, then Q-missile and pull her down before she can reach a fresh Mist.","late":"This is hers. Once Gwen has Riftmaker and Nashor's Tooth, her Snip Snip! (Q) centre snips deal true damage that ignores your low mage HP, and her E dash refunds itself to stick to you — she shrugs off your poke and out-duels you. Across the Veil and the Between Worlds teleport are your only outs once she commits. You MUST close the game on your mid-game lead; do not scale a poke war against a true-damage hyperscaler who sits untargetable in Mist.","whys":["Level 1 you have one spell ranked and no escape, and Gwen has barely any Mist to hide in — neither can commit, so just trade last-hits.","Your Q curse plus its recast-pull lands two hits and E slows her, and her Hallowed Mist isn't a full cloud yet to vanish into.","Your poke-and-heal pattern from Spirit Abjuration out-trades her, and you punish every time she steps outside Mist range.","A Thousand Cuts heals her off every auto, so buy Oblivion Orb early — her 450 cone still cannot reach your 900-range Q.","Between Worlds slows and zones her off the wave and Across the Veil turns you invisible mid-fight — your cleanest all-in window.","Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst and her Q true damage and Riftmaker healing aren't online yet — force the kill now.","Gwen out-scales hard: her Q true-damage snips and refreshing E dash shred your squishy body once Riftmaker/Nashor's land — play for picks, not a duel."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Skill","Heimerdinger"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Heimer drops a turret on the wave and chips you with W rockets while it beams you — you can't last-hit at melee range, so you concede the opener and farm at max Q range."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your Q poke plus Spirit Abjuration heal let you trade back: leap in with W, land Q, recast it through him for the second hit, then E-hop out before his stun grenade tracks you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your clean swing — the rift damages and slows him, and Across the Veil carries you past the turret line invisible, so you ignore the beam and burst him on his grenade cooldown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's or Malignance sharpens your combo, but a Liandry's plus turret upgrade lets Heimer re-zone the wave and his E grenade still answers your W-leap all-in."}],"wants":{"you":["W (Across the Veil) past the turret line so you land Q from invisibility, not into the beam where the turret free-hits you","Reach Level 6 healthy so the Between Worlds rift gives you the one all-in his turrets can't zone","Bait his E stun grenade with a feint, then commit your Q recast-pull burst while the grenade is on cooldown"],"foe":["Plant a turret on the wave so you eat beam damage every time you step up to last-hit","Land his E stun grenade to freeze your W leap mid-trade, then chunk you with turret beam plus W rockets","Stack and upgrade turrets on the choke so your Q poke never out-trades his zone control"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to him and it stings. His turret beam plus W rocket poke wall you off the minions before your one-spell Level 1 can answer, and your W leap is too short a window to dive a fresh turret yet. Don't walk into the turret to throw a Q he just out-zones — last-hit at max Q range, soak the chip, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the poke off the spirits you draw. You do have E to disengage if he grenade-stuns you, but never burn your W approaching him; a spent W is exactly when his stun grenade lands and the turret deletes you.","mid":"Levels 4-5 even out as your Q recast-pull and passive sustain come online — bait the turret beam, leap in with W to land Q, recast it back through him for the second hit, then E-hop out before the next grenade lands. Remember the grenade is placed, not tracked: only a direct hit stuns and the splash merely slows, and it is a flat 11s at every rank. Level 6 is your real window: Between Worlds drops a rift that damages and slows him while Across the Veil carries you past the turret wall invisible, so you burst him on that grenade cooldown and crack the lane open.","late":"Late game he reclaims it. A Liandry's-plus-Rylai's Heimer re-zones every wave with an upgraded turret farm, kites your W-leap with the slow, and his E stun still freezes your only escape the moment your leap is on cooldown — then turret beam plus rocket DPS shreds a squishy mage. Your favor windows are 6 and your first item; if you haven't snowballed a W-reset kill lead by then, your Q poke can't out-trade a fortified turret line. Close it before two items or accept the splitpush stalemate.","whys":["His turret on the wave plus W rocket poke wall you off CS, and your one-spell Level 1 can't contest the zone.","He out-ranges your single Q with the turret beam and rockets — eat the poke and heal it with Spirit Abjuration rather than trade into the turret.","With Q recast-pull and spirit sustain online you trade back, but the turret beam still free-hits you mid-combo — it's a wash.","Only a direct grenade hit stuns — the splash just slows, so sidestep the centre; the turret zone still holds the lane.","Between Worlds slows him off the wave and Across the Veil walks you past the turret line invisible — burst him on his grenade cooldown.","Luden's sharpens your combo, but a Liandry's Heimer re-zones the wave and his E still answers your W all-in — call it even.","Hextech Affinity speeds him up beside his own turrets, so an upgraded nest plus the grenade out-zones your poke once your hop is down."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"illaoi","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Skill","Illaoi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q out-ranges her tentacle slams: curse her with Twofold Hex, recast to pull it back for the second hit, and let your Spirit Abjuration passive heal you up while she can only poke with a single tentacle and her auto."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your answer to her ult: when she casts Leap of Faith, drop the rift to slow and zone her and use Across the Veil to leave the spawned tentacle wall invisible, so her 450-range R deals almost nothing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q burst combo — this is your last clean trading window before her tentacle count and passive-driven sustain start matching your poke on extended fights."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Her power spike: a full tentacle field plus repeated Test of Spirit slams out-sustain and out-DPS you, so any extended stand-and-fight in her field is death — only commit when her R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Twofold Hex from max range and let Spirit Abjuration heal you, winning the attrition before her tentacle count climbs","Fight on open ground using Across the Veil's invisibility to reposition and the Between Worlds teleport to disengage — never inside her tentacle field","Respect Test of Spirit: if she rips your spirit, stay close to it and step out of tentacle reach — running away is what makes you a Vessel"],"foe":["Land Test of Spirit (E) so you either let the spirit die or run too far from it and become a Vessel","Pull you into a stacked tentacle field where her passive and tentacle slams out-sustain your poke","Hit Leap of Faith (R) to spawn a tentacle wall and snowball her 2-item field-control lead"]},"early":"Level 1 she'll slap down a tentacle and try to zone you, but she has no way to answer your Q range — fire Twofold Hex to curse her, recast to pull it back for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the spirits back to you. The cardinal rule is her E, Test of Spirit: you become a Vessel if the ripped spirit dies OR if you get too far from it, so do NOT leap away — step sideways out of tentacle reach while staying close to the spirit. Last-hit from Q range; never step into her auto-plus-tentacle range.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you control spacing with Q pokes and your E slow-and-hop disengage, but she's stacking tentacles and her passive heals off every tentacle hit, so this is genuinely even — buy Grievous Wounds and neither of you snowballs unless someone mispositions. At 6 you tilt it your way: when she commits Leap of Faith, drop Between Worlds to slow and zone her and use Across the Veil's invisibility to leave the tentacle field, and her ult value evaporates — it only reaches 450. Stand and fight only on open ground away from her tentacles.","late":"This is her lane to reclaim. Once she has 2+ items and a full tentacle field, standing to fight is suicide — her tentacle slams and Test of Spirit out-sustain and out-DPS your poke, and your W/R only buy escape, not a kill. Use Across the Veil's invisibility to break her all-in and the Between Worlds teleport to splitpush or roam, but never duel her on her own field. Bank the leads from your early-mid windows and let your team collapse on her away from her tentacles.","whys":["Tentacles swing only at spirits, Vessels and her Harsh Lesson target, so your Twofold Hex curse plus Spirit Abjuration heal out-trade her at near-zero risk.","Your Q-recast double-hit and W reposition let you win the poke war before her tentacles stack — bait the E and leap clear.","Even window: you poke and heal off your passive, but her passive sustain and stacking tentacles match you the moment a trade drags into her field.","Skill matchup — you control spacing with Q and the E-hop, she heals through it; whoever mispositions into the tentacle field loses the trade.","Between Worlds slows and zones her while Across the Veil turns you invisible — you leave the tentacle field and blank her 450-range R.","Your Luden's burst sharpens the poke, but her tentacle count is climbing — it stays even, so only force the all-in when her R is down.","Her stacked field and Test of Spirit out-sustain and out-DPS you at 2 items; play off vision, splitpush, and never duel her on her own field."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"irelia","win":["Skill","Irelia","Irelia","Skill","Aurora","Irelia","Irelia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Irelia's sharpest early swing: she Q-dashes off the wave straight onto you and chains it with E to stun, opening a full reset combo before your Twofold Hex can stack the heal off her."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your poke window: land Q and recast it to drag the curse back through her for the second hit while her Q dashes are spent on minions, healing off the spirits on your passive, then E backward to break the trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one clean swing — drop the rift to slow her dashes, use Across the Veil's invisibility to break her Mark chase, and a takedown lets you leap out and snowball the kill."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Trinity online, Irelia reclaims it: Sheen procs turn every Marked Bladesurge into burst and she heals off each strike, so a straight poke war stops paying once she has resets off the wave."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q and recast to pull the curse back through Irelia for the second hit while her Q dashes are committed to minions, healing off your passive spirits","Save Across the Veil to leap out of her Q-dash E-stun engage so the reset all-in whiffs, rather than burning it as a poke tool","Hit 6 and use Between Worlds to slow her dashes and Across the Veil to vanish out of her Mark chase, then snowball the takedown"],"foe":["Q-dash through the wave to gap-close, then E to stun you into the full Sheen-reset combo","Keep a slow, stacked wave so she always has minion targets to chain Q resets off and all-in you","Charge Defiant Dance to shrug off physical damage, then snowball resets into her Trinity spike"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — Irelia has no E stun yet and you only have Q, so just last-hit and don't get clipped wandering into her Q-dash range. From level 2 she's the bully: she Q-dashes through the minions onto you and lands E to stun you into her combo before your poke matters, so respect that engage and save Across the Veil to leap out of it rather than burning it for repositioning. Throw Q and recast it to clip her only when her dashes are spent on the wave; the spirits you exorcise heal you on your passive and keep the trade even even if you don't eat the stun.","mid":"Levels 4-5 even out as your Q-recast poke and passive sustain come fully online — drag the curse back through her whenever her dashes are committed to CS, then E backward to break contact. Do not wait out her Defiant Dance: it only reduces physical damage, so your magic burst goes through it in full. Level 6 is your window: Between Worlds slows her dashes and Across the Veil turns you invisible mid-fight, and if you secure the takedown you leap out and snowball. Buy Grievous Wounds early, because Bladesurge heals her on every strike.","late":"This is where Irelia reclaims the lane. With Sheen and then Trinity Force she chains Bladesurge off Marked targets and minions, healing herself on every strike, so a straight poke war stops working once her items come online. Your only outs are her cooldowns — leap her Flawless Duet with Across the Veil, kite with the Weirding slow and your rift, and never get caught in a big stacked wave where every minion is another reset back onto you. If she snowballed off the early levels, give up the sidelane duel and group with your team.","whys":["Neither of you has a real all-in yet — she lacks E for the stun-combo and you only have Q, so it's just last-hitting and spacing around her Q-dash range.","She gets her Q-dash going off the wave and lands E to stun you into a full reset all-in before your single-spell poke can punish her.","Flawless Duet Marks you and the Mark refreshes Bladesurge, so her stun chains into a reset all-in — Across the Veil is your only escape.","Your Q-recast poke and passive spirit healing finally come online — pull the curse back through her when her dashes are on minions, then E back.","Between Worlds slows her dashes and Across the Veil turns you invisible, so you break the Mark chase and snowball your one clean window.","Her Sheen/Trinity spike turns every Marked Bladesurge into burst, and each strike heals her back through your poke.","A fed Irelia chains Marked resets and heals off every Bladesurge — kite her cooldowns and play with your team rather than duelling."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"jax","win":["Jax","Aurora","Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Jax","Jax"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q-out, Q-recast poke window: fire Twofold Hex, then recast to drag the curse back through him for the second hit while your passive heals the trade. He has only Leap Strike (Q) range, so chip him before he can stick."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds slows and zones his all-in while Across the Veil turns you invisible to break his stick — and Counter Strike never stopped your spells anyway, only your autos. Your cleanest commit window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance sharpens Q burst, but Jax's Blade of the Ruined King power spike lets him chase through your slow and stick — the lane tips back toward him here unless you already have a lead."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Grandmaster-at-Arms (his R) plus Counter Strike take over any extended duel — his sustained DPS beats your cooldown-gated poke, so refuse the fight and disengage with E."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q, then recast it to pull the curse back through Jax for the second hit while your passive exorcises spirits to heal the trade","Hold W (Across the Veil) for when he Leap Strikes onto you — leap away to break his stick, then re-poke from range","Pop R at 6 to slow and zone him, use Across the Veil to break his stick, and burst him while Counter Strike is spent"],"foe":["Bait out your W, then Leap Strike (Q) onto you and Counter Strike (E) for the dodge-and-stun burst","Hold Counter Strike to dodge your autos — it never stops your spells — then stun you when you step up","Drag the duel past 2 items so Grandmaster's Might and Blade of the Ruined King out-sustain your poke"]},"early":"\"Level 1 is even-leaning-Jax — you're a one-spell mage with no escape up and he's a melee whose only stick is Leap Strike, so last-hit safely and respect his all-in if he gets a leash. From level 2-3 you get your poke window: throw Q and recast it to drag the curse back through him for the second hit, then E to slow-and-hop backward while your passive heals you off the exorcised spirits. The whole lane hinges on W discipline — keep Across the Veil up so that when he Leap Strikes onto you, you can leap away and re-space, because the moment you waste W on a bad trade he Counter Strikes the stun and chunks you for free.\"","mid":"\"Levels 4-5 are yours if you space right — Counter Strike dodges attacks, not abilities, so Twofold Hex, its recast pull and the Weirding all land on a Jax sitting inside it; only your autos whiff, and the counterattack still stuns. Level 6 is your spike: Between Worlds slows him inside the zone while Across the Veil turns you invisible to break his stick, and you burst with Q recasts. Bait Leap Strike first — it is 8s at 700 range — and never open into an active Grandmaster-at-Arms, which hands him Armor and MR.\"","late":"\"This is where the lane slips away from you, and the 46% win rate lives here — plan around it. Once Grandmaster-at-Arms (his R) and Blade of the Ruined King come online, his sustained DPS out-trades your cooldown-gated poke and Counter Strike is down to 9s, so any extended fight ends in a stun. Don't 1v1 a 2-item Jax — use E and W to disengage, R to escape ganks or split, and shove-and-roam instead. You needed the 2-6 window to bank a lead; if you got one, group and end before his scaling takes the game.\"","whys":["At level 1 you're a single-spell mage with no W up and he has only Leap Strike to stick — neither side can punish hard, but his all-in threat off a leash means you play respectful, so the edge is faintly his.","With Q-recast and E online you out-poke him from range and slow-hop away while your passive heals — he can only walk up into chip damage with no answer yet.","Level 3 is a pure skill check: your poke is real but the Counter Strike counterattack still stuns, so it comes down to whether you step in while his E is down.","Counter Strike dodges attacks, not spells, so your Q-recast burst lands through it — just hold the hop to leap away from his Leap Strike commit.","Between Worlds slows and zones his all-in and Across the Veil turns you invisible to break his stick, and Counter Strike never stopped your spells — this is your one clear spike.","Jax's Blade of the Ruined King spike lets him chase through your slow and stick to you, answering your Luden's/Malignance poke — the lane tips back to him unless you already snowballed.","Grandmaster-at-Arms and a 9-second Counter Strike give him sustained DPS and a stun that win any extended duel — your poke cannot burst a 2-item Jax, so the late game is his."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Skill","Aurora","Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Jayce"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Jayce's cannon-stance Shock Blast fired through his Acceleration Gate out-ranges your Twofold Hex and chips you every time you step up to last-hit. Body-block it on the minion wave, then let Spirit Abjuration heal the chip back."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Q and E online you can finally trade: fire Twofold Hex through him, recast it to drag the curse back for the second hit, layer The Weirding's slow, and let E's backward hop carry you out before he swaps to hammer stance."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds drops a rift Jayce can't safely poke into and makes you untargetable to him from outside it. Bait him in, land the Q-pull burst, and Across the Veil resets on the takedown for a free reposition."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Two-item Jayce out-ranges and out-DPSes you, and his hammer-stance E knockback cancels your Across the Veil mid-leap. This is his peak, so cash your level 6 and first-item windows before his poke build comes online."}],"wants":{"you":["Body-block Shock Blast on the minion wave and let Spirit Abjuration stacks heal the poke so his cannon Q never out-paces your sustain","Trade only when his Acceleration Gate Shock Blast is down: Q through him, recast for the double-hit, then E-slow and hop to safety","Use Between Worlds at 6 to fight in the rift untargetable from outside, land the Q-pull, and snowball the Across the Veil reset on the kill"],"foe":["Fire Shock Blast through the Acceleration Gate to poke you off the wave before you ever reach Twofold Hex range","Save hammer-stance E to knock you out of your Across the Veil leap mid-air, then burst with the stance-swap combo while your escape is gone","Hold the wave at range and out-poke you into his AD item spike, where he chips you down from a screen away"]},"early":"Jayce owns the opening levels because his Shock Blast — the cannon-stance Q fired through his Acceleration Gate — out-ranges your Twofold Hex and chips you every time you step up to last-hit, and at level 1 you only have a single missile to answer with. Don't throw Q into his poke war you can't win; body-block the Shock Blast on the minion wave and let Spirit Abjuration's spirit-heals claw the chip back. Once you hit 3 with Q and E online you start to even it out: fire Twofold Hex through him, recast to drag the curse back for the second hit, layer The Weirding's slow, and let E's backward hop pull you out before he can swap to hammer stance and all-in.","mid":"This is where you claw the lane back. Levels 4-5 stay a poke war and it is genuinely close — trade only when his Shock Blast is on cooldown, because that gate-empowered shot is the one thing that out-damages your sustain. At 6 you take over: Between Worlds drops a rift he can't safely poke into and makes you untargetable to him from outside it, and Across the Veil's cooldown resets on a takedown — so bait him into the rift, land the Q-pull burst, and the W reset finishes anyone you catch low. Respect his hammer-stance E during your leap; if he knocks you out of Across the Veil mid-air you lose your only escape.","late":"Late is Jayce's window, not yours. Once he has two items his AD poke build chips you from a full screen away before you ever reach Twofold Hex range, and his hammer-stance E knockback into the stance-swap burst deletes you the instant Across the Veil is down. You don't out-scale a fed ranged poke carry — your edge was the level 6 and first-item rift windows, so cash those into a lead and a closed-out game. If it runs long, never facecheck into his Shock Blast, save Between Worlds to walk through walls and disengage rather than to dive, and let your frontline soak his poke.","whys":["His gate-empowered Shock Blast out-ranges your single level-1 missile and pokes you off every last-hit before you can answer.","Even at 3, Spirit Abjuration lets you heal his chip but his cannon Q still wins the raw range war — the trade math is a wash.","Q through him, recast for the double-hit, then E-slow and hop out — you trade back the moment his Shock Blast is on cooldown.","The 4-5 poke war is a coin-flip: you control trades when his gate shot is down, he controls them when it's up.","Between Worlds zones a rift he can't poke into and makes you untargetable from outside — your cleanest all-in, and Across the Veil resets on the kill.","Your first-item Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-pull burst — force the all-in on his Shock Blast cooldown before his items land.","Two-item Jayce out-ranges and out-DPSes you, and his hammer E cancels your Across the Veil leap — play safe and close the game before this."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Skill","Skill","Karma","Aurora","Karma","Karma"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Karma opens the poke war: her Q (Inner Flame) lands its delayed bonus damage and slow from outside your reach, and she just walks out of your single Twofold Hex missile before you can recast the pull-back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your one clean window. Between Worlds drops you into spirit mode, so you tank the rift on her and W in before she can RW-tether you — burst her down while her Mantra is the only peel she has."},{"when":"Mantra up","text":"Her biggest threat: Mantra-W (Renewal) tethers and roots you, or Mantra-Q (Soulflare) detonates an AoE root if you stand in it. Either one eaten while your W leap is down lets her free-poke you and sets up the jungle gank."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Liandry's online (plus her mana from Lost Chapter) lets Karma perma-poke and E-shield through your Spirit Abjuration heals — the chip you can't out-sustain is when the lane tips fully to her."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her base E shield onto a throwaway Q, then commit the real Twofold Hex curse-and-pull while she has no shield to eat the burst","Hold W (Across the Veil) to dodge her Mantra-W tether or sidestep the Soulflare detonation, then punish the long Mantra cooldown","Force the level 6 all-in: drop Between Worlds for spirit mode, W in, and Q-burst her before her Mantra peel resets"],"foe":["Land Mantra-W (Renewal) tether or a Soulflare (Mantra-Q) detonation to root you for free poke and jungler follow-up","Poke with raw Q (Inner Flame) range and the slow while staying outside your Twofold Hex pull range","Pre-shield with E (Inspire) and ride its move speed to kite your W all-in, then out-sustain the trade with shields"]},"early":"Karma out-ranges you from the first wave — her Q (Inner Flame) detonates its bonus damage and slow before your single Twofold Hex missile even arrives, and she strolls out of your recast pull-back. Don't try to win the raw poke war; your passive, Spirit Abjuration, heals the chip back as spirits drift home, so just farm and stack. The one thing that flips a trade is baiting her early E shield onto a throwaway Q, then committing your real Q-into-pull combo while she has nothing left to absorb it.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay hers — her Q poke plus E shield out-trades your pre-6 kit, and she just shields off most of what you land. Everything hinges on level 6. Between Worlds is your window: it drops you into spirit mode, so you can eat the rift damage on her, W in on top, and burst her with Q before her shield resets. If you don't kill in that window, she peels out and the lane snaps back to her. Respect her Mantra above all — a Mantra-W (Renewal) tether or a Soulflare detonation eaten while your W is down pins you for her jungler with no second escape.","late":"This is where she fully pulls ahead. Once Karma finishes Liandry's (the Lost Chapter mana lets her cast freely), she perma-pokes and shields through your Spirit Abjuration sustain, and your poke-and-blink pattern stops paying — she out-ranges and out-sustains you outright. Her Mantra-W tether and Soulflare also become fight-defining peel and engage tools. Your only real path is converting a lead off the level 6 spike before her items come online; if the game goes long and even, she controls the lane and the sidewaves with range you simply can't close.","whys":["Karma's Q (Inner Flame) detonation out-ranges your single Twofold Hex missile at level 1 — she pokes for free and walks out of your recast pull.","Your Q plus E come online and Spirit Abjuration heals the chip she lands, so the poke war evens out even though she keeps the range edge.","With your full poke-and-W-dodge kit you can trade back, but her E shield blanks enough of your burst that it stays a coin-flip rather than your favor.","Her Q poke plus pre-emptive E shield out-trades your pre-ult kit, and she kites your engage on the shield's move speed.","Between Worlds drops you into spirit mode at 6 — you tank the rift on her, W in, and Q-burst her before her Mantra peel comes back.","Liandry's plus her Lost Chapter mana let Karma perma-poke and shield through your passive sustain, so your poke trades stop paying off.","At 2+ items she out-ranges and out-sustains you while her Mantra-W tether and Soulflare define fights — you can't close the gap once her poke scales."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"kassadin","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Fire Q across Kassadin, then recast to drag the curse back through him for the double-hit while spirits drift back to heal the trade. He has no Riftwalk yet, so he can only eat it walking up to last-hit — his Q silence blanks one of your casts, not the whole poke war."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Drop Between Worlds across his Riftwalk escape lane to zone the blink, go untargetable through the rift, and chase with W (resets on takedown). This is his clearest pre-item window to die before his passive and blink make him unpinnable."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance online sharpens the Q-recast burst — every time his Riftwalk is down, collapse and convert it into a kill so he never hits his item timings on schedule."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Kassadin lands Rod of Ages plus Tear/Seraph's, his anti-magic passive eats your all-AP poke and Riftwalk's cooldown drops low enough to dodge your Q on reaction — the duel flips and his Q-silence-into-burst deletes you when W is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack spirit healing with Q-recast double-hits so his early melee farm costs him health he cannot trade back as a no-escape melee","Bait his Q silence and small shield with a throwaway cast, then commit the real Q burst plus W-leap while both are on cooldown","Close the game before his 2+ item Riftwalk-spam spike — snowball off Level 6 rift all-ins and W-reset takedowns while he is still pinnable"],"foe":["Survive lane and farm safely under tower, leaning on his anti-magic passive to soak your full-AP poke until items come online","Reach 2+ items so Riftwalk's low cooldown lets him dodge your Q and reposition out of every E-and-hop","Hit the Rod-into-Seraph's window where his Q silence-into-burst one-shots you the instant your W-leap is down"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are yours to bully. Kassadin is a melee with no Riftwalk yet, so every time he steps up to last-hit you fire Q across him and recast it to pull the curse back through for the double-hit, and your spirits drift back to heal whatever chip he lands. His Q silence and small magic shield blunt one cast, not a full poke war — bait the shield with a throwaway Q, then land the real combo. Keep the wave nearer your side so he has to walk into your range to farm, and respect that his anti-magic passive means your all-AP poke does a touch less than the numbers suggest — so hit him often, not just hard.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your takeover. Your poke, spirit healing, and W cooldown line up, so you control every trade — E in to blast-and-slow, hop back to safety, then Q-recast through him. At 6 his only real escape is Riftwalk, so drop Between Worlds across his blink lane to zone the path, become untargetable through the rift, and chase with W (its cooldown resets on the takedown). This is the window you must cash in: a dead or item-starved Kassadin is the entire game plan, because he only gets harder to catch from here.","late":"Be honest — once Kassadin has two items (Rod of Ages into Seraph's) the lane inverts hard. His Riftwalk cooldown drops so low he dodges your Q on reaction and repositions out of every E-and-hop, his anti-magic passive shrugs off your all-AP poke, and his Q silence into magic burst deletes you the moment your W-leap is down. You have to have a lead banked from lane and end the game — group, take towers, and close before the 2+ item mark, because in a straight late duel he kites you with blinks and one-shots you through your sustain.","whys":["Kassadin is a no-escape melee pre-6 — your Q-recast double-hit chips him while spirits heal you, and his small shield only blanks one cast.","Your W-leap makes the poke untouchable; he cannot punish your spacing without Riftwalk, so fire Q-recast every time he steps to farm.","Full kit online — E to blast-and-hop, Q-recast through him; bait his Q silence and shield first, then land the real burst.","Your poke, spirit sustain, and W cooldown all line up while he is still a melee with no escape — you own these trades outright.","Between Worlds zones his Riftwalk lane and turns you untargetable; W-reset-on-takedown lets you chase the blink and kill him before he scales.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q burst — convert every Riftwalk-down window into a kill and starve his item timings.","Kassadin out-scales: at Rod/Seraph's his anti-magic passive eats your AP poke, his low-cooldown Riftwalk dodges your Q, and his Q-silence-burst kills you when W is down — end the game before this."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"kayle","win":["Skill","Kayle","Kayle","Skill","Skill","Kayle","Kayle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q's curse plus E's slow you start a poke war melee-form Kayle cannot answer — chip her every time she walks up to last-hit, and Spirit Abjuration heals the trade back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds drops a rift that zones Kayle off the wave and lets you cross it at will, while Across the Veil hides you and resets on takedown to chain the all-in — your hardest kill window before her ranged form exists."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst — force every all-in now while she's still meleed and item-starved, because this edge expires fast."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kayle hits ranged form plus her item spike: her R invuln blanks your commit and her auto-DPS out-trades your poke. The lane is hers now — stop dueling and group."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Q curse-and-recast and E's slow every time Kayle steps up to CS, healing the chip back with three Spirit Abjuration stacks","Hit level 6 and use Between Worlds plus the W-reset to all-in her before her ranged form comes online","Snowball your early-mid lead and close the game before her 2-item ranged DPS spike reclaims the lane"],"foe":["Farm safely under tower and soak XP through your poke without feeding a kill before her item timings","Reach ranged form and her 2-item spike so her autos and R invuln out-DPS your poke","Survive your level-6 all-in, then take over the map with waveclear and uncatchable splitpush scaling"]},"early":"Kayle is a meleed last-hitter levels 1-3 and you punish that hard. Lead with Q to curse her, recast to pull the curse back for the second hit, and weave E to slow and chip her every time she walks up for a CS — Spirit Abjuration heals the poke right back, so the trade war is one-sided. Level 1 is roughly even because you're a single-spell mage with no leap up yet, so don't over-extend, but from 2 onward you own the lane. Hold W; save the leap for a kill commit, not a chase.","mid":"This is your takeover and your only real kill window. At 6 your R drops a rift that zones Kayle off the wave and turns you untargetable to her from outside it, while W resetting on takedown means one pickup chains into the next — all-in her hard before ranged form matters. With your first item (Luden's/Malignance) your Q-recast burst spikes and she's still a defenseless melee scaler. Bait her E waveclear, then Q-curse, recast for the second hit, and commit with W and R. Every minute you don't close is a minute closer to her reclaiming the lane.","late":"This is where it flips and you have to respect it. Once Kayle hits her 2-item ranged spike her autos and waveclear out-DPS your poke, and her R invulnerability blanks your all-in burst the instant you commit — even your W reposition and R untargetability can't out-trade a fed Kayle. Stop trying to solo her; the poke war is over. Win the game off the early-mid lead you built, group with your team, and never hand her the free farm and 1v1 splitpush she scales into.","whys":["Level 1 you're a one-spell mage with no leap up yet — but melee-form Kayle is just as harmless, so neither commits; just deny her last-hits.","Q curse-and-recast plus E's slow start the poke war, and melee Kayle has no way to trade back through your Spirit Abjuration healing.","With Q and E both online you out-poke a meleed Kayle every time she steps to CS, and she has no dash to close on you.","At 6 your rift zones her off XP and you can cross it at will, while the W-reset-on-takedown lets you chain the all-in before her 160s ult matters.","Kayle's R invulnerability blanks your level-6 burst the moment she hits ranged form — once she can pop it, your commit windows start closing.","At one item you're still ahead, but she's nearing her 2-item ranged spike — the lane is already tilting toward her DPS scaling.","Kayle's 2-item ranged form out-DPSes your poke and her R invuln eats your burst — she owns the duel now and you must group instead."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"kennen","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Skill","Kennen","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Kennen owns it — his Thundering Shuriken (Q) out-ranges your single Q missile and his energy never runs dry, while you have one spell, no W, and no way to close."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your poke-and-blink peaks: Q-curse then recast pull for the double-hit, E to slow-and-hop out, and your Spirit Abjuration spirits heal you through his shuriken chip before either ult is up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Skill window — your W-leap into the R rift can dodge his shuriken and hide you, but if he lands 3 marks his Slicing Maelstrom (R) stun chains into Q-W burst when you misjudge the realm timing."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kennen reclaims it: Zhonya's stalls your all-in until his marks proc the stun, and full-AP energy-free shuriken poke out-DPSes your spirit healing."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q's missile then recast the pull back through him for the double-hit, so your Spirit Abjuration spirits out-heal his shuriken chip","Hold W until his Slicing Maelstrom is on cooldown, then leap in and burst before he can stack 3 marks for the stun","Use R's rift to cross onto him and W to vanish out of his ranged poke mid-trade, before three marks land"],"foe":["Kite back with his Lightning Rush (E) move speed and chip you with Q shuriken before you ever reach W range","Bait or wait out your W, then land E-Q to stack marks and proc the Slicing Maelstrom stun into a Q-W-auto burst","Zone you off CS with energy-free poke and scale to a full-AP teamfight ult"]},"early":"Level 1 belongs to Kennen — his Thundering Shuriken (Q) out-ranges your single Q missile, his energy never empties, and with no W yet you can't punish him, so just last-hit and eat minimal chip. From level 2-3 you stabilize: get Q plus E online and the lane evens because your passive, Spirit Abjuration, heals you back through his shuriken poke every time your Q-curse and E-blast exorcise spirits off him. Don't recast Q's pull into nothing — line it so the return hit catches him for the double-tap, and keep E's backward hop ready so you can poke and slide out of his auto range before he stacks Mark of the Storm on you.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your window — your Q cooldown drops, your spirit sustain is fully online, and W is up often enough that you control the trade: Q-curse, recast pull for the second hit, E to slow and disengage, and your spirits out-heal his shuriken war before either ult matters. At 6 it gets skill-intensive: your W-leap into R rift lets you dodge his shuriken and go untargetable, but if you blow W early he lands E-Q autos to stack 3 marks and his Slicing Maelstrom stun chains into a Q-W burst that deletes you. Bait his engage or wait the stun window out, then commit — never all-in while your leap is on cooldown.","late":"This is where Kennen takes it back. A full-AP Kennen with Zhonya's stalls in stasis through your all-in until his marks proc the Slicing Maelstrom stun, and his energy-free shuriken poke out-DPSes your spirit healing once his items come online. Your R untargetability and W invisibility keep you alive in skirmishes, but you can't win the straight 2+ item poke duel anymore, and his AOE teamfight ult outclasses your single-target rift. Convert your level 4-6 and first-item leads into a closed game — if it goes long and full-build, you're the one playing safe.","whys":["Kennen owns level 1 — his Thundering Shuriken (Q) out-ranges your lone Q missile and his energy pool never runs out while you have one spell and no W to close.","It evens out as you get Q plus E and your Spirit Abjuration spirits start healing the shuriken chip back — neither of you can win the trade outright yet.","With Q-curse, the recast pull double-hit, and E's slow-and-hop online, your spirit sustain out-trades his poke and you start owning the spacing.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all line up here — you control the trade and zoning before his Slicing Maelstrom is even relevant.","Skill window at 6: your W-into-R dodges his shuriken and hides you, but if he stacks 3 marks his R stun chains into burst, so the better player wins.","Your Luden's-class first item sharpens the Q burst and your spirit healing still beats his shuriken poke — force the all-in while his R is on cooldown now.","Full-AP Kennen reclaims it — Zhonya's stalls your all-in until his marks proc the stun, and his energy-free shuriken DPS out-paces your spirit heals."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"kled","win":["Aurora","Skill","Kled","Kled","Aurora","Kled","Kled"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Kled's Bear Trap on a Rope hooks you and yanks him onto you, and Skaarl's frenzied mounted autos shred your squishy frame faster than your Spirit Abjuration heals — with only Q up, you have no Across the Veil leap to escape, so give him the trade entirely."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one clean window: the rift slows him inside it and you teleport from one side to the other as he commits, so his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! engage and remount attempt whiff and his all-in is wasted."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance spike lets you Q-curse and burst a dismounted, Courage-empty Kled from max range before he can build Courage to remount — punish the window where Skaarl has run off."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kled reclaims the duel: his sustained mounted DPS plus a Bear Trap re-engage out-trade your poke once Across the Veil is on cooldown and you have no second escape."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge Bear Trap on a Rope — if it hooks, save Across the Veil to leap out the instant he yanks himself onto you, before Skaarl's bonus autos stack","Reach 6 and fight on the rift — it slows him inside and you cross it on command, so his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! and remount whiff","Abuse his dismount: Q-curse and E-poke a Courage-empty Kled from range so he can never safely rebuild Courage to remount"],"foe":["Land Bear Trap on a Rope to pull himself onto you and chunk you with Skaarl's frenzied autos before your spirits heal the trade","Force early all-ins while your Across the Veil is down and you are a squishy mage with no escape","Hit Chaaaaaaaarge!! to engage or chase your leap, build Courage off the trade to remount, and snowball the lane"]},"early":"Kled owns these levels and you cannot fight him straight. His Bear Trap on a Rope hooks you and reels him in, then Skaarl's frenzied mounted autos shred you faster than your Spirit Abjuration spirits can heal the trade — and at level 1 you are a single-spell mage with no Across the Veil to leap away. Hug the wave, last-hit at max Q range, and do NOT step up to throw a curse he can answer with a grab. If the trap lands, your only out is leaping with W the instant he yanks himself onto you — burn it to escape, not to trade.","mid":"Level 6 is your one breath of air. Standing inside Between Worlds makes you untargetable to enemies outside the rift, so if Kled commits Chaaaaaaaarge!! or tries to remount on top of you, walk the rift and his whole all-in whiffs. Outside that window you're still behind — at 4-5 his mounted DPS plus a Bear Trap re-engage beats your trade math. Your real edge is his dismount: when Skaarl runs off, Kled is a short-range melee who has to rebuild Courage to remount, so chunk him with Q-curse and E from range and deny him the damage he needs to get Skaarl back.","late":"This stays hard — Kled is a scaler and reclaims the duel at 2+ items. His sustained mounted damage and Bear Trap re-engage out-DPS your poke once Across the Veil is on cooldown, and a single grab pulls him onto you and out of your safe spacing into his team. Don't try to 1v1 him in a side lane; use Between Worlds' untargetability and your W leap to disengage, take the poke-and-zone role in teamfights, and let your team body him. If you got an early lead off his dismount windows, end before his items come fully online.","whys":["Kled's Bear Trap on a Rope plus Skaarl's mounted auto-aggression bursts you and you have no Across the Veil to escape at level 1 — concede it.","He out-trades you with mounted autos while you only have Q and your Spirit Abjuration heal can't keep pace — don't step up.","Even with your full kit, one Bear Trap grab undoes any poke you land and reels him onto you — he owns the all-in at level 3.","His mounted DPS and trap re-engage beat your trade pattern through these levels — give ground and farm safely.","Between Worlds slows him inside the rift and you teleport across it as he commits, so his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! engage and remount whiff — your one clean window.","Your Luden's/Malignance poke can chunk a dismounted, Courage-empty Kled, but he can rebuild Courage and remount — genuinely a coin-flip skill window.","Kled out-scales hard: sustained mounted damage plus a Bear Trap re-engage out-duel you once Across the Veil is down."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"ksante","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-curse then recast the pull-back chunks him twice for free; his only answer is charging W, which cuts his damage taken but pins him — he cannot hold it and last-hit at once."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds slows him inside the rift and lets you teleport across it, so his All Out knockback loses the isolation it needs — pop it as he charges, cross the zone, and his one kill button finds nothing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance spike: your Q-recast double-hit plus passive spirit heal out-trades a K'Sante who's still spending gold on armor and HP, not damage — convert the lead before he scales."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His window — All Out converts his own resists into raw AD and empowers his W-dash + Q knockup, so he out-dives your W cooldown and your poke no longer brings him low enough to kill."}],"wants":{"you":["Fire Q to curse him, then recast to drag the curse back through him for a free second hit while his W charge is down","Hold Across the Veil for his W-dash + empowered Q knockup all-in — leap out the moment he commits and keep the poke going","At 6, use Between Worlds untargetability so his All Out can't isolate-and-execute you, then burst him before he reaches 2 items"],"foe":["Pre-charge W to block your Q missile and eat the poke, then release the dash to close on you","Land the empowered Q knockup off a W-dash to pin you for an all-in before your leap is back up","Stall to 2+ items so All Out fighter-form lets him dive through your poke and percent-HP you down"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you're a single-target mage with one poke spell and no early escape, and his W charge can block your Q missile outright, so just farm and don't throw a naked Q into a held W. From level 2-3 you take over: fire Q to curse him, then recast to drag the curse back through him for a second hit, and his only counter is pre-charging W to block the missile — which he can't do while last-hitting. Respect his one all-in: W-dash into the empowered Q knockup. If he steps up to charge W, leap away with Across the Veil and keep poking. Your passive pulls the exorcised spirits back to heal you through every trade, so the poke war is yours.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your peak. Your Q cooldown drops, the passive spirit-sustain is rolling, and you out-trade him cleanly because he's buying armor and HP while your poke compounds. At 6, Between Worlds is the key: his whole kill pattern is All Out to knock you off and isolate you for the dive, but you pop your rift to become untargetable to him from outside, walk through the wall, and his ult finds nothing to follow. Bait the W charge out or trade when it's down, Q-curse-recast for the double hit, then leap in for the kill and reset Across the Veil on the takedown. Force every all-in here, before his items come online.","late":"This is where it flips. Once K'Sante hits 2+ items and pops All Out — converting his own armor and MR into raw attack damage and empowering his W-dash and Q knockup — he out-dives your W cooldown and your poke stops bringing him low enough to kill. You're a squishy mage, and his percent-HP damage plus the isolation knock will delete you the moment your leap is down. Don't try to 1v1 a scaled K'Sante into the late game; you needed your lead from lanes 2 through 6. Play for picks with R untargetability, group with your team, and let your poke and rift zone teamfights instead of dueling him.","whys":["You're an escape-less single-target mage at level 1 and his W charge can block your only poke missile — neither of you threatens a kill, so just farm.","Q-curse plus the recast pull-back nets a free double-hit, and his W block can't be charged while he's last-hitting — you start winning the poke war.","With Q on a low cooldown and your passive healing the exorcised spirits back onto you, every trade nets you HP while he only buys tank stats.","Your poke, passive sustain, and the Across the Veil cooldown all line up — you control spacing and he can't punish you before ultimates land.","Between Worlds slows him inside the rift and you cross it on command, so his All Out cannot hold the isolation — he burns his only kill button and you walk free.","Your Luden's/Malignance burst plus the Q-recast out-trades a K'Sante still buying armor and HP, not damage — convert your lead now.","Once All Out turns his resists into raw AD at 2+ items, his empowered W-dash and Q knockup out-dive your W cooldown and percent-HP you down — the duel is his."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"lillia","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q plus E online your curse-pull poke out-trades her — she chips you with Blooming Blows and passive burn but has no point-click answer to the Q recast, and your passive heals back the Dream Dust she stacks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds zones her off the wave and your W leap is your saver against her R sleep cast — your cleanest all-in window before she has items."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens the Q-recast burst; her squishy frame folds to one curse-pull combo here before her kite scaling comes fully online."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Her threat window — a fed Lillia kites you forever on Blooming Blows' stacking move speed, then lands R sleep into a burn-stacked detonation once your W is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q on her then recast to pull the curse back for the second hit before she peels away with her E dash","Hold your W leap to dodge or interrupt her R sleep cast, then all-in while it is down","Burst her with the first-item Q-recast combo before her kite-and-burn scaling comes online"],"foe":["Stack her passive burn with Q spins and E pokes, then dash out with E before your curse-pull lands","Catch you with R sleep while your W is on cooldown, then burn-stack the detonation","Drag the game past two items where her kite and DOT out-sustain your poke war"]},"early":"Lillia wants to chip you with her Q spin (Blooming Blow) and E seed-bounce while her passive burn ticks, dancing at range — but her only real mobility is the E dash, so your Q is a poke she struggles to answer. Fire Q to curse her, then recast to pull it back through her for the second hit; her escape is the E hop, and your Spirit Abjuration passive heals back the burn she stacks on you. Don't chase her into her own minions where the E gets value, and respect that level 1, before your Q recast is meaningful, she can out-spin a single cast.","mid":"This is your window. Your Q-recast poke and E slow-and-disengage out-trade her kite because she can't burst you back — she just stacks a burn you sustain through. At 6 your R rift zones her off the wave and lets you walk through walls to cut her off, and the real key is your W: bait or dodge her R sleep cast with the leap, because a slept-then-detonated burst is the main way she kills you. Land Q, pull it, E to slow her, then W in for the takedown and the cooldown reset.","late":"She flips the matchup once items come online. A fed Lillia kites you indefinitely with her E move speed and Q spins, out-sustains your poke with her passive burn, and only needs one R sleep landed while your W is down to detonate you. Your favor windows are all early-mid — close the game before she hits two items. Late, never throw your W aggressively or facecheck for her; if your leap is on cooldown you are a squishy mage with no escape from her sleep.","whys":["She pokes with her Q spin and her burn ticks, and at level 1 your Q recast isn't online yet — this stage is a genuine wash before your kit comes together.","With Q plus E your curse-pull out-trades her Q-spin poke and your passive heals her burn chip — she has no point-click reply to the recast.","Your full poke combo punishes Lillia's short E dash every time she steps up to spin, and she can only kite from the Q-pull.","Your poke, passive healing, and W reset line up to control trades she can only kite, not contest.","Between Worlds zones her off CS and your W is your answer to her R sleep cast — your cleanest all-in before her items.","Luden's/Malignance sharpens the Q-recast burst and her squishy frame folds to one combo on this spike.","A fed Lillia kites you forever and one landed R sleep into a burn detonation kills you while W is down — close before two items."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"lucian","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Lucian wins level 1 — he Lightslinger double-shots off a single Q-W and Aurora has only one Q and no W escape yet, so concede CS at max range and eat minor poke."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once Aurora has Q-curse plus E's slow, her passive heals her spirit stacks through his autos and Lucian has zero sustain to answer it — the poke war flips her way."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is Aurora's cleanest all-in: the rift slows Lucian inside it and she crosses the zone mid-channel to break The Culling's line — W-reset on the kill snowballs the lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Lucian's real spike: a completed lethality/crit item plus a Relentless Pursuit dash lets him close, Lightslinger-burst, and re-dash out the instant Aurora's W leap is on cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Curse Lucian with Q, then recast it so the return hit catches him while he's mid-dash on Relentless Pursuit and can't sidestep it","Only commit a trade when your W leap is up — it's your only out once he dashes in and Lightslinger procs","Drop your R rift across his Relentless Pursuit escape lane so the slow traps him and untargetability eats his Culling"],"foe":["Use Relentless Pursuit to dodge your Q return or close the gap for a Lightslinger burst","Weave Lightslinger double-shots out of each ability cast to out-DPS your passive sustain","Hold E and The Culling to all-in the moment your W leap is on cooldown"]},"early":"Level 1 is genuinely Lucian's — one Q or W procs Lightslinger, so his next two shots out-poke Aurora's single Q while she has no W to escape, so just last-hit at max range and eat a little chip. It flips at 2-3: once Aurora has Q-curse and the slow on E, her Spirit Abjuration passive exorcises spirits off Lucian to heal her through his autos, and he has no sustain to trade back. Curse him with Q, then recast it so the pull-back hit lands while he's committed to a Relentless Pursuit dash — that double-tap is what makes him respect her range.","mid":"This is Aurora's window. Her Q poke, passive healing, and the W leap line up so she controls the spacing Lucian needs to step up and Lightslinger — every time he dashes in, leap away with W, land the Q curse-and-return, and drain him while his Relentless Pursuit is on cooldown. The rule: only commit when W is up, because once your leap is down a Relentless Pursuit dash plus Lightslinger can burst you. At 6, Between Worlds answers his whole kite — drop the rift on his escape lane to slow him, walk through the wall untargetable so The Culling whiffs, and the W-reset on the takedown snowballs.","late":"The lane is Aurora's through mid, but once Lucian completes his first lethality or crit item the duel swings back — a fed Lucian uses Relentless Pursuit to close, Lightslinger-bursts Aurora down, and dashes back out before her W comes up, and The Culling out-ranges her poke. She's the mid-game-tilted skirmish mage and he's the item-reliant carry, so this stays a coinflip into teamfights. Close it on the 4-6 spike: get a W-reset kill, take plates, and force the game before his first item comes online and the duel slips out of her favor.","whys":["Lucian procs Lightslinger off one ability and double-shots Aurora at level 1, while she has only a single Q and no W escape — concede it and farm safe.","With Aurora's Q and E online it evens out — she can start the poke war, but a Relentless Pursuit dash plus Lightslinger still wins an all-in if her W is down.","Q-curse, E slow, and passive spirit-healing let Aurora out-trade his autos — recast Q while he's dashing on Relentless Pursuit to punish the commit.","Aurora's poke, healing, and W cooldown line up to control the spacing Lucian needs to step up — she trades freely as long as her leap is available.","Between Worlds slows Lucian inside the rift and lets Aurora cross the zone to break The Culling's line — her hardest all-in lands at 6.","Lucian's first lethality/crit item plus a Relentless Pursuit dash lets him close, burst, and re-dash out — the duel swings back to him.","A 2-item Lucian out-DPSes Aurora's poke and deletes her the moment her W is on cooldown — she must close the game on her mid-game lead before his item comes online."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"malphite","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Aurora","Skill","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Malphite owns it: his Q (Seismic Shard) slows you and his Granite Shield passive eats your first auto, so he pokes and walks while you are a single-spell mage with no W yet."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once your W, E and a Spirit Abjuration stack are online you flip it — Q-curse, recast the pull for the second hit, then E-slow and hop back faster than his Q poke chips you, and every spell heals you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-pull burst, but his armour is never wasted on you — Ground Slam scales straight off it — so take your poke-and-zone window now, before he has R cover."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"Respect his R (Unstoppable Force): it is an unmissable point-and-click-ish charge from fog that knocks you up — bank your W leap or R rift to dodge the engage, never burn either on poke."}],"wants":{"you":["Keep three Spirit Abjuration stacks rolling off Q and E pokes so his Granite Shield and armor stacking never let him out-sustain your magic chip","Run the Q-curse, recast-pull, E-slow-and-hop combo to chunk him, then disengage before he can land a Seismic Shard slow to stick you","Save your W leap for his R charge, and use the rift slow and cross to leave the landing spot — your only counter to Unstoppable Force"],"foe":["Land Seismic Shard slows to stick on you and trade while your W dash is down","Wait out the lane and hit a fog or flank R (Unstoppable Force) to knock you up and all-in past your spacing","Stack armor and farm safely behind Granite Shield, conceding the poke since he is built to win the level-6+ teamfight, not the 1v1"]},"early":"Level 1 is Malphite's — his Seismic Shard slow plus his Granite Shield passive absorbing your first hit let him poke and walk away while you are still a single-spell mage with no W leap to answer, so just farm and bank a Spirit Abjuration stack off anything you land. From level 3 the lane tilts to you: your Q curse, the recast pull for a second hit, and your E slow chip him faster than his Q poke can answer, and because every spell you land heals you off your passive while his only durability is armor (dead weight against your AP), he gains nothing from his tank stats. Heal through trades and never step into a fresh Seismic Shard slow.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your sweet spot — your Q cooldown drops, your passive heals are flowing, and you can run a clean Q-curse, recast-pull, E-slow-and-hop pattern that he can only answer with a Seismic Shard he has to land on a moving target. At 6 it becomes a coin flip you respect: his R, Unstoppable Force, is an unmissable charge that knocks you up and cannot be cancelled, so the mid-game is pure W discipline — hold your leap for his engage, not for poke. If he R's and your W is up, leap out of the path; if your W is down, drop your R rift to walk through the wall untargetable, or you eat the full all-in.","late":"Your first item (Luden's/Malignance) is a real spike because his only answer to you is armor, which does nothing against your full-AP burst — keep poking and zoning him off objectives. But at 2+ items the matchup swings back to him: Malphite stops being a laner and becomes a teamfight R that one-shots your positioning, and your squishy poke-mage frame folds to a single Unstoppable Force from fog. So push your lead in the mid-game window and group to force picks before his R gets to decide a fight from the side.","whys":["Level 1 he out-pokes you: Seismic Shard slows and his Granite Shield passive eats your first auto while you have no W yet — concede it and farm a passive stack.","Levels 2-3 even out as your W, E and passive sustain come online — you can start trading, but his Q slow still answers your step-ups, so it is a skill window.","From level 3 your Q-curse-and-pull plus E slow out-chip his Q, and his armor stacking is worthless against your AP — you own the trade and heal through it.","At 4-5 your poke, passive healing, and shorter Q cooldown all line up while his only tool is a Seismic Shard he must land on a moving target — you control the zone.","At 6 it is a coin flip on his R: Unstoppable Force is an unmissable knock-up, so if your W or R rift is up you dodge it, and if both are down he all-ins — pure skill check.","Your first item sharpens your Q-pull burst and his stacked armor does nothing to magic — this is your cleanest poke-and-zone window before his R cover.","At 2+ items he becomes a teamfight engage whose fog R catches your squishy frame past your spacing — he reclaims the matchup off one knock-up."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"maokai","win":["Skill","Maokai","Maokai","Skill","Skill","Maokai","Maokai"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus the recast online — start the poke war chucking Twofold Hex through his saplings, but remember every hit shortens his Sap Magic heal, so poke to set up kills, not to grind."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds slows him inside the rift and lets you cross it as he commits, so his Twisted Advance dash-root arrives out of position — but hold damage until he lands, because the dash itself is untargetable."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Liandry's sharpens the Q-curse-recast burst — one full combo plus E chunks a pre-tank Maokai who can't gap-close to punish you back."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Maokai's real window: if your W is down and he lands Twisted Advance to root, his E saplings plus Q knockback-slam can chain you long enough for a jungle gank — hold W for his root, don't burn it to poke."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Twofold Hex through his saplings and recast it to pull the curse back for the second hit while your passive heals the return chip","Hold Across the Veil until his Twisted Advance commits, then leap the root and Q-burst the whiff","Stack passive spirits in the poke war so you win the HP race outright and zone him off CS at Q range"],"foe":["Land Twisted Advance to root you in place, then chain E saplings and the Q knockback-slam to set up a jungle gank","Soak your poke with Sap Magic sustain and his sapling shields, out-lasting your mana in a long lane","Survive to teamfights where his AoE root, sapling zone and tank frontline matter far more than the 1v1"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you're a one-spell mage with just Q, and he drops an E sapling to push and farm safely, so concede the wave and last-hit at max Twofold Hex range. Once you hit 2-3 you take over: throw Q to curse him through his saplings, recast it to drag the curse back for the second hit, and let your passive spirits heal the chip his saplings deal. His only real kill button is W, Twisted Advance — a short dash that roots — so never sit at melee range with your W down; bait his root, leap it with Across the Veil, and punish the whiff with a Q-recast. Watch your mana, because Sap Magic gives him near-infinite sustain and he wants the poke war to grind long.","mid":"This is your window. Your Q cooldown drops and your passive out-heals his sapling poke, so you own the HP race and zone him off the wave with E slows. At 6, Between Worlds answers his engage — drop the rift and if he's outside it he can't target Twisted Advance onto you, so you walk through, dodge the root, and all-in once he's chipped low. Keep Across the Veil reserved for his W: he commits the root, you leap it, and the takedown reset refunds your escape. Don't dump your whole kit into a sapling-shielded Maokai without a curse-recast lined up — his Sap Magic erases sloppy chip damage.","late":"Lane is yours, but Maokai scales into a teamfight tank — his AoE Twisted Advance root, sapling zone and bramble-tank frontline matter far more in a 5v5 than they ever did 1v1, and he keeps soaking your poke with Sap Magic. Your edge narrows once he's stacked health and magic resist, because a full-tank Maokai shrugs single-target poke. Convert the lead before that lands: take plates, use Between Worlds' wall-walk to roam, and force the side-lane 1v1 where you still own him. Respect a flash-into-Twisted-Advance root picking you off when Across the Veil is down — that's the one way he flips a fight.","whys":["You're a single-spell mage at level 1 and he just drops an E sapling to push and farm — neither side threatens a kill, so set up your CS at max Q range.","Second Q point plus the recast lets you start the poke war through his saplings, and your passive spirits heal the chip he answers with.","With Q, E and W online you poke-and-disengage faster than Sap Magic regenerates — bait his Twisted Advance root, leap it with W, and punish the whiff.","Your passive sustain and dropping Q cooldown win the HP race; zone him off the wave with The Weirding's slow while staying at Q range.","Between Worlds lets you all-in: outside the rift he can't target Twisted Advance onto you, so you dodge his only engage and burst him low.","When your W is down and he lands Twisted Advance, his saplings plus the Q knockback-slam can chain you into a jungle gank — that's his one kill window.","A full-tank Maokai out-sustains single-target poke and his AoE root scales into fights — close the game on plates and side-lane pressure before that lands."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"mel","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q's curse-and-recall double hit plus E's slow-and-hop you win the spell exchange against her single Q poke, and Spirit Abjuration heals the chip back so her attrition never lands."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds slows her inside the rift and lets you cross it at will — bait Rebuttal, dodge Solar Snare, drop in with the W leap, and curse-recall her down before she can answer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your curse-recall burst — one Q double-hit plus the W all-in converts her low base health into a kill before her passive stacks ramp."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Mel ramps her Overwhelm passive and brings Golden Eclipse (R) online, her stacked-target execute and longer range reclaim the poke war — close the lane before then."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the Q-poke war — curse her, recast for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the trade back faster than her single Q chips you","Hit Level 6 and use Between Worlds' outside-untargetability to ignore her Q line and Solar Snare, then W-leap the all-in onto her low base health","Snowball your W-reset takedowns and end the lane before her Overwhelm stacks and Golden Eclipse execute scale online"],"foe":["Land her ranged Q poke and ramp Overwhelm stacks to chip you down before you ever close the gap","Catch your W-leap commit with Solar Snare (E) and burst you while your hop and E disengage are on cooldown","Glow up Rebuttal (W) as you commit so your Q missile and E blast reflect back, then finish with the Golden Eclipse execute"]},"early":"Level 1 is a coinflip — you're a no-escape single-spell mage and she's a ranged poke mage, so just last-hit and don't walk into a free Q. Once Q and E come online at 2-3 the lane tilts your way: curse her with Q, recast for the second hit, and slow-hop out with E so her return poke whiffs. Crucially, Spirit Abjuration heals every spell you land, so you win a war of attrition her single Q can't sustain. Don't poke into her Rebuttal (W) when it glows — it reflects your Q missile straight back — and never sit in her Q line while your W hop is down.","mid":"This is your takeover. Levels 4-5 your poke, passive healing and W cooldown all line up, so you control the trades and zone her off CS. At 6 it becomes lopsided — Between Worlds makes you untargetable to her from outside the rift, so you can walk straight through her Q poke and Solar Snare, drop in with the W leap, and burst her down with the curse-recall combo. Bait her Rebuttal (W) reflect before you commit your projectiles, and remember every W takedown resets the leap so you can repeat or roam off the kill.","late":"You own the lane through your first item, but Mel is a scaling stack-mage and 2+ items is where she reclaims it — her Overwhelm passive ramps her poke and Golden Eclipse (R) executes you for fishing in her range once she's stacked you. Itemized, she out-ranges your poke war and Rebuttal (W) turns your committed Q and E back on you. Win the lane outright in the mid window, force a W-reset snowball, and end the game before her items come fully online — don't get dragged into a long-range poke trade you no longer win.","whys":["You're a no-escape single-spell mage and so is she — neither can hard-commit level 1, so last-hit and set up the poke war.","Q's curse plus the recast second hit gives you trade damage her single Q can't match, and Spirit Abjuration heals it back.","With Q and E online you curse-recast then slow-hop away — her single poke whiffs while your passive keeps you topped off.","Levels 4-5 your poke, passive healing and W cooldown all align — you out-trade and zone her off the wave before ults.","Between Worlds slows her inside the rift and you cross it on command, so you pick the angle on her Q line and W-leap the all-in.","Luden's/Malignance sharpens your curse-recall burst — one combo plus the W converts her low base health into a kill.","Mel out-scales you — her Overwhelm-ramped poke, longer range and Golden Eclipse execute reclaim the lane once itemized, so close it before her items land."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Skill","Mordekaiser","Skill","Mordekaiser"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Morde has only his Q (Obliterate) up and no E (Death's Grasp) to pull you, so you can float a Q (Twofold Hex), recast it back through him for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration spirits drift home to heal the trade before he can isolate you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Realm of Death is his kill button: he seals you in a 1v1 and steals your stats, and neither W (Across the Veil) nor R (Between Worlds) breaks you out of his realm — hold W to leap-dodge the R cast and only contest 6 when your W is up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His Riftmaker/Rylai's spike turns the lane: W (Indestructible) heals through your poke, his isolated-Q out-damages your trades, and Rylai's slow makes his E-pull land for free — your spirit-poke war stops paying off here."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once your Luden's/Malignance is online you reclaim the skirmish — kite his dashless frame with E's (The Weirding) slow-and-hop, but burst rather than chip, since damage he takes refills Indestructible."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Q (Twofold Hex) and recast it back through Morde for the double hit, healing the trade with Spirit Abjuration spirits while staying outside E-pull range","Hold W (Across the Veil) as a reaction, not an engage — leap to dodge his E (Death's Grasp) or to blink the R cast, since W's takedown reset never comes in this lane","Drag the game to a sidelane skirmish at 2+ items where E's slow-and-hop kites a champion with no dash"],"foe":["Land E (Death's Grasp) to pull you in, then slam isolated Q (Obliterate) for the bonus damage and bank the W shield off the trade","Hit level 6 and R you into Realm of Death while your W is on cooldown, stealing your stats inside the sealed duel","Force extended fights past his first item so W's heal and isolated-Q out-sustain your spirit poke"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours for once: Morde has only Q (Obliterate) up and no E (Death's Grasp) to drag you in, so throw a Q (Twofold Hex), recast it back through him for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration spirits float home to heal any return poke. The danger arrives at 2 — his E hooks you into isolated-Q range and his W (Indestructible) eats your trade, so never stand in pull range to greed a double-Q. By 3 it is a genuine skill lane: poke from max range, recast Q to pull the curse back through him, and use E's (The Weirding) slow-and-hop to peel off the instant he steps up to E.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your window — your Q comes up faster, your spirit healing stacks, and W (Across the Veil) is available to leap his E-pull, so you own the poke war before his ult exists. Bank every plate and chunk here, because 6 flips it: Between Worlds does NOT save you once Realm of Death seals the 1v1 and steals your stats. Treat his level 6 like a trap — hold W and E purely to react, and never trade with your W on cooldown. If you must contest, bait the E first, leap it with W, then re-poke while his pull recharges.","late":"His first item is his strongest point against you — Riftmaker/Rylai's lets W heal and his isolated-Q out-grind your poke, and the slow makes his E-pull nearly unmissable. Survive that bump and the game tilts back: at 2+ items your Luden's/Malignance poke and E-slow kite punish a champion with no dash, so push for sidelane skirmishes where you chip his decaying W shield, stay out of E range, and commit your W-reset all-in only when his R is down. Win the spacing war and his isolation duel never gets to start.","whys":["He has only Q and no E-pull at level 1, so a single Q (Twofold Hex) recast chips him while Spirit Abjuration spirits heal the trade clean — Aurora's window.","Level 2 hands Morde his E (Death's Grasp) to drag you into isolated-Q range plus the W shield to eat your poke, so the trade math swings to him — respect the hook.","By 3 it is even: you poke from max range and recast Q through him, but his E-pull and W sustain answer back, so neither side owns the trade — pure skill.","Levels 4-5 line up your faster Q, stacked spirit healing, and W being up to dodge the E-pull — you control the poke war before ults exist, so this is Aurora's.","Realm of Death seals you in a 1v1 and steals your stats, and no W leap or R rift breaks out of it once he times R on your W cooldown — Morde's kill window.","His Riftmaker/Rylai's spike lets W heal and isolated-Q out-grind your poke while the slow makes his E-pull stick, so your spirit poke stops winning the math — Morde's bump.","At 2+ items your Luden's poke and E-slow kite punish his dashless frame — skirmish in the sidelane and all-in only when his R is down, so the late game is Aurora's."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"nasus","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Nasus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q (Twofold Hex) and E (The Weirding) online you start the poke war — fire Q, recast to drag the curse back through him for the second hit, then E to slow-and-hop away while his only answer is to keep last-hitting for Siphoning Strike stacks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your hardest kill window before he is online: drop the rift to slow and zone, leap in with W (Across the Veil) untargetable, and the Q double-hit bursts him — a takedown resets W so you leap straight back out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q burst and waveclear — keep shoving and zoning him off the wave so Siphoning Strike never reaches the stack count it needs to matter."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"This is his window: Wither (W) craters your attack and move speed so you cannot kite, and a stacked Siphoning Strike chunks you for half your bar — close the game before he gets here."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish every walk-up with Q recast + E so he either eats free poke or gives up Siphoning Strike last-hits","Hit 6 and use the Between Worlds + W-reset all-in to snowball a kill while he is still farming for stacks","Convert the early-mid lead into plates, roams off W, and objectives — end the game before his stacked Q and Wither flip it"],"foe":["Free-farm Siphoning Strike stacks safely under turret, soaking your poke until his sustain outlasts it","Land Wither (W) the instant you leap in with your W, gutting your attack/move speed so you cannot disengage","Drag the lane past 2+ items where stacked Q, Wither, and R lifesteal/size make him unkillable"]},"early":"Level 1 is roughly even — you are a single-target poke mage with no hard escape until W, and he only wants to last-hit, so stay at range, deny his Siphoning Strike (Q) stacks, and do not over-extend into a jungle gank. From level 2 the lane tilts to you: fire Twofold Hex (Q), recast it to pull the curse back through him for the second hit, then E (The Weirding) to slow him and hop backward so he eats poke he can't trade back — Wither reaches 700 units, so hold that gap and he has no answer. Your passive spirits heal you through every exchange, so the longer the poke war runs the further ahead you get. Just hold W (Across the Veil) for the dodge — it is your only real escape if his jungler shows.","mid":"This is your takeover window. Your Q poke, passive healing, and short W cooldown all line up so you control trades and zone him off the wave — every stack you deny is permanent damage he never gets. At 6, Between Worlds is the all-in: drop the rift to slow and zone, leap in with W untargetable, and burst with the Q double-hit; land the takedown and W resets so you immediately leap to safety or chase. The one thing that flips a won fight is Wither (W) — if he lands it your attack and move speed crater and you can't kite out, so commit only when his Wither is on cooldown, never when you are already low and in point-blank range.","late":"Be honest — this flips. Nasus is a hard scaler, and once Siphoning Strike (Q) is stacked and he has Wither plus his R lifesteal and size online, he shrugs off your poke and a single Wither craters your kiting long enough for a stacked Q to delete you. Your kit has no way to survive a fully-stacked Q connecting. So your entire job is to make late game never happen: snowball your early-mid lead into turret plates, roam off W mobility, and force objectives to end before the 2+ item mark. If it goes long, use R untargetability to reposition and let your team peel — never duel him.","whys":["Level 1 is a skill check — you out-range him but have no escape till W, while he just farms; deny his Siphoning Strike last-hits and don't over-extend.","At 2-3 your Q-recast plus E poke starts chipping him and his Q stacking can't trade back, while your passive heals the exchange.","Your full Q double-hit plus E out-damages anything he can do at range, and your spirits sustain you through the whole poke war.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all line up — you out-trade and zone him off CS before either of you hits 6.","Between Worlds makes you untargetable for the all-in and W resets on the takedown, so he has no escape from your level-6 kill window.","Your Luden's/Malignance Q-burst spike outpaces him on the wave — keep shoving and zoning so his Siphoning Strike never gets dangerous.","He out-scales hard: stacked Siphoning Strike plus a Wither that shuts off your kiting one-shots you, so this 2+ item window is his."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"nautilus","win":["Nautilus","Skill","Skill","Nautilus","Aurora","Skill","Nautilus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Nautilus walks up under his Titan's Wrath shield and lands a Dredge Line hook into a passive root-and-auto — his single biggest snowball window before you have W: Across the Veil to leap out of the pull."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one clean swing — drop the rift to become untargetable to him from outside, walk through his Dredge Line range, and Q-burst him while his immobile tank body has no way to answer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden’s/Malignance sharpens your Twofold Hex, but his 1150-range Dredge Line outreaches your 900 Q — chip only while the hook sits on its 12s cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"His Riptide slow into Depth Charge single-target knockup chains long enough that one missed W means full lockdown — and a two-item tank shrugs off your poke, so never get sidelaned without W or R up."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke at your 900 max range and sidestep the hook — Dredge Line reaches 1150, so distance alone never keeps you safe","Save W: Across the Veil purely to leap his Dredge Line hook or his R knockup, not to engage","Hit 6 and use Between Worlds' untargetability to disengage his all-in or walk in for a free Q combo from inside the rift"],"foe":["Land Dredge Line to pull you in and chain it with his passive root-and-auto before you can W out","Walk you down with Titan's Wrath shield up and pin you in the Riptide slow waves whenever your W is down","Reach 6 and chain Depth Charge knockup into a Dredge Line hook to lock you for his whole follow-up or a gank"]},"early":"Nautilus is a real lane bully into you early — his Titan's Wrath shield eats your level-1 Twofold Hex poke and his Dredge Line hook plus passive root-and-auto catch you before you have W: Across the Veil to leap out. Do not walk up to throw a Q he can answer with a hook; hug max range and chip with the missile so the recast pull-back hit lands without you stepping into Dredge Line distance. Your Spirit Abjuration passive heals you back through his shield-poke, so you can win a slow attrition CS war — just respect that getting hooked once before you have W means eating a full root-and-auto into Riptide.","mid":"Once you have W up every trade, you get to actually poke. Bait his Dredge Line — when it whiffs or you W-dodge it, he's a sitting immobile tank you can Twofold Hex from range while your passive sustains the trade and E: The Weirding slows-and-hops you back out. Level 6 is your one clean swing: Between Worlds makes you untargetable to him from outside the rift, so you slip his hook, ignore the Depth Charge knockup, and burst him from inside. Hold W religiously for his hook; if you blow it to engage, his passive root plus the Riptide slow will stick you for the counter.","late":"This is where he reclaims it. A two-item Nautilus is a CC machine — Riptide slow into single-target Depth Charge knockup chains long enough that one missed W means you're locked the entire duration, and a tank shrugs off your poke. You can't out-DPS his HP bar in a straight fight, so never get caught sidelaning without W or R available. Your job is to have closed the lead in the mid window and to poke/peel for your team from max range, not to 1v1 him once his items and the enemy jungler arrive on top of his chain CC.","whys":["Nautilus walks up with Titan's Wrath shield and threatens a Dredge Line hook into passive root-and-auto before you have W to escape it.","You get Twofold Hex plus passive sustain online and can start chipping, but his shield and hook keep the level genuinely even.","With Q and E: The Weirding you can poke-and-disengage, yet one landed Dredge Line still flips the trade — neither side owns it cleanly.","His shield-poke and the constant hook threat let him walk you down whenever your W cooldown is exposed.","Between Worlds makes you untargetable to him from outside the rift to dodge his hook and Depth Charge, plus the W-reset snowball — your clearest window.","Your Luden’s/Malignance poke chips him from range, but his first tank item soaks it and the 1150 hook still reaches you.","A two-item tank shrugs off your poke and chains the Riptide slow into Depth Charge knockup to lock you the moment your W is down."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"neeko","win":["Skill","Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Neeko","Skill","Neeko"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q (Twofold Hex) and E (The Weirding) poke-and-hop come online, but her E (Tangle-Barbs) is a long-range line root that locks you for her Q+W burst before you can answer with a recast."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R (Pop Blossom) is the danger window — she dashes in and AOE-stuns, and if your W (Across the Veil) is on cooldown you have no leap to dodge it; your R untargetability only saves you if it is up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst — your one window to out-trade her IF her clone (W, Shapesplitter) disguise is down and she has no E to answer your step-up."},{"when":"Late","text":"She picks you from fog with R the instant your team catches your W down; never facecheck a brush or a 'minion' that could be her W clone disguise."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait out her E (Tangle-Barbs) root, then Q-recast and E-hop poke while it is on cooldown","Hold your W (Across the Veil) leap to dodge her R Pop Blossom dash-stun, not to chase poke","Spot her W clone disguise in the wave and never commit your Q-recast combo onto the fake"],"foe":["Land her E root to freeze you for her Q-into-W burst chain","Hide a clone (W) in the minion wave to bait your Q-recast onto nothing and fish for a free root","Catch you with W on cooldown and AOE-stun you with R Pop Blossom"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you are both single-target pokers with no hard escape, so trade your Q (Twofold Hex) for her Q at max range and last-hit safely; your passive (Spirit Abjuration) heal off her minion-spirits actually wins a clean poke war here. From Level 2 her E (Tangle-Barbs) out-ranges your poke and roots you long enough to land her whole Q-into-W combo, so do not step up to throw a Q she can answer with a line root. Bait the E, then poke with your Q-recast and E-hop while it is down — and watch the wave, because a clone (W, Shapesplitter) hiding in her minions is how she fishes for a free root.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are hers. Her root sets up more burst than your passive spirit-heal can claw back, and at 6 her R Pop Blossom is the problem your kit cannot fully answer: she dashes in and AOE-stuns, and your only dodge is the W (Across the Veil) leap. If you have burned W to poke or reposition, you eat the full stun-burst and die before your R untargetability matters. Hold W exclusively to blink her R or her E — never to chase a poke — and only all-in when both her E and R are down and you have eyes on the real Neeko, not a clone.","late":"She out-picks you late. From fog her R one-shots a squishy mage, and your R untargetability (Between Worlds) plus W invisibility only save you if they are up the moment she commits — one caught W and you are deleted before your Q poke matters. Group with vision, never facecheck a brush or a stray 'minion' that could be her disguised W clone, and treat every missing Neeko as a primed Pop Blossom. Your realistic out is converting an early-mid lead off her whiffed E roots into objectives before her pick potential decides fights.","whys":["You are both escape-light single-target pokers at 1 — trade Q for Q at max range, and your passive spirit-heal off her minions actually edges a clean poke war.","Her E (Tangle-Barbs) line root out-ranges your poke and locks you for her Q burst, so stepping up to Q gets you rooted and traded down.","With E plus Q online she roots-and-bursts harder than your passive heals back, and your E-hop disengage cannot outpace a landed root.","Her root keeps setting up trades your poke loses, and you cannot all-in into a long-range CC that catches you before your W resets.","Her R Pop Blossom dashes in and AOE-stuns — if your W leap is down there is no dodge, and the stun-burst kills a squishy mage.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens your Q-recast enough to out-poke her IF no clone is up and her E is down — your one even window.","Full-AP Neeko picks you from fog with R the moment your W is on cooldown — her pick potential out-scales your poke."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"olaf","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Twofold Hex out, then recast to drag the curse back for the second hit while your E damages, slows, and hops you backward out of axe range — your passive heals the chip and Olaf can only answer with one axe throw."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds: drop the rift to damage and slow his all-in, walk through the wall and go untargetable to his outside the moment he charges, then collapse with Q-recast burst plus W — land the takedown and your Across the Veil resets."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's or Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst — chunk him below his lifesteal threshold before his bruiser items (Black Cleaver / Bramble) come online and his axe-sustain spikes."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Ragnarok cleanses your E-slow and the rift slow, makes him CC-immune, and Reckless Swing's true damage ignores shields — his lifesteal then auto-DPSes straight through your poke, so never stand in axe range once he has 2 items."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the poke war with Q-curse recasts and E's damage-slow-and-hop while Spirit Abjuration heals the chip back between trades","Trade when Reckless Swing is on cooldown so his self-damage true hit and lifesteal sustain are both offline","Use Level 6 Between Worlds untargetability and wall-walk to dodge his R charge, then snowball Across the Veil resets before his items"],"foe":["Pick up his thrown axes to reset the 9s Undertow, and let Berserker Rage turn his own low health into attack speed","Land Reckless Swing's flat true damage when your Across the Veil leap is on cooldown to chunk you with no counterplay","Hit 2 items and pop Ragnarok to cleanse your slows, go CC-immune, land Reckless Swing's true damage, and out-DPS you in the straight duel"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you're a single-target poke mage with no leap until 2 and Olaf wants to walk up and throw an axe, so just last-hit and hold your distance. From level 2-3 you take over: fire Twofold Hex to curse him, recast to pull the curse back for the second hit, weave in The Weirding to damage, slow, and hop yourself backward, and Spirit Abjuration heals the chip so the poke war is yours. The one thing to respect is Reckless Swing — flat true damage on a short cooldown that costs him health — so trade only when his E is down, and don't let him pick up his thrown axes (it refunds Undertow's cooldown and gives him attack and move speed to chase).","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your peak. Your Q cooldown drops, your passive sustain stacks, and you out-poke him long before his bruiser items land — keep cursing and recasting, slow and disengage with E, and never stand still in axe-throw range. At 6, Between Worlds is the trump card: drop the rift to damage and slow, walk through the wall and go untargetable the moment he pops Ragnarok and charges, then collapse with the Q-recast burst plus the Across the Veil leap. Land the takedown and your W resets — that's how you snowball this lane before his scaling kicks in.","late":"This is where Olaf takes the matchup back, so the clock is your enemy. Once he has 2 items, Ragnarok cleanses your E-slow and the rift slow, makes him CC-immune, and his Reckless Swing true damage ignores any shielding in your kit — and his lifesteal lets him heal straight through your poke. You cannot win that straight 1v1 late, so close the lane in the early-mid windows: snowball your Across the Veil resets, take plates and a lead before his first-item axe-sustain spike, and end before the 2-item mark. If it goes long, stop dueling him and play the rift for picks and zoning around your team.","whys":["You're a no-leap-until-2 poke mage at level 1 and Olaf wants to walk up and axe-trade — concede it, last-hit, and set up your level 2 spike.","With Twofold Hex's recast and The Weirding online you start the poke war; the curse's second hit plus Spirit Abjuration's heal win the trade while he can only commit one axe.","Your Q-recast burst plus E damage-and-slow out-trades him and your passive out-sustains his pre-item poke — punish whenever Reckless Swing is on cooldown.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all line up — you control trades and zoning before his bruiser items exist.","Between Worlds' wall-walk and untargetability dodge his Ragnarok charge while the rift zones his all-in, and the Across the Veil reset on takedown snowballs the lane.","Your Luden's or Malignance burst spike outpaces his first axe-sustain item — convert your lead and force the all-in before his bruiser stats arrive.","Olaf out-scales hard — Ragnarok cleanses your slows, goes CC-immune, and Reckless Swing ignores shields while his lifesteal out-DPSes you, so don't duel him late."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"ornn","win":["Ornn","Ornn","Skill","Skill","Ornn","Ornn","Ornn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Ornn drops his Q pillar (Volcanic Rupture) to wall you off, then E-charges (Searing Charge) into terrain for a knockup-stun and follows with W Brittle — and you have only one spell, no W escape, and no way to punish his greed early."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your only honest window: Q-curse poke plus the recast pull-back chips him while your passive spirit heals refund the trade, and a missed Ornn E or W cone leaves him with no way to catch you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ornn's R (Call of the Forge God) summons a ram that he recasts to knock you up and re-apply Brittle — the ram's ground AoE still hits you inside Between Worlds, since untargetability only blocks OUTSIDE single-target attacks, not the rift-overlapping elemental."},{"when":"2nd item","text":"Ornn self-forges his Masterwork upgrades and stacks armor/MR, so your Q+E poke stops denting his health bar while his W Brittle (max-health damage + tenacity shred) makes every all-in his."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit the level 4-5 poke window with Q-curse + recast pull-back and let passive spirit heals refund each trade, before his Brittle and E knockup come fully online","Use W (Across the Veil) to leap OUT when he commits E — bait the charge into empty space so it whiffs terrain and grants no knockup, then curse him on the recovery","Roam with R untargetability or snowball elsewhere — you cannot grind down a self-itemizing tank in a straight poke war and have no kill threat on his health bar"],"foe":["Q-pillar to wall Aurora against terrain, then E-charge into the wall for the knockup-stun and chain W Brittle before her W escape is up","Land W Bellows Breath to Brittle her, then AA-knockback or R-recast knockup the instant her Across the Veil leap is on cooldown","Self-forge Masterwork upgrades and stack armor/MR — his bulk and Brittle max-health damage win every trade and all-in from two items on"]},"early":"Ornn is one of the worst level-1s in the game, but so are you on a single spell — and his payoff is the brutal one. The trap is his Q pillar (Volcanic Rupture): he drops it to wall you against terrain, then E-charges (Searing Charge) into that wall for a knockup-stun and follows with W Bellows Breath to Brittle you. You have no escape until you rank W. Don't sit in his W cone or E lane to force a Q — last-hit with the curse missile's tip and let your passive spirit heals tick up. His W is a skillshot cone, not point-and-click, but if you over-step into it the Brittle AA flips the trade hard.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your one honest window — your Q-curse poke and recast pull-back chip his bulk, your passive spirit heals refund the trade, and his cooldowns (W cone, E charge) are long enough that a single whiff leaves him unable to catch you. Throw the Q, recast for the second hit, and hold W to leap OUT the instant he commits his E — bait the charge into open ground so it never reaches terrain and grants no knockup. But this is chip, not a kill: he is a tank with no kill threat to YOU until 6, and your poke alone will never out-pace his health bar plus self-forged resistances.","late":"This is where the lane is simply lost on a straight 1v1. Ornn self-forges his Masterwork item upgrades and stacks armor and MR, and your Q+E poke stops registering on his health bar. His R is the back-breaker: a summoned ram (Call of the Forge God) that he recasts to knock you up and re-apply Brittle — and its ground AoE still catches you inside Between Worlds, because untargetability only blocks OUTSIDE single-target attacks, not an elemental overlapping your own rift. Don't try to duel him for the lane; use R untargetability to walk through walls and roam, find picks on weaker targets, and let your team peel his engage.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1, but his Q pillar can wall you for a free E-charge knockup-stun into W Brittle while you have only one spell and no escape.","His Q-wall plus E knockup combo means any step-up for a Q-curse lets him flip the trade with hard CC you can't yet dodge with W.","You finally get Q+E online to start the poke war and W-bait his E charge into whiffing terrain — but his tank bulk makes it even chip, not a lead.","Your poke, passive spirit heals, and W cooldown line up, but his W on cooldown only buys you trades, not a kill on a self-healing tank with resistances.","His R ram knocks you up and re-applies Brittle, and its ground AoE lands even inside your untargetable rift — your level 6 all-in answer is far worse than his.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens poke, but he self-forges Masterwork armor/MR the same patch and your curses stop denting him.","Ornn out-scales hard: self-forged upgrades, stacked resistances, and W Brittle max-health damage mean your poke is irrelevant and his CC ends every fight."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"pantheon","win":["Pantheon","Pantheon","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Pantheon point-clicks Shield Vault (W) at 600 to stun you and follows with an empowered Comet Spear (Q) — that lands before Spirit Abjuration has stacked healing, so give ground and last-hit at your 900 tip."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your Q (Twofold Hex) recast-poke plus passive spirit healing come online together — start chipping him, and bait Aegis Assault (E, 22s) so your poke lands on the side it isn't blocking."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds (R) is your answer to his all-in: when he Shield Vaults in, walk into the rift untargetable, let his Q whiff, then W-reset off the takedown to flip the lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your first AP item (Luden's/Malignance) sharpens the Q recast burst while Pantheon's spear damage flattens into items — the duel tilts to you from here."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the level 1-3 Shield Vault into empowered Spear all-in without feeding, last-hitting at max Q range","Reach 4-6 where stacked Spirit Abjuration healing lets you win the Q poke war his spear can't sustain","Bait Shield Vault, drop Between Worlds to go untargetable through his combo, then W-reset the takedown"],"foe":["Land the level-2 Shield Vault stun into empowered Comet Spear before your passive healing exists","Angle Aegis Assault toward your Q to block the poke and trade for free while ahead","Snowball the early lead or use his global R to roam before Aurora out-scales him into items"]},"early":"Pantheon owns these levels and you have to respect it — his point-click Shield Vault (W) stun into an empowered Comet Spear (Q) is a real all-in that lands before Spirit Abjuration has stacked enough healing to carry a trade. Do not step up to throw a Twofold Hex he can answer by stunning you mid-animation, and watch his Aegis Assault (E): when he holds it toward you it eats your Q and autos from that direction, so a face-up trade does less than you think. Last-hit at the very tip of your Q, eat a little spear poke, and just survive to level 4 — your sustain wins the long game, not the level-2 fight.","mid":"Now it starts to even out. By 4-5 your Twofold Hex recast-poke and passive spirit healing line up, so you can open a poke war a falling-off Pantheon can't sustain — he heals nothing back while your spirits trickle health to you. Bait his Aegis Assault first so your Q lands on his open side, and never commit into an up Shield Vault. At 6 your R answers his all-in: when he leaps in and stuns, drop Between Worlds, walk untargetable through the rift while his Spear whiffs, then W-reset off the takedown. The lane is a coin-flip until you respect that one stun.","late":"This is your half of the lane — Pantheon is a level 1-6 bully who flattens into a worse skirmisher once items arrive, while your first AP spike (Luden's/Malignance) sharpens the Twofold Hex recast burst and poke. Keep forcing trades and side-lane skirmishes where stacked Spirit Abjuration healing and Between Worlds' untargetability shrug off his fading spear. The one real threat now is his global Grand Starfall roam, so ward, ping his MIA, then press your duel advantage before he decides another lane for free.","whys":["Pantheon's Shield Vault stun into empowered Comet Spear out-damages your single level-1 spell before Spirit Abjuration has stacked any healing.","He hits his level-2 power spike first and can point-click stun-into-Q all-in you while you still lack the recast poke to answer.","Your Twofold Hex poke and spirit healing start trading back, but his spear and a well-angled Aegis Assault keep the trade a coin-flip.","Your passive sustain and W-dodge come online, yet a mistimed step-up still eats his Shield Vault stun, so the window is a true skill test.","Between Worlds walks untargetable through his Shield Vault all-in and the takedown W-reset lets Aurora flip and snowball the lane.","Aurora's first AP item sharpens the Twofold Hex recast burst while Pantheon's spear damage has already fallen off into the item phase.","In a straight 2-item duel Aurora out-sustains and out-scales him, but his global Grand Starfall lets Pantheon decide the game on another lane."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"poppy","win":["Poppy","Skill","Skill","Poppy","Poppy","Poppy","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"The moment Poppy has Steadfast Presence (20s at rank 1) she can stop your Across the Veil leap inside 400 units of her and ground you where it stops — never leap toward her."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your one early window: Q-curse then recall it for the second hit and E-poke while her E (Heroic Charge) is on cooldown, then hop back with The Weirding before she can wall-pin you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R is an ESCAPE here, not a kill button — Between Worlds' slow and the free crossing pull you out of a Heroic Charge wall-stun, not into an all-in on a tank."},{"when":"1st item","text":"One armor item and her Steadfast Presence outlast your full Q-recall-E rotation — she eats the poke, lands one wall-pin while your W is down, and Hammer Shock plus autos finish you."}],"wants":{"you":["Q-curse and recall it for the second hit only when her W (Steadfast Presence) is down — that is the only window your leap and poke both work","Hold The Weirding (E) hop and your W leap as anti-engage answers to her Heroic Charge wall-pin, never spend them as poke openers","Save Between Worlds to break out of a wall-stun all-in and farm the lane out — never commit it onto a tank you cannot burst"],"foe":["Keep Steadfast Presence up so any leap you make within 400 units of her is stopped, slowed and grounded","Land Heroic Charge (E) into a wall for the stun while your W is on cooldown, then Hammer Shock (Q) slow and autos for the kill","Soak your poke behind her buckler shield, build armor, and swing teamfights with the Keeper's Verdict (R) knockback while you farm safely"]},"early":"Respect this from minute one — the second Poppy has Steadfast Presence (20s at rank 1) she can stop your Across the Veil leap inside 400 units of her and ground you, so you never jump toward her. Farm at max Q range and chip with the recast second hit, but do not step into Heroic Charge range with your leap on cooldown, because a wall-pin stun into Hammer Shock and autos is a free kill. Your one micro-window is around level 3 while her E is down: curse, recast it for the second hit, poke with The Weirding and hop straight back before she can answer.","mid":"My passive spirit-heal sustain means little here — she soaks the poke behind her buckler shield and her armor only grows, so the trade math that beats squishy bruisers does not apply to a tank. At 6 I do NOT all-in: Between Worlds can't burst through her health and armor, so I treat R as the escape that finally beats her wall-pin — go untargetable or walk a wall out when she commits Heroic Charge. The whole mid-game is denying her the wall-stun engage and farming, not winning trades.","late":"This stays bad. Once she has an armour item she walks through your full curse-recast-Weirding rotation, and she only needs one Heroic Charge into a wall while your leap is grounded to kill you, while Keeper's Verdict makes her a problem in every fight you don't dictate. Look for sidelane farm and pick-offs on her squishier teammates with your poke rather than the 1v1, and lean on the rift purely to survive her engage. Get the lead elsewhere on the map — this lane is damage control, not a kill lane.","whys":["Once Poppy picks Steadfast Presence she stops any leap made within 400 units of her and grounds you — your escape is only safe at range.","Her Heroic Charge cooldown gives you brief level-2 windows to last-hit and land a little Q poke, but you still respect the wall-pin and keep your distance.","Level 3 with Q-recall and the E hop is your one even window — chip and disengage while her Heroic Charge is down, never while it is up.","Her buckler shield and growing armor soak your Q-recall-E poke, so your spirit-heal sustain trade flips in her favor on a tank.","Your R can't burst a tank — Between Worlds is the escape here, so at 6 she still owns the all-in off her wall-pin stun.","One armor item lets her walk through your full combo, and a single Heroic Charge into a wall with your W down sets up her Hammer Shock and autos to kill you.","Late she pins you with a grounded escape and swings fights with her Keeper's Verdict (R) knockback — you survive and farm, you do not win the 1v1."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"quinn","win":["Quinn","Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Quinn's Harrier-marked auto and Blinding Assault (Q) poke own level 1 — you only have Twofold Hex (Q) and no W leap yet, so just last-hit and eat the chip."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Q-curse + recast, your E slow online, and Spirit Abjuration spirits healing the chip, you start the poke war and out-sustain her Harrier."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds: drop the rift on her and she is slowed inside it while you cross freely — Vault bounces her to the rift edge, not out of the fight, so the all-in lands."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst — one full curse combo plus W deletes a squishy Quinn before her Vault-and-Harrier kite resets the gap."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q out-going and recast it so the curse-pull return hit clips her even after she sidesteps with Harrier move speed","Use Across the Veil to leap onto her, and at 6 drop the rift so Vault's bounce leaves her slowed inside it instead of clear of you","Stack Spirit Abjuration spirits off Q/E pokes so her Harrier chip never out-trades your passive sustain"],"foe":["Vault onto you to interrupt, then bounce back to attack range and kite with Harrier's nimble move speed","Poke you from max auto range and roam the second you back off the wave — she pressures the map, not just the lane","Save Vault to interrupt your leap all-in and bounce straight back out to attack range"]},"early":"Level 1 is hers — she's a ranged carry with Harrier nimble move speed and you only have Twofold Hex (Q) and no leap yet, so don't try to trade, just last-hit and accept the Blinding Assault poke and its blind. The lane flips fast though: once you have the curse plus The Weirding's slow at 3, recast your Q so the curse-pull drags the missile back through her even after she Harrier-kites the first hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the chip back. Respect Vault (12s at rank 1) — it dashes onto you, interrupts what you are doing and bounces her back to attack range, so poke on your terms and never burn W chasing a kite.","mid":"This is your window. Through levels 4-5 your poke, passive spirit healing and Across the Veil's cooldown all line up — you out-sustain her Harrier chip and zone her off CS while she has no way to punish your spacing. At 6 Between Worlds changes the matchup: the rift slows her while you cross it freely, so Vault's bounce only carries her to the rift edge and still inside the slow, and then you leap in for the kill. Bait Vault first if you can; once her interrupt is down she has no disengage and the all-in is clean.","late":"You hold the duel into your first item — Luden's/Malignance burst means one full Q-recast curse combo plus W deletes a squishy Quinn faster than her Vault-and-Harrier can kite out. Past two items it levels off: she becomes a roaming, splitpushing map threat with vision and lane-to-lane pressure, and a fed Quinn's burst can clip you the moment your W is down. Close the game on your spike — convert your level 6 and first-item leads into towers before her roam-and-splitpush pattern takes over the map.","whys":["Quinn's Harrier-empowered autos and Blinding Assault (Q) poke own level 1 — you have only Twofold Hex and no W escape, so concede it and just farm.","Skill window — your Q-curse and recast come online and you can start poking, but her Harrier kite still trades evenly until your E slow and spirits land.","With Q-recast, E slow and Spirit Abjuration sustain you out-heal her Harrier chip and win the poke war against a Quinn who can't punish your spacing.","Your poke, passive spirit healing and W cooldown all line up — you control trades and zoning before ultimates while she can't answer your spacing.","Between Worlds slows her inside the rift while you cross it freely, so Vault's bounce lands her still inside the slow — that is what turns the rift into a kill.","Your Luden's/Malignance burst spike lets one Q-recast combo plus W delete a squishy Quinn before she Vault-kites out — force the all-in here.","Skill — she reclaims tempo as a roaming splitpush threat and a fed Harrier burst clips you when W is down, so close before two items matter."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"renekton","win":["Renekton","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"His one real window: a fury-empowered Ruthless Predator is a 1.5s point-blank stun straight into Cull the Meek heal-slices. Stay out of melee at level 1 and never trade while Across the Veil is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your poke war opens: Q (Twofold Hex) out-and-recast plus E (The Weirding) chip-and-hop while Spirit Abjuration heals the spirits back, and he has no ranged answer until his E dash is up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your takeover: the rift slows him while you cross it freely, so his Slice and Dice all-in has to start from outside it and you leap clear before the stun."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst right as his fury combo stops one-shotting and his base damage flatlines into your scaling — this is where you snowball the kill."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach level 3 to open the Q-recast plus E-hop poke war his fury combo cannot sustain through, healed back by Spirit Abjuration","Hold W (Across the Veil) for his E dash-in or fury-empowered W stun, never burn it to engage while he has fury and his stun is up","Hit 6 and first item to convert: make him start every all-in from outside the rift, then Twofold Hex burst the kill"],"foe":["Land a fury-empowered W stun while your W blink is down, then chain Q heal-slices on top before you can hop away","Force an all-in at levels 1-2 with full fury, before your Q-E poke range and passive sustain come online","Burn his E dash to close the gap the instant your W (Across the Veil) is on cooldown and stun you in melee"]},"early":"Level 1 belongs to him: a fury-empowered Ruthless Predator is a 1.5s point-blank stun and Cull the Meek (7s) heals him through your chip, so do not walk into melee to throw a Q he can stun you out of. Last-hit at max Q range, keep Across the Veil up for Slice and Dice, and concede a little CS rather than eat the stun. From level 2 it flips — Twofold Hex out-and-recast plus The Weirding's hop chips faster than his fury combo can answer, and Spirit Abjuration heals the trade back.","mid":"This is your lane. With your Q cooldown dropping and three stacks of Spirit Abjuration sustaining you, you out-poke his 300-range trades — he has to burn Slice and Dice (16s at rank 1) to even reach you, and once it is down he is a melee with no follow-up. Bait the fury-empowered Ruthless Predator, then E-poke and Q-recast burst as his fury bar empties. At 6 the rift slows him while you cross it freely, so his all-in has to begin from outside it and every fight happens on your terms.","late":"You take over completely. Renekton has no sustained threat once his early fury combo stops one-shotting and his base damage flatlines — your scaled Q-recast burst out-trades anything he can do, while the rift slow and Across the Veil let you disengage every time he commits Slice and Dice and the stun. Keep poking, zone him off objectives with the rift, and snowball the kills. His only path back is a level-1 snowball banked before your poke turned the lane.","whys":["His fury-empowered Ruthless Predator is a 1.5s point-blank stun and Cull the Meek heals his trades — at level 1, with only one spell up, you lose any melee fight.","Your Q out-and-recast plus E-hop poke chips faster than his fury combo, and Spirit Abjuration heals it back while he has no ranged answer — start the poke war here.","His fury bar empties after one combo and he must walk back into Twofold Hex range to refill — punish the gaps with the recast and hop out.","Your Q cooldown, three-stack passive healing and W reset line up — bait his E dash, then out-trade his point-blank combo from range.","Between Worlds slows his all-in while you cross the rift freely, so Slice and Dice has to start from outside it — you own this window.","Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst right as his fury combo falls off and his base damage flatlines — force every all-in here.","He has no late threat once his early kit stops one-shotting — your scaling burst out-damages him and your R/W mobility mean he can never catch you committed; just close it out."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"riven","win":["Riven","Riven","Skill","Riven","Aurora","Skill","Riven"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Riven leads with Broken Wings dashes to close off your CS, and at 2 Ki Burst adds an 11s stun to lock the trade — you're a single-spell mage with no movement spell yet, so you cannot answer her gap-close before your passive sustain matters."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one clean all-in: the rift slow holds her in your Twofold Hex burst while you cross it freely, and a takedown resets Across the Veil — but Blade of the Exile's Wind Slash still reaches you as you walk out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens Twofold Hex and its recast, but her first bruiser item lets Valor tank a full rotation and stun-burst you the moment Across the Veil is on cooldown."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Riven reclaims it hard — Valor eats your poke and Ki Burst lands a full Broken Wings rotation in the gap after your leap, with no second movement spell to bail you out."}],"wants":{"you":["Fire Twofold Hex on the way out and recast it back through her so the return hit clips her mid-dash, then The Weirding to slow-and-hop clear before Ki Burst lands","Save Across the Veil (22s at rank 1) for AFTER she commits her three Broken Wings dashes — use it to dodge the Ki Burst stun, not as a face-first engage","Reach Level 6 even in HP so the Between Worlds rift slows her while you cross it freely — one all-in her dashes can't answer"],"foe":["Bait out Across the Veil or The Weirding, then dash in on the Ki Burst stun while both your movement spells are down","Use Valor's shield-dash to absorb Twofold Hex poke and close the gap, turning your poke war into her all-in","Land Ki Burst the instant Across the Veil touches down so a full Broken Wings rotation connects before your spirits heal it back"]},"early":"Riven owns the early game and you concede it — at level 1 you're a single-spell mage with no movement ability while she closes with Broken Wings off your CS, and at 2 Ki Burst adds an 11s stun to lock you. Don't throw Twofold Hex to poke when she's even slightly close: she'll dash sideways to dodge the missile, then come back in and trade before your passive spirits matter. Last-hit at max Q range, hold The Weirding as your slow-and-disengage rather than burning it as poke, and treat levels 1-2 as survival, not trading.","mid":"Levels 4-5 still favour her Valor-and-dash all-in, but level 6 is your one real window — Between Worlds slows her inside the rift while you cross it freely, so drop it once she has already spent her three Broken Wings dashes and Valor's 10s shield. The slow pins her in your Twofold Hex curse-and-recast burst, and a takedown resets Across the Veil. Outside that window never sit in lane at half HP: the second your leap is on cooldown she'll Ki Burst into a full rotation and one-combo you, and your spirit sustain can't out-heal a shielded burst.","late":"This is where she takes the lane back for good. Once her bruiser items come online her E shield eats your entire poke rotation and her W stun lands a full Q3 combo in the gap after your W leap — and you have no second movement spell once Across the Veil is down. Your job was to steal kills in your level 6 and first-item rift windows and end before her 2+ item spike; if the game goes long, don't sidelane near her — group where Between Worlds zones a fight and let your team body-block her dashes instead of dueling her solo.","whys":["Level 1 you're a one-spell mage with no movement ability while she dashes in with Broken Wings off your CS — you cannot trade into that.","By 2 she has a second Broken Wings dash plus Ki Burst's 11s stun, and your passive spirit sustain isn't enough to win a trade she initiates.","By 3 you have Twofold Hex and The Weirding to poke-and-hop, but she sidesteps skillshots with Broken Wings — the recast return is your real hit.","Levels 4-5 Valor's shield-dash (10s at rank 1) tanks your poke and closes the gap before Across the Veil's 22s cools for a second reposition.","Between Worlds is your spike: the rift slows her while you cross it freely and holds her in the Twofold Hex burst — your one clean all-in window.","Your Luden's/Malignance sharpens the poke, but her first bruiser item lets Valor shield through it and stun-burst you the instant your W is down — call it even.","She out-duels you at 2+ items: Valor absorbs your combo and Ki Burst lands a full Broken Wings rotation in the gap after your leap, with nothing left to bail you out."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"rumble","win":["Skill","Aurora","Skill","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Aurora's Q-into-recast double-hit out-ranges Rumble's Flamespitter while his heat bar is cold, and her Spirit Abjuration heals back the chip he trades — own the poke war before he banks heat."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aurora's R rift lets her teleport across it to dodge his Equalizer or all-in through it, but on a 130s cooldown he can drop the same line across her CS to zone — neither ult clearly wins the window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Aurora's Luden's/Malignance sharpens Q burst, but Rumble's Liandry's plus a well-timed overheat Flamespitter matches her spike — only commit when his heat bar is empty and Scrap Shield is on cooldown."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Rumble's overheat Flamespitter plus Liandry's burn out-grinds Aurora in any extended fight once his items are online — this is his window, so poke and leave instead of dueling."}],"wants":{"you":["Fire Q through Rumble and recast it to drag the curse back for the second hit, then let your drifting spirits heal you to win the level-2 chip war while his heat is cold","Bait his E harpoon, then W (Across the Veil) sideways into the spirit realm so the slow whiffs and you reposition out of the Flamespitter cone with the move-speed and brief invis","Hold R for when he commits Equalizer — walk through it untargetable to dodge the channel, or use the rift to all-in him while he's locked into the line"],"foe":["Bank heat to max and overheat Flamespitter for the empowered sustained DPS that out-trades Aurora's poke in melee range","Land E harpoon to slow Aurora into a full Flamespitter cone before she can W out, denying her the kite-and-heal pattern","Drop The Equalizer across her wave or escape path to deny CS and zone her out of Q range during the fight"]},"early":"Rumble banks no heat at level 1, so the lane opens neutral — contest the wave but don't walk into a free E harpoon with only one cast available. Once Aurora hits 2-3, her Q-and-recast double-hit out-ranges his cold Flamespitter and Spirit Abjuration heals the chip he trades back, so own the poke war while his heat bar is dark. The trap is his overheat: step into Flamespitter range while he's near max heat and his empowered cone shreds you — poke from max Q distance and back off the moment his bar glows yellow.","mid":"Levels 4-5 belong to Aurora — her Q comes up faster, her passive heal stacks toward three spirits, and she controls spacing before either ult is online. Bait his E harpoon, W sideways into the spirit realm so the slow whiffs, then recast Q for the punish. At 6 it evens out: her R lets her go untargetable to walk out of his Equalizer or all-in through it, but his Equalizer zones her CS and trades just as hard, so respect the line and never channel a fight inside his burn. Save W for after his harpoon, never before — it's her cleanest out once Flamespitter latches on.","late":"This is where Rumble takes over. Once his Liandry's and overheat Flamespitter are online, his sustained AP DPS plus the burn out-grinds Aurora's poke in any extended fight, and his E slow makes her W the only reliable escape. Don't sit in prolonged trades — land the Q burst, leash spirits to heal up, then disengage with E's backward hop before his heat bar fills. If the game goes long, use R for picks and zone control rather than dueling him head-on, because his 2-item skirmish DPS beats hers.","whys":["Rumble banks no heat at level 1 and Aurora has one cast with no leap yet — neither side can commit, so the opening wave is a coinflip.","Aurora's Q-and-recast double-hit out-ranges his cold Flamespitter and her passive heals the return chip, so she owns the level-2 poke war before he banks heat.","It tightens once Rumble has E harpoon to slow her into a Flamespitter cone, but Aurora's Q poke and spirit-heal still edge the trade if she spaces the cone — a near-even window.","Aurora's faster Q cooldown and stacking passive heal line up before ultimates, so she controls spacing — bait his E, W into the spirit realm, and punish out of the Flamespitter follow-up.","At 6 Aurora's untargetable R answers his Equalizer, but his ult zones her farm and trades evenly, so neither side clearly owns the level-6 window.","Aurora's Luden's Q burst spikes, but his Liandry's plus a timed overheat Flamespitter matches it — the trade is even, and she should only all-in when his heat and Scrap Shield are both down.","At 2 items Rumble's overheat Flamespitter and Liandry's burn out-DPS Aurora in extended fights, so she must disengage with E and play for picks rather than duel him."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"ryze","win":["Aurora","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Ryze","Ryze"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Ryze out-ranges your single Q and never has to commit: his Overload (Q) pokes from safety while you have no W leap, no E hop, and zero passive stacks to heal the chip. Just hold max-Q range and farm — you cannot win a stat-check trade yet."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Once you have all three spells, you finally have a pattern: E-in, Q the curse and recast-pull it back through him for the double hit, then W-hop out. Trade only when his W (Rune Prison) root is down — if it lands while your W leap is on cooldown, his E-flux into Q-Overload chunks you with no answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one clean swing of the lane: the rift slows him and you go untargetable to him from inside it, so you can all-in straight through a Rune Prison, secure the kill, and reset your W leap for a free escape."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Ryze becomes the raid-boss this lane was always building toward — Tear-fueled Overload spam with low-cooldown resets out-DPSes your Q-E poke faster than three passive spirits can heal, and Realm Warp (R) answers your roam/splitpush. Snowball a 6 lead and end, because you do not out-scale him."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his W (Rune Prison) or his E-flux, then E-in, Q-curse and recast-pull it back through him for the double hit, and W-hop out before his Overload resets land","Hit Level 6 and use Between Worlds: go untargetable to him inside the rift, all-in through a root, and reset your W leap on the takedown","Convert a 6 power-spike kill into ending the game early — you must close before his Tear stacks turn him into a raid-boss you can't out-trade"],"foe":["Land E (Spell Flux) into W (Rune Prison) to root you the instant your W leap is on cooldown, then free-burst with Overload resets before your passive heals it","Win the open poke war on raw DPS — Tear-fed Overload spam out-chips your Q-recast combo whenever you're caught without your hop","Farm safely behind range to two items, then out-DPS every poke trade and warp the map with Realm Warp (R) to punish your roams"]},"early":"Respect the root chain, but know it's his W that cages you: Ryze's E (Spell Flux) marks you, then W (Rune Prison) roots, and if that lands while your W leap is on cooldown he free-bursts you with Overload (Q) resets before a single passive spirit drifts back to heal you. At Level 1-2 you only have your Q and no escape, so just last-hit at max Q range and eat a little chip. From Level 3 — with E to hop and W to leap — you can start playing around his pattern, but only commit when his Rune Prison is down. Getting rooted with your hop unavailable is exactly how this lane snowballs against you.","mid":"This is a poke war you have to win on spacing, because raw DPS favors him — Tear-fueled Overload spam out-chips your Q-recast chunk over a long trade. Trade strictly around his W cooldown: when Rune Prison is down, E-in, fire Q to curse him, then recast Q to pull the curse back through him for the double hit, and hop out before his Q resets come back around. Level 6 is your one clean swing — Between Worlds slows the all-in and makes you untargetable to him from inside the rift, so you can commit through a root, kill, and reset your W leap. Force that window; outside of it, give nothing and just farm.","late":"Past two items Ryze is the raid-boss this lane was always building toward — Tear-fed Overload resets and his E-W root chain shred you faster than three passive spirits can heal, and your only safety net is a W leap on cooldown. Your R untargetability buys you a single clean dodge or escape, not a sustained duel. Don't try to out-scale him; you can't. Snowball any Level-6 lead into ending the game, because his Realm Warp (R) answers your splitpush and roams, and the longer the game runs the harder his Overload spam out-DPSes every poke trade you try to take.","whys":["Ryze's poke out-ranges your lone Q and his E-into-W root threatens you, while with no leap, no hop and no passive stacks you can neither trade back nor escape the chip.","By Level 3 you have E to hop and W to leap, so you can finally play his pattern — but his Overload poke still matches your Q-recast chip, leaving the open lane a genuine wash when his root is down.","When his W (Rune Prison) is on cooldown, your E-in, Q-curse, recast-pull double-hit lets you win a spacing trade and drift a passive spirit back to heal — your cleanest non-ult edge.","In the open lane his E-flux into Rune Prison plus Overload resets out-trade your poke — if your W leap is down when the root lands, he wins the all-in outright.","Between Worlds slows him and makes you untargetable from inside the rift, so you commit through a root, secure the kill, and reset your W leap — your single clearest window of the lane.","Even with a Luden's/Malignance spike sharpening your Q burst, his Lost Chapter into Tear means Overload spam keeps the raw-DPS poke war tilted to him here.","By two items Ryze is a raid-boss: Tear-fed Overload resets and the E-W root chain shred you faster than passive heals, and his Realm Warp (R) out-scales and out-ranges your splitpush."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"sejuani","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q (Twofold Hex) out-and-back plus E (The Weirding) online, you start a poke war Sejuani can't answer — she has no ranged tool, so she eats your curse-recast chip and your passive heals it back faster than her Frost-stacking autos can punish."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds (R) leaves a slow zone you can teleport across, so you win her spacing outright — but Glacial Prison reveals stealth, so Across the Veil's invisibility will not shake it. Drop the rift on her and recast Q through her for the double hit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's or Malignance sharpens your Q recast into real kill burst on a tank who hasn't stacked resists yet — force the all-in now, before her armor/MR turn your poke into a chip war she can sit through."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ (her threat)","text":"Her only win is landing her Frost-stacked E stun while your W is down — that lock lets her percent-HP W and her jungler collapse, so never commit a trade without Across the Veil up to break the stun setup."}],"wants":{"you":["Open every trade with Q (Twofold Hex) out-and-back poke and let Spirit Abjuration heal the chip — she has no ranged tool to trade the damage back","Hold W (Across the Veil) to break her Frost-stun setup, then all-in the instant her E is on cooldown","Close the game on your early poke lead — her 120s Glacial Prison is her only 1v1 answer, and she only gets tankier and more teamfight-relevant the longer it goes"],"foe":["Stack Frost with autos, land the E stun while your W is down, then percent-HP you with her W and call her jungler onto the lock","Soak the poke, build armor/MR, and survive to a teamfight where her R is a game-changing AOE stun","Walk you down between your W cooldowns so a single stun lands — she can't dash to you, so she has to force the spacing"]},"early":"Sejuani has no ranged tool at levels 2-3, so your Q (Twofold Hex) out-and-back chips her for free while she can only answer with autos. Spirit Abjuration heals back whatever her Frost-stacking autos chip off you, so you win the war of attrition as long as you stay spaced. The one thing that flips it is her E stun: she stacks Frost on you with autos and then her E locks you, so poke from outside her auto range, don't walk into her stacks, and keep W (Across the Veil) ready to break the setup. Stay disciplined and she literally cannot win the level-1-to-3 exchange.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your takeover. Your Q recast burst plus E (The Weirding) slow-and-hop out-damages anything a tank can return, and your passive eats her Frost-auto chip in the brawl. At 6 it gets one-sided: Between Worlds (R) lets you walk through walls and become untargetable to enemies outside the rift, so even a clean Glacial Prison whiffs against your spirit form — drop the rift on her, recast Q for the double hit, and your W resets on the takedown. Just respect the one trap: don't get caught with W down, because a Frost-stacked E stun is her only path to flipping a trade.","late":"The 1v1 stays yours — she's a tank, not a damage scaler, so she never out-DPSes your poke the way a Kayle or Mordekaiser would; she just gets harder to kill. The danger shifts off the lane: her R is a game-changing AOE stun in a teamfight, and her percent-HP W stays relevant against tanky targets. Convert your lane lead into objectives and a number advantage before that matters. In skirmishes keep using R to step out of her ult's reach and W to break her stun setup — as long as you don't get chain-CC'd with both down, she can't kill you, she can only peel for her carries.","whys":["You're a single-target mage with no escape at level 1 and she's a passive farm-tank who won't fight — neither side wants to commit, so the opener is a wash.","With Q out-and-back plus E online you start a poke war Sejuani has no ranged tool to answer, and your passive heals the chip her autos trade back.","Your Q recast and E slow out-chip a melee tank kit, and as long as you space her autos her Frost stacks expire before her E can stun.","Levels 4-5 your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all line up — you control every trade and her only counterplay is a stun you can blink away.","Between Worlds makes you untargetable outside the rift and your W resets on the takedown, so even a perfect Glacial Prison whiffs against your spirit form.","Luden's or Malignance sharpens your Q recast into real kill pressure while she's still building resists and can't trade the poke back.","She never out-DPSes you 1v1 as a tank, but her armor stacks up and her R becomes a teamfight engine — the lane is yours, the late map is a coin-flip."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"sett","win":["Aurora","Skill","Sett","Sett","Aurora","Sett","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your single Q (Twofold Hex) chips Sett before his grit-charged W is online — the last clean window where his true-damage W center can't punish you, since he has no E pull to lock your spacing yet."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Sett's E (Facebreaker) pull-stun into his grit-charged W deletes a chunk of your HP if your W (Across the Veil) leap is on cooldown and you can't dodge the smash."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds gives you a two-way teleport across the rift he cannot copy, but The Show Stopper grounds — once it lands, W and R are both locked out, so cross before he commits, never after."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Sett's bruiser first-item spike plus his grit W out-trades your burst — his sustain eats your poke, so don't sit in a prolonged trade war once he itemizes."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Q (Twofold Hex) and recast-pull at max range, then E (The Weirding) hop back before his E pull can lock you in","Bait his grit-charged W with a feint, then commit Q burst plus W leap only when his E pull is on cooldown","Cross the Between Worlds rift to sidestep his Haymaker centre, and leap before The Show Stopper grounds W and R"],"foe":["Land E (Facebreaker) to pull-stun you in place, then follow with the grit-charged true-damage W center","Build grit off the damage in your trades so his next W smash one-shots your trade window","Hit level 6 and chain Facebreaker into The Show Stopper — the grounding locks out her W leap and her R rift both"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: your Q (Twofold Hex) missile chips Sett before his W has any grit stored, and his only answer is to walk at you — last-hit at Q range and pull the curse back for the second hit. Once he has E (Facebreaker) at level 2-3 the lane flips. Never throw a Q from inside pull range; if his E lands and you have no W charged, the true-damage center of his grit-charged W punches through any trade you thought you won. Poke, then E (The Weirding) hop back the instant he steps up, and keep your W (Across the Veil) leap held purely as a pull-dodge — not as engage.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are Sett's grit window and you have to respect it. His passive double-punch and grit-charged Haymaker mean he out-trades you in any sustained exchange your spirit healing cannot keep up with, and the centre of that smash is true damage, so MR does nothing about it. At 6 you finally get a tool: Between Worlds gives you a two-way teleport across the rift that he has no way to copy. Bait Facebreaker on its 16s cooldown, cross the rift while it is down, then Q-burst. What you must not do is hold the rift until he presses The Show Stopper — it grounds, and grounding locks out Across the Veil and Between Worlds together.","late":"Past two items this stays a knife-fight, not a free win. Sett's bruiser scaling and grit-charged Haymaker still threaten to delete you the moment Facebreaker lands and your W is down — you are a squishy mage with one leap. Your edge is the W-reset snowball: catch him with a rift crossing in a skirmish, land Q burst, and your W refreshes off the takedown to peel out. Never facecheck for a pull, never trade into a full grit Haymaker, and never let The Show Stopper catch you holding a movement spell — its grounding locks both of yours. Pick him in the side lane with vision instead of brawling him head-on.","whys":["Your Q (Twofold Hex) poke and pull out-chip him at level 1 before his W has any grit stored, and he has no E pull yet to punish your spacing.","His E pull and your Q-recast both come online — it's a spacing duel where one missed leap or one landed pull decides the trade, so it's genuinely even.","Sett's E (Facebreaker) pull-stun into his grit-charged true-damage W punishes any Q you throw in range, and your W can't dodge a pull you didn't see coming.","His passive double-punch and grit-charged W out-trade your poke in sustained exchanges your spirit healing can't out-sustain.","Between Worlds hands you a two-way teleport Sett cannot follow, so you reclaim this window — but only if you cross before The Show Stopper grounds you.","Sett's bruiser first-item spike plus his grit W beats your prolonged poke trade — his sustain eats your chip before your burst finishes him.","It's a coin-flip skirmish: his pull-plus-smash can delete you, but your R-untargetable W-reset pick can delete him first if you catch his E off-cooldown."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"shen","win":["Skill","Shen","Shen","Skill","Skill","Shen","Shen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-out then Q-recall to pull the curse back through Shen for the double-hit while your passive spirits heal the return chip — punish him before his Q (Twilight Assault) empower and W zone are leveled."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds rifts him off the wave and the untargetable spirit window dodges his E taunt, but his global R (Stand United) means a won lane can save a losing teammate — ping the instant his ult is up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recall burst — force poke trades while his E taunt is on cooldown, since that dash is his only gap-closer onto you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Shen reclaims it: Twilight Assault's max-HP autos shred through your passive heals. Spirit's Refuge blocks attacks only, so keep casting Q and E through it — just never auto."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-out then Q-recall for the double-hit, then E to slow-and-hop backward before his E taunt dash can reach you","Stack passive spirit heals off your poke so he can't shove-and-roam or ult bot at full HP","Bait his E taunt, blink it with W into the spirit realm for the untargetable window, then punish the free trade with Q"],"foe":["Sit in his W zone to block your Q-recall autos, then E-taunt you into a Q-empowered auto chain","Soak your poke behind W and out-sustain to free up a global R (Stand United) for a fed lane","Scale into a tank that your passive heals can't out-damage — every Aurora lead bleeds out past 2 items"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you're a single-spell mage with no real escape yet, and Shen drops his W spirit zone over the minions to block your autos, so don't burn mana poking into it. The lane turns yours at 2-3: fire Q out, recast to pull the curse back through Shen for the double-hit, and let your passive spirits heal whatever his autos chip in return. Respect his E — it's a long taunt dash that locks you in place for a Q-empowered auto, so never poke from inside its range with your W blink on cooldown.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are your cleanest window: your Q-recall poke, E slow-and-hop, and stacked passive heals out-trade a Shen who can only shield-and-taunt before his W zone fully comes online. Bait the E taunt, blink it with the W leap into the spirit realm for the untargetable window, then punish the free trade with Q burst. At 6 it evens out — your R zones him off the wave, but Shen's global R (Stand United) means a won lane can become a lost game elsewhere, so track his ult cooldown and ping it the instant he's pressured.","late":"This is where Shen takes it back. He scales into a tank with Q-empowered autos and a W zone that blanks your poke, so once your W blink is down he taunts you and burns you through your passive heals while you're a squishy mage with no second escape. Your favour windows were early-mid — convert that lead into plates and tempo before he hits 2+ items, because in the 5v5 his global R save and front-line taunt swing fights your single-target poke can't carry.","whys":["You're a one-spell no-escape mage at level 1 and Shen just drops his W zone over his minions to block your autos — neither of you wins this, so set up the wave instead.","Q-out into Q-recall double-hits him while your passive spirits heal the trade, before his W zone and Q empower come fully online.","With Q-recall poke, E disengage and stacked passive heals you out-trade a Shen who can only shield-and-taunt — chip him whenever his E taunt is down.","At 6 it's a coin-flip — your R zones him off the wave, but his global R (Stand United) can win another lane, so map awareness decides this window, not the 1v1.","Your Luden's/Malignance poke spike is real, but Shen's tank scaling and W zone keep it a contested trade rather than a stomp once he itemizes.","Shen out-scales: his Q-empowered autos punish your W-blink cooldown windows and grind through the passive heals that carried you early.","In teamfights his global R save and front-line taunt swing fights your single-target poke can't carry — the squishy mage loses the 5v5 he was winning in lane."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"singed","win":["Singed","Singed","Singed","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Singed proxies your wave behind your turret, so there is no body in lane for your Q missile to curse or for the recast to pull through."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Your only clean window: poke with Q-missile, recast it back through him for the second hit, and E-blast to slow and hop away while Spirit Abjuration heals his poison back. Take it before he ults."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds lets you teleport across the rift to break his Fling-into-Mega-Adhesive run-down — cross before the goo lands, since it grounds W and R."},{"when":"Late","text":"His Liandry's drain-tank sustain plus permanent Insanity Potion move speed run you down before your Luden's burst kills him, and The Weirding's slow will never hold him for long."}],"wants":{"you":["Catch him standing still with Q missile, recast the curse back through him, and chip him while Spirit Abjuration heals the poison ticks","Leap with Across the Veil before Mega Adhesive lands, not after — the goo grounds you, and a grounded Aurora has no W and no R","Cross the Between Worlds rift to break his run-down rather than to commit an all-in you cannot finish"],"foe":["Proxy your wave behind your tower so you get no CS, no XP, and no target to poke","Fling you (E) onto Mega Adhesive (W) so the grounding locks your leap, then chase through his Q trail","Press Insanity Potion so its Grievous Wounds halves your spirit healing, then grind the long trade out"]},"early":"Singed will likely proxy your wave behind your turret, so there is nothing in lane to land your Q missile on and no body to pull the curse recast through. When he is present, never chase him through his Q (Poison Trail). If you step up to poke, keep W (Across the Veil) ready, because his E (Fling) will toss you onto his W (Mega Adhesive) and trail, and his move speed makes him impossible to disengage from once you are stuck. Farm safe and concede this phase.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your only real window. When he commits to a wave, hit him with the Q missile, recast it to pull the curse back through him for the second hit, and E-blast to slow and hop back while Spirit Abjuration heals you through his poison ticks; take it before Insanity Potion Grievous-Wounds that healing. At 6, Between Worlds is worth far more as an escape than an engage: cross the rift to break his Fling-and-chase, but cross before Mega Adhesive lands. The goo grounds, and grounded means no W and no R at all.","late":"This is where it slips fully out of your hands. A Liandry's drain-tank Singed out-sustains your Luden's poke, his Insanity Potion move speed means he runs you down whenever he wants, and its Grievous Wounds halves your spirit healing. Your rift crossing and W leap still keep you alive — provided you spend them before Mega Adhesive grounds you. You cannot kill him in a straight 1v1. Group, peel for your carries with The Weirding's slow and the R rift, and let your team body the run-down threat instead of duelling him.","whys":["He proxies behind your turret, so your Q missile and curse-recast have no target and you simply bleed CS and XP.","Still no body to poke, and if you step up his E (Fling) tosses you onto Mega Adhesive and his Q trail before your E can disengage.","His move speed plus poison run-down beats your spacing, and Spirit Abjuration cannot out-heal a sustained Poison Trail.","Your Q-missile-and-recast poke plus E-blast finally out-trades his step-ups, and your passive heals the poison ticks back.","Between Worlds gives you a two-way rift crossing to break his Fling-and-chase, owning this one safety window.","Your Luden's poke spike and his first drain-tank item roughly trade off, so neither of you cleanly wins the lane here.","His drain-tank sustain and Insanity Potion move speed out-last your burst, and its Grievous Wounds halves your spirit heal."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"sion","win":["Sion","Skill","Sion","Sion","Aurora","Sion","Sion"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Sion's Q (Decimating Smash) charges into a knockup that scales with charge time — fully charged it stuns for over two seconds. At level 1 you have only Q and no W leap yet, so respect the windup and never sit in the swing line."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q (Twofold Hex) curse-and-recall plus E (The Weirding) poke comes online, but his W (Soul Furnace) shield soaks the chip and recasts for max-HP AOE that MR will not reduce — trade into an empty shield only."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one clean window — the rift slows him and you can teleport side to side inside it, so a 10-second Decimating Smash charge whiffs while you burst and zone the wave."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Past two items his stacked HP and MR shrug off your Q-E poke, and his passive (Glory in Death) means killing him just buys a few seconds before his zombie form keeps diving — close the lane before this."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his W (Soul Furnace) shield empty with a single E or auto, then commit your Q curse-and-recall combo while his chip-absorb is on cooldown","Read his Q charge and leap with W (Across the Veil) so the knockup whiffs, then punish the long Q cooldown with free poke","Hit 6 and cross the R rift so his charge whiffs, all-in him or wall off the wave, resetting W on any takedown"],"foe":["Land a fully charged Q (Decimating Smash) knockup to lock you for a free combo or a jungle gank","Keep W (Soul Furnace) up through your poke and recast it for max-HP AOE so your chip nets nothing","Soak the wave safe, stack HP and MR, then use Glory in Death to keep diving you even after you score the kill"]},"early":"Sion is exactly the slow, immobile target Aurora's kit wants to kite, but his shield makes the early game his, not yours. At level 1 he can fully charge Q (Decimating Smash) for a two-plus-second knockup and you have only Q with no W leap to escape it, so play behind the wave and never stand in the swing line. Once Q (Twofold Hex) and E (The Weirding) are online you can open the poke war — fire Q to curse him, then recast to drag the curse back through him for the second hit, and use E to slow and hop yourself back out — but his W (Soul Furnace) shield soaks that chip and recasts as max-HP AOE, so only commit poke into a shield that's already down. Your passive (Spirit Abjuration) heals you off the spirits you exorcise, which keeps the trickle survivable, but his shield uptime still tilts these levels his way.","mid":"This is where Sion firmly edges you. He shields on cooldown with W, so your Q-recall and E-slow poke gets eaten for almost nothing, and a fully charged Q knockup punishes any greedy step-up — respect it and hold W (Across the Veil) purely to leap the charge. At 6 the math flips for exactly one window: Between Worlds slows him inside the rift and lets you teleport side to side, so his charge whiffs and that is your cleanest commit — burst him, and let the W reset-on-takedown snowball if you catch him low. Outside that spike, farm safe and count his shield: Soul Furnace is 15s at rank 1 and his Q only 10s, so the empty-shield window is real but short.","late":"You don't win the long game here. Two items in, his stacked HP and MR shrug off your Q-E poke entirely, and his passive (Glory in Death) means even landing the kill just hands him a few seconds of zombie form to keep diving — there's no clean solo kill on a fully tanky Sion. Your value shifts to zoning his Q windup with the R rift and chunking his backline in teamfights rather than dueling him. If you banked a level-6 lead, cash it into plates and tempo before his scaling makes him an unkillable frontline; if the lane is even, accept it and farm — this is a sub-50 matchup you survive and out-scale-around, not solo-stomp.","whys":["His charged Q (Decimating Smash) knocks you up for over two seconds and he is base-tanky — at level 1 you have only Q and no W leap to escape, so he owns this window.","Your Q-recall and E poke come online and Spirit Abjuration heals the trickle, but his recastable W (Soul Furnace) shield absorbs the chip — a true coin-flip decided by who reads the shield timer.","Even once W can dodge his slow Q, Soul Furnace refreshes on 15s while his Q is only 10s, so a mistimed leap eats a knockup and he keeps control of the trade pace pre-6.","He shields on cooldown and a fully charged Q knockup punishes any step-up, so he dictates every trade before ultimates are online.","Between Worlds slows him inside the rift and lets you cross it side to side, so his charge whiffs — your one clean commit, with a W reset-on-takedown if he is low.","Your first-item poke sharpens, but a tank first item climbs his HP and MR just as fast, so the poke war tilts back to the body that doesn't die.","Past two items his stacked HP and MR ignore your Q-E poke and Glory in Death lets him dive you even after dying — he reclaims the lane hard."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"swain","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-curse out, recast the pull for the second hit while your passive heals the trade — you out-poke Swain before his E-root into W combo is reliable."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds drops your all-in: rift him, leap the instant Nevermove snaps back, and burst him before his R banks souls. Vision of Empire reveals you, so leap outside it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst — chunk him under tower before his Q cone and Vision of Empire (W) come back up."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ (Swain)","text":"His biggest window is landing Nevermove (E) on its 12s cooldown while your W is down — that root into W-strike and R drain is the one thing that flips the duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Sidestep the return half of his Nevermove (E), then Q-curse and recast the second hit while your passive heals you through his Death's Hand poke","Hold W as the dodge for his 12s Nevermove, and never leap into a Vision of Empire zone — it reveals you","All-in at 6 with R rift + W-reset, closing the kill before his R soul-drain and Vision of Empire AoE stack up"],"foe":["Land Nevermove (E) while her W is down, then drop Vision of Empire — the zone reveals her spirit realm","Drag the trade into a long stand-and-drain fight where his R out-heals your poke once souls are stacked","Soak souls off your dying minions and farm safe until his stacked R wins extended AoE skirmishes"]},"early":"Swain's whole early threat is Nevermove (E) — a pair of demonic hands that fly out then snap back to root you on the return, and that root is the only thing that lets him land his Vision of Empire (W) strike and start a real trade. Don't stand creepwave-straight or you eat the return for free. Throw your Q-curse to poke, recast the pull for the bonus hit, and let your passive heal the chip back; his Death's Hand cone can't out-sustain your drain. At level 1 with one spell and no escape you both flounder, so just last-hit and dodge — but by 2-3 you own the poke war.","mid":"This is your window. Keep spacing so the return of his Nevermove misses, then E-blast to slow him and hop back out of his W range while you Q-recast for burst. Crucially, save your W leap as the dodge for that 12s root — if you blow it early and he roots you, his W-strike plus R drain is the one combo that out-trades you. Never leap into a Vision of Empire zone: it reveals stealth. At 6 your R flips every all-in: rift him so he is slowed, leap the moment the hands return, and delete him before his ult banks souls.","late":"Late-game Swain is the scarier champion in a stand-still teamfight — his R is a sustained AoE drain that heals him through your poke once he has stacked souls and built tanky AP, and Ravenous Flock keeps topping him up off every soul, so Grievous Wounds has to be on him before the fight, not during. Your edge is the early-mid lead you should already have, plus W mobility to pick him before he transforms. Never fight him inside a Vision of Empire zone, which reveals your leap. Flank, bait his root, and burst him with Q before the drain grinds you down.","whys":["You both have one spell, no escape, and no all-in — it's a coin-flip last-hitting stage and his Nevermove root is dodgeable with sidesteps.","Your Q-curse-and-recast out-pokes his Death's Hand cone while your passive heals it, and his E-root into W combo isn't reliable yet.","With Q plus E online you poke-and-disengage faster than he can land his Nevermove root, and his Vision of Empire can't catch you out of leap range.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all line up — you control the trade before his R drain exists to bail him out.","Between Worlds rifts and slows him the instant his Nevermove returns; you W-reset on the takedown before his ult banks any souls.","Your Luden's/Malignance burst spike outpaces his Q cone and W poke — chunk him before his abilities come back up.","Stacked-soul Swain with tanky AP out-sustains your poke in a long R drain fight, so the late teamfight tilts back to him."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"sylas","win":["Sylas","Sylas","Sylas","Sylas","Aurora","Sylas","Sylas"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Sylas points his E1 dash in, chains E2 to pull and stun you, then Q/W drains back to full through your Twofold Hex poke — his early all-in beats your one-spell start."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds plus the W-reset-on-takedown is your one clean all-in window — take it while Hijack is rank 1 and the steal is on 80 seconds."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"Once Hijack drops to 30 seconds at rank 3 he takes Between Worlds every fight — never press your ult while his R is up and waiting for it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His Q/W lifesteal turns him into an AP drain-tank that out-sustains your Spirit Abjuration heals and wins the even AP duel — you must have a lead banked by here."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q's curse then recast Twofold Hex to drag it back through Sylas for the second hit while your spirit heals sustain the trade","Hit level 6 and force the all-in with Between Worlds before he respects you enough to hold R","Bait his E1 dash, leap clear with W into the spirit realm, and re-poke with Q once his chain is on cooldown"],"foe":["Lead with E1, chain E2 for the dash-pull stun while your W is down, then Q/W drain back to full","Hold his R to hijack Between Worlds and turn her own slowing rift into the engage that lands on her","Out-sustain your poke with Q/W lifesteal and scale the even AP duel into an unkillable drain-tank past 2 items"]},"early":"Sylas wins the early scrap and you have to respect it. At level 1 you are a single-spell mage with no escape charged yet, while his Q already drains health back on every hit — don't walk up for a greedy Twofold Hex and eat free trades. From level 2 his E1 dash into E2 chain-pull stun is the trap: if it lands while your W is on cooldown, his Q/W drain combo heals through your poke and chunks you. Last-hit with the tip of your Q, let Spirit Abjuration spirits drift back and heal you, and only fire Q when you can immediately recast it to pull the curse back through him and disengage before he can dash on you.","mid":"Levels 4-5 Sylas still edges you because his Q/W lifesteal out-sustains your spirit heals in a straight poke war, so keep trades to single Q-recast pokes and leap the instant you see his 13s Abscond wind up. Level 6 is YOUR window and the whole matchup hinges on it: Between Worlds gives you a slowing rift you can cross side to side, plus the W-reset-on-takedown snowball, and at rank 1 his Hijack is on 80 seconds — that gap is the window. By rank 3 it is 30 seconds and it closes for good. Bait his E1, leap in with W, Q-pull through him, and only drop the rift when Hijack is already spent.","late":"This is Sylas's half of the game. He builds into an AP bruiser whose Q/W lifesteal makes him a drain-tank, so your poke stops mattering once his second item lands unless your Grievous Wounds landed first. Worse, Hijack is down to 30 seconds, so every fight he can take Between Worlds and your safety-net ult becomes his engage. Don't solo him at 2+ items — play for the lead you banked at 6, group so a stolen rift is wasted on a 1v1 he cannot get, and never leap your W in when his R is up and waiting to be turned back on you.","whys":["At level 1 Sylas already has Q drain healing him on every hit while you are a single-spell mage with no escape — he holds the edge, so deny his last-hits and don't trade into his point-blank drain.","Sylas gets E for the dash-pull stun plus the Q/W drain-heal — his level 2 all-in beats your one-spell poke and heals straight through it.","His E1-E2 chain-dash plus Q/W lifesteal out-trades you before your Spirit Abjuration can stack three spirits back, so keep leaping away with W.","A pre-item Sylas still out-sustains your poke war with Q/W drain — leap into the spirit realm with W when his E1 winds up rather than fighting the lifesteal.","Between Worlds' slowing rift and the W-reset-on-takedown is YOUR one clean all-in — strike while Hijack is still 80s at rank 1, because at rank 3 it is 30s.","His first AP item sharpens the drain-tank duel and a shorter Hijack takes your fresh Between Worlds — your poke spike cannot keep pace with Q/W lifesteal.","He out-scales the even AP fight hard — drain-tank Sylas duels you down and steals your own rift, so play safe and group instead of soloing him at 2+ items."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"tahmkench","win":["Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench","Skill","Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Tahm's Tongue Lash out-ranges your auto and his Thick Skin grey-health soaks your level-1 poke, so respect the slow-into-3-stack stun before you have W to leap out."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds turns you untargetable through his Tongue Lash and Abyssal Dive, so pop the rift to zone the wave and chunk him while his engage whiffs."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's Companion or Malignance sharpens your Q-recast burst, your best shot at out-pacing his Thick Skin regen before he stacks bruiser HP."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Tahm builds HP his Thick Skin grey health and health-scaling autos out-last your spirit poke, and Devour turns any skirmish into a pick."}],"wants":{"you":["Fire the Q missile then recast it back through him for the double-hit, exorcising spirits to heal before his Thick Skin caps the damage","Hold W until his Tongue Lash is thrown, then leap the slow and trade while his engage is on cooldown","Save R at 6 to go untargetable through his Tongue Lash and Abyssal Dive, then zone the wave for a clean chunk"],"foe":["Land Tongue Lash to slow you, stack his passive to the stun, then Abyssal Dive in for the all-in while your W is down","Soak your spirit poke into Thick Skin grey health and out-sustain you with his percent-HP regen","Stack bruiser HP and roam with his global R to snowball other lanes off a farm-even top"]},"early":"Tahm Kench out-ranges you at level 1 — Tongue Lash pokes from outside your auto range and slows you, and his Thick Skin grey health eats your early damage before it sticks. Respect the passive: three stacks of An Acquired Taste turns his next Tongue Lash into a stun, which sets up an Abyssal Dive all-in the instant you overstep without W. Once you have Q plus E, poke his real HP in bursts: fire the Q missile, recast it back through him for the second hit, and E to slow and hop away. Your poke only sticks before Thick Skin tops off, so trade in spikes — and never walk into Tongue Lash range with W on cooldown.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your window. Spirit Abjuration heals you off every spell that lands, and his only real threat is the Tongue Lash slow-into-stun, so bait it: hold W until you see the tongue thrown, leap over the slow, then burst with the Q-recast combo. At 6, Between Worlds makes you untargetable to both his Tongue Lash and his Abyssal Dive engage — pop it to zone the wave and chunk him while he can't answer. This is the stage to build a lead, because his Thick Skin sustain only scales harder from here once the HP stacks come online.","late":"This is where the lane slips back to him. Once Tahm stacks bruiser HP, Thick Skin grey health plus his percent-HP kit simply out-last your spirit poke — you chip him and he regens it before you can convert a kill. He also has his global R to roam off a stalemated lane, so a farm-even top becomes a losing map. Close it in the mid-phase: convert your level-6 and first-item windows into a CS and plate lead, then group, because the longer the 1v1 runs the more it belongs to him.","whys":["Tongue Lash out-ranges your auto and slows, his passive stun sets up Abyssal Dive, and you have one spell with no W escape — concede level 1 and last-hit safe.","His Thick Skin grey health already blunts your poke before your E or passive sustain is fully online — the lane stays his while you only have one trading tool.","With the Q-recast double-hit and E disengage you finally chip his real HP and heal off it — but Thick Skin still tops him off, so this window is roughly even.","Your passive heals stack and your Q-recast burst lands cleanly here while his sustain isn't yet HP-backed — bait the Tongue Lash and this stage is yours.","Between Worlds makes you untargetable to his Tongue Lash and Abyssal Dive, so you zone the wave and chunk him freely — your strongest window.","Your Luden's or Malignance spike sharpens the Q-recast burst, but it's a coin-flip against his Thick Skin regen as his HP stacking begins — skill decides it.","Thick Skin grey health and An Acquired Taste's health-scaling damage out-last your poke once he stacks HP, and Devour makes every skirmish a coin-flip."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"teemo","win":["Skill","Teemo","Teemo","Skill","Skill","Teemo","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Teemo's Q blind blanks the auto that follows your Q and the autos that fuel Spirit Abjuration, so your poke war stalls until your E is online to deal damage that the blind can't turn off."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your one clean window: the rift slows him, you go untargetable to him outside it, and with no dash he can't leave the realm — Q-curse, recast-pull, W on top, takedown resets W to chain out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance sharpens the Q-recast burst, but his Liandry's/Nashor poison and W move-speed kite scale with it too, so the burst window he simply blinds away stays his to dictate."},{"when":"Late","text":"R shrooms wall every choke and gank path, his Q blinds your engage auto the instant you commit, and your W/R approach lines get zoned — a kite game your poke-and-blink can't close past two items."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Q blind on a throwaway step, then E-slow and Q-recast burst before the blind cooldown refreshes","Hold for 6 — Between Worlds gives you an untargetable, wall-walking all-in his kite has no answer to","Chip with Q poke and heal it back through Spirit Abjuration to outlast his E poison instead of racing his raw range"],"foe":["Blind the auto behind your Q and your passive-stacking autos every trade, then kite back on W move speed","Layer E poison and Q so Spirit Abjuration never fully heals the trade and you're always behind on chip","Carpet your W/R escape lines and objective approaches with shrooms, zoning you off CS and vision"]},"early":"Teemo's Q blind defines the early game: it blanks the auto that follows your Q and shuts off the autos that stack Spirit Abjuration, so don't walk into his range just to land a missile he can negate. Last-hit at max Q range and lean on E for damage, since the blast slows him and hops you back out of his auto range without needing autos that the blind can cancel. His E poison out-chips your passive heal if you stand in it, so trade in short bursts, never extended, and don't chase him into brush where his W move speed lets him kite free.","mid":"Levels 4-5 he still edges you — the blind plus W-kite out-paces your poke war, because the committed auto-trades you want are exactly the ones he turns off. Your moment is 6: Between Worlds slows him, makes you untargetable to him from outside, and lets you walk the rift's walls, and with no dash he can't leave the realm. Land Q to curse, recast to pull and double-hit, leap W on top, and the takedown resets W so you can chain out. If he Flashes the rift, disengage — don't burn everything chasing a Teemo whose shrooms already cover his retreat.","late":"Past two items this slips away. Teemo becomes a map problem: R shrooms wall every choke and objective approach, cutting your W-leap and R escape lines, and his Q blinds your engage auto the second you commit. Your poke-and-blink pattern has to reach him, and a kiting Teemo with shroom vision never lets you close the gap. Convert your Level 6 and first-item windows into a lead and force the game before his shrooms own the map, because both the extended 1v1 and the splitpush go his way.","whys":["His Q blind cancels the auto behind your Q and your Spirit Abjuration stacks, so at level 1 you're a single-spell mage with no escape conceding the poke war.","With E online you trade through the blind via the slow-and-hop, dealing spell damage he can't negate and pulling the lane back toward even on your terms.","Through levels 4-5 his blind plus W move-speed kite out-paces your poke — every auto-trade you want is one he simply turns off.","His range and kite mean he dictates every trade tempo before 6, chipping you with E poison faster than your passive heals it.","Between Worlds slows him, makes you untargetable from outside the rift, and walls him in with no dash to escape — your W-reset-on-takedown owns this all-in.","Your Luden's poke spike sharpens the Q-recast burst, but his Liandry's poison and W kite scale right alongside it, keeping the trade window contested.","R shrooms wall your W and R escape lines and his Q blinds your engage, so his kite and splitpush reclaim the lane past two items."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"trundle","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Trundle owns the first level — his Frozen Domain move-speed/attack-speed zone and Chomp bite let him walk up and trade before your Q is a real threat, so hold spacing and don't get pulled into his W circle."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full kit unlocks: Twofold Hex out-and-back poke, The Weirding's slow-and-hop-back, and Across the Veil all online — start chipping from outside Chomp range while Spirit Abjuration heals you off the spirits you exorcise."},{"when":"Lvl 4-6","text":"Your cleanest zoning window — Q recast poke plus passive spirit-heal outpaces his sustain and he has no ranged answer at all. Bait Pillar of Ice, hop clear of the terrain on its 21s, and shove him off CS."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His drain-tank scaling flips it: Pillar-into-Subjugate steals your armor and MR and heals him full through your poke — burst and leave on Across the Veil, never sit in his Frozen Domain trading."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Twofold Hex out-and-back and The Weirding from outside Chomp range so Spirit Abjuration out-sustains his drain","Bait Pillar of Ice, then hop or leap clear before he walks you down in his Frozen Domain — the pillar is 21s at rank 1","Snowball your Lvl 3-6 ranged-poke lead and end the lane before his resist-steal Subjugate scaling takes over"],"foe":["Drop Pillar of Ice to wall off your Across the Veil reposition and pin you in Chomp range against terrain","Catch you in his Frozen Domain so his move/attack speed and Subjugate let him stick and drain you full","Soak your poke with his passive heal and Frozen Domain, then outscale into a two-item armor-and-MR-stealing drain monster"]},"early":"Trundle's Chomp steals attack damage, which is nearly dead weight against an AP mage, so his early trades lean on the Frozen Domain move/attack-speed zone and his passive heal rather than burst — at level 1 he can still walk you down inside that circle, so hold spacing until your kit comes online. Once you have Twofold Hex, chip him with the out-and-back recast and The Weirding from outside Chomp range and let Spirit Abjuration heal you off the spirits you exorcise. The one thing that ends you is Pillar of Filth: it walls your retreat and lets him pin you in melee, so never poke from a spot where a pillar can trap you against terrain.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are your window — Twofold Hex poke, passive spirit-healing, and the Across the Veil reset all line up, and Trundle has no answer to ranged chip until Subjugate exists. Bait his Pillar of Filth, then E-hop or Across the Veil out of the trap, and poke him down while his sustain can't keep pace. At 6 your ult lets you become untargetable and walk through walls to escape or zone, but his Subjugate steals your armor and MR and heals him, so use the rift to reposition and refuse the drain-trade, not to stand in it.","late":"This is where Trundle reclaims it. A two-item drain tank shrugs your poke, and his Pillar-into-Subjugate all-in heals him full while stealing your armor and MR — the exact extended fight your kit is built to avoid. Refuse the drawn-out trade: blink in with Across the Veil, burst, and leave before his sustain turns the fight; never linger in his Frozen Domain. If you didn't build a lead in your 3-6 window, sidelane and let your team handle the 1v1.","whys":["His Chomp bite is built to steal attack damage and out-trade melee, and inside his Frozen Domain his speed lets him stick before your Q is a threat — respect level 1 and hold spacing.","Trundle out-sustains a melee trade with his Frozen Domain and passive while you only have one spell up — neither of you converts here, so poke and back off rather than commit.","Twofold Hex's out-and-back recast plus The Weirding lets you chip from outside Chomp range while Spirit Abjuration heals you through his drain — your poke wins this level.","Your ranged poke, passive sustain, and Across the Veil cooldown align and he has no ranged answer or ult yet — own the zone and force him off CS.","Still your window at 6: Across the Veil and Between Worlds let you dodge his Pillar-into-Subjugate all-in and keep poking, and his sustain can't outrun your spirit-heal yet.","Your Luden's-class spike sharpens the poke, but if Across the Veil is down his pillar-trap can still catch you — it's a coinflip on whose tool lands first.","A two-item Trundle out-sustains your poke and his Pillar-into-Subjugate steals your armor and MR in the long fight — refuse the extended drain and let your team deal with him."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"tryndamere","win":["Aurora","Skill","Tryndamere","Tryndamere","Aurora","Tryndamere","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Level 1 is Tryndamere's — his Fury-stacked crit autos and Spinning Slash gap-close blow up a squishy mage, so don't walk into spin range to last-hit before you have Q+E online."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"With Twofold Hex (Q) poke plus Spirit Abjuration healing on every hit, you out-sustain his crit autos and Fury-starve him — he chases, whiffs, and gets nothing while you stay topped."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds (R) lets you walk the rift untargetable to him from outside, so his spin whiffs entirely, and the W-reset on a takedown snowballs the kill — he can't spin-kite what he can't hit."},{"when":"Late","text":"With crit items, Undying Rage's 5s immortality means your Q-W-E burst can't finish him — he face-tanks the combo, heals through it, and spin-kites you down on the next trade."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Twofold Hex (Q) out-and-pull, then E (The Weirding) to slow and hop back — chip his Fury bar down faster than his crit autos can heal off you","Hold Across the Veil (W) for his Spinning Slash engage — leap the instant he gaps in, drop into the spirit realm, and his spin hits air","Save Between Worlds (R) for his all-in — walk the rift untargetable so his crit autos whiff, then collect the W-reset kill"],"foe":["Stack Fury with autos, then Spinning Slash onto you and crit you down before your poke adds up","Catch you with your back turned, because Mocking Shout (W) only slows you if you are facing away","Survive to crit items, where Undying Rage lets him face-tank your full burst and outscale the lane"]},"early":"Level 1 belongs to Tryndamere — his Fury-fueled crit autos and Spinning Slash gap-close blow up a squishy single-target mage with no point-blank escape yet, so don't step into spin range to last-hit before you have Q and E. Once you hit 2-3 with Twofold Hex (Q) and The Weirding's slow-and-hop (E), flip it: land the Q out-and-pull, then E back so his autos never connect. Spirit Abjuration heals you off every spell and attack that lands, so the poke war is one-sided — he burns Fury chasing and walks away with nothing.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your window. Your Twofold Hex cooldown drops and the passive healing keeps you topped through any trade he forces, so out-poke him and never let his Fury bar sit full. The key skill: save Across the Veil (W) — not your E — for his Spinning Slash engage, leaping away the instant he gaps in so he's left spinning at air. At 6, Between Worlds (R) is the trump card: drop the rift, walk through it untargetable from outside so his crit autos whiff entirely, and cash the W-reset on the takedown to snowball the kill.","late":"This is where Tryndamere reclaims it. Once he has crit items, Undying Rage makes him immortal at 1 HP for 5 seconds — your Q-W-E burst and R commit just can't finish him, and he spin-kites away to heal back to full. You must convert your early-mid lead into a closed game or tower plates before that point. Late, never solo-commit: your burst can't kill through his ult, and if his Mocking Shout slow lands while your W is down, he runs you over.","whys":["Tryndamere's level-1 Fury crit autos plus Spinning Slash shred a squishy single-target mage with no escape yet — concede the first wave and farm safe.","With Twofold Hex's out-and-pull online you start a poke war his crit autos can't out-trade, and Spirit Abjuration heals back every bit of chip he lands.","Q plus The Weirding's slow-and-hop lets you space him completely — he can't close without eating poke, and his chase Fury-starves into nothing.","Your Twofold Hex cooldown and Spirit Abjuration healing line up so you out-sustain his crit autos and own every trade in the 4-6 window.","Between Worlds goes untargetable to him from outside the rift and W-resets on the takedown — he can't spin-kite what he can't hit.","Your first AP item sharpens the Twofold Hex poke-and-burst — keep forcing trades while his crit build is still bare and your healing wins the exchange.","Crit-item Tryndamere face-tanks your full burst behind Undying Rage's 5s immortality, then spin-kites away and outscales you — late game flips to him."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"urgot","win":["Aurora","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Urgot owns level 1: his Corrosive Charge leg deals percent-max-HP and the slow lets him walk you down before your Spirit Abjuration heal stacks or your recast-Q double-hit exists."},{"when":"Lvl 4-6","text":"Your poke window: fire Q, recast it to drag the curse back through him for the double-hit, and let the exorcised spirits heal the chip while his Disdain flip is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds is your swing turn: drop the rift and go untargetable so his E flip and his R fear-execute can't land, and a takedown resets Across the Veil for the snowball."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Urgot reclaims it: his percent-max-HP shred out-DPSes your poke in any sustained brawl, and Fear Beyond Death executes the instant a leap leaves you low."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q and recast it to drag the curse back through Urgot for the double-hit, then top off with Spirit Abjuration spirits","Use Across the Veil to leap his Disdain flip and reposition so his shotgun legs and R execute whiff","Win the levels 4-6 poke window and snowball Across-the-Veil resets before his percent-HP items come online"],"foe":["Land his Corrosive Charge slow to lock you in shotgun-leg range and grind your max HP","Hit Disdain to flip on top of you and start the sustained percent-HP brawl he wins","Drag you below the threshold so Fear Beyond Death fears and executes the kill"]},"early":"Respect his level 1 — Corrosive Charge slows you into shotgun range before your Spirit Abjuration has any spirits stacked or your recast-Q double-hit exists, so concede it and last-hit from max range. From 2-3 start the poke war: fire Q, recast it to pull the curse back through him for the second hit, and let the exorcised spirits heal you through his return chip. The trade you never take is standing still in Purge (W) — that is where his shred eats you — so poke and slide out on The Weirding's backward hop.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are mine. My Q poke, passive healing, and Across the Veil cooldown all line up, so I out-trade him whenever his Disdain flip is down and that flip is his only hard engage — which my leap dodges clean. At 6 Between Worlds is the swing: drop the rift to go untargetable and his E flip, his W shred, and his R fear-execute all whiff, and an Across-the-Veil reset on the takedown lets me snowball. Bait the flip, leap it, then Q-recast burst him while my spirits top me off.","late":"This is where Urgot takes the lane back. Once his items come online a sustained brawl out-DPSes your poke no matter how well you heal, and Fear Beyond Death executes you from 2500 units the moment a leap leaves you low. Never facecheck a Disdain flip late � it shields him as it lands, so one swap into his legs puts you straight into execute range. Convert the early-mid lead into objectives and end the game before the 2+ item mark.","whys":["Urgot owns level 1: his Corrosive Charge slow and percent-HP chip beat my single-spell start before my passive heal has spirits or recast-Q is online.","Still his at 2 — I have Q poke and a spirit heal, but his shotgun legs out-trade me the moment I sit in W range, so I can only chip and slide out.","Level 3 is a coinflip: my Q-recast double-hit and passive healing answer his chip, but his Corrosive slow still threatens a flip-in all-in either way.","Levels 4-5 swing to me — my poke, passive heal, and Across the Veil cooldown align so I control trades whenever his Disdain flip is down.","At 6 Between Worlds goes untargetable through his flip, his W shred, and his R execute, and the Across-the-Veil reset on takedown lets me snowball.","My first item sharpens the Q-recast burst, so I can convert a poke lead into a kill before his percent-HP items arrive.","Urgot reclaims it at 2+ items: his percent-max-HP shred out-DPSes my poke and Fear Beyond Death executes any leap that leaves me low."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"vayne","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Aurora","Skill","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"The Weirding's slow plus your Q recast starts a poke war before Vayne has range — but Silver Bolts counts abilities as well as autos, so her third hit of any kind is true damage."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds rift makes you untargetable to outside enemies — drop it on Vayne so her Condemn can't pick you, then W-leap in; the takedown resets your W."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's/Malignance spike turns one Q out-and-back combo into burst that deletes a no-items Vayne before she can Tumble away."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Vayne's window: Silver Bolts' percent-max-HP true damage plus a Condemn stun shred you the instant your W leap is on cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Fire Q through Vayne then recast it back through her for the double-hit before she Tumbles out of the return path","At 6, drop the R rift on her and W-leap in — the rift's untargetability blanks her Condemn while you burst","Snowball the W-reset-on-takedown lead and close the game before Vayne's second carry item comes online"],"foe":["Stack Silver Bolts to three autos and proc percent-max-HP true damage in any extended trade","Land Condemn to stun you into a wall the instant your W leap is on cooldown","Farm safely with Tumble behind minions and reach two carry items to flip the duel"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you are a one-spell mage with no escape and she has Tumble to reposition, so just last-hit at Q range and stay out of her auto-attack range. The moment you get E at 2 and your Q recast is online, the lane tilts your way: poke with Q out-and-back and the E blast-and-slow, and your Spirit Abjuration spirits heal the trade back. Her Silver Bolts need three straight autos to land their first true-damage tick, so short trade-and-retreat beats her — never let her free-cast onto you, but she cannot out-poke you this early.","mid":"This is your takeover window. Your Q double-hit plus E poke chips her down while your passive heals, and she is a squishy with no sustain to answer it. At 6, Between Worlds is the dagger — drop the rift on her so you're untargetable to her Condemn from outside, W-leap in, and burst; the takedown resets your W. Bait her Condemn into terrain (it only stuns when she pins you to a wall) and punish its long cooldown. First item sharpens the kill — one full Q combo can delete her here.","late":"Once Vayne has two carry items the matchup flips and you must respect it. Silver Bolts' percent-max-HP true damage plus her Tumble kiting out-DPS your poke, and a single Condemn stun while your W is down gets you killed. Don't chase her in a straight fight — your favor window was levels 2 through first item, so the game should already be closing. If it drags, use R to zone and peel for your team rather than dueling, and never face her 1v1 in a sidelane after two items.","whys":["You are a single-spell mage with no escape at 1, and Vayne's Condemn/Silver Bolts also need setup — last-hit at Q range and aim for the level-2 spike.","E's slow plus your Q recast come online and your Spirit Abjuration heals the trade — Silver Bolts still need three autos to threaten you back.","Your Q out-and-back double-hit out-pokes a squishy Vayne who has no sustain to answer your spirit healing.","Poke, passive healing, and her short trading range line up — you control trades and zoning before she has items.","Between Worlds makes you untargetable to her Condemn from outside the rift, and the takedown resets W to snowball the all-in.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike converts one Q combo into a kill before Vayne's carry items come online to save her.","Two carry items and Silver Bolts' percent-HP true damage flip the duel — her kite and a Condemn stun shred you once W is down."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"vladimir","win":["Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir","Skill","Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your one clean window: Q-curse then recast for the second hit, weave E for the slow-and-hop chip, and let your passive spirits heal the trade before his Q drain is online to undo it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"You want to R for the rift zone and W-leap on top to all-in, but the instant you commit he Sanguine Pools — untargetable, taking zero, your Q-recast burst whiffs while he heals inside your rift."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Riftmaker plus Rylai's flips it: his Q drain becomes real sustain, your spirit-poke stops netting health, and his E slow zones you off the wave for good."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-AP Vlad pools your committed burst, Zhonya's eats your follow-up, and his empowered-Q heals shrug off your poke — your leap is the only out and it's on cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the Lvl 2-3 window with Q curse-recast and E slow while your passive spirits heal the trade, before his Q drain comes online","Poke him into pooling, then commit your R-rift and Q burst only once Sanguine Pool is on cooldown","Convert any early lead before his first AP item — Riftmaker/Rylai's give you no path back"],"foe":["Take the early chip, then out-sustain it with Q drain once you stop landing clean poke","Pool (W) the instant she recasts Q or drops her R so the burst hits an untargetable Vlad","Stall to two items where Rylai's slow and Riftmaker sustain make him unkillable into her single-target kit"]},"early":"Vlad has one of the weakest level-1s in the game, but you are a single-spell mage with no escape until W comes up, so concede level 1, deny his Q last-hits, and set up your level 2. Your real window opens at 2-3: land Q to curse him, recast to drag it back for the second hit, and weave E for the slow-and-hop chip while your passive spirits heal whatever he trades back. The catch is short — once his Q drain is online it heals most of your poke straight back, so every Q has to land clean and you have to respect that you have no second escape if he steps up.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a knife-edge: your poke and W reset off takedowns line up, but his Q drain blunts any trade you don't land perfectly. At 6 the lane tips to him. Your instinct is to R for the rift and W-leap on top to all-in, but the moment you commit he hits Sanguine Pool, goes untargetable, takes zero from your rift, and your Q-recast burst whiffs while he heals inside it. Bait the pool FIRST — poke until he flashes it and it's on its long cooldown, then commit; otherwise you dump your whole kit into an invuln frame and hand him the trade.","late":"This is where you lose. Once Vlad finishes Riftmaker plus Rylai's, his Q drain is real sustain, his E slow zones you off the wave, and your spirit-poke stops netting you health because he just heals through it. Late-game he kites your single W leap, pools your committed R-and-Q all-in so it hits nothing, and adds Zhonya's so even a clean engage stalls while his empowered Q out-heals your damage. You needed to close this before two items — if you didn't, stop solo-committing into a full-AP Vlad and let your team apply the pressure.","whys":["Vlad has one of the weakest level-1s, but so do you — a single-spell mage with no escape until W, so deny his Q last-hits and set up your level 2 instead of forcing a fight you can't disengage.","With Q curse-recast plus E slow online you out-poke a pre-drain Vlad, and your passive spirits heal the chip he can't yet sustain back.","Your Q double-hit and E chip still beat his early Q drain — keep every Q clean so the spirit heal stays ahead of his sustain before it scales.","At 4-5 your poke and W reset line up, but his Q drain blunts any trade you misfire — it's a coin-flip, not a clear lead.","The instant you commit your R-rift and Q burst, Sanguine Pool makes him untargetable so it all hits nothing and he heals inside the rift — bait the pool first or waste the all-in.","Riftmaker and Rylai's turn his Q into permanent sustain — your spirit-poke stops netting health and his E slow zones you off the wave.","Full-AP Vlad pools your committed burst, Zhonya's eats the follow-up, and his empowered Q out-heals your poke — your single leap is the only escape, so play safe and let your team handle him."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"volibear","win":["Aurora","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q and E both online you open the poke war Voli can't return at range — curse him with Q, recast to pull it back for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal the chip his W bite can't out-trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds zones his all-in and W resets on takedown, so a kill on him refunds your leap — your hardest punish window against a melee with no ranged answer and only one gap-closer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-pull burst — force every poke trade now while his HP and resists are still thin and before his Q-into-stun threat gets reliable."},{"when":"Late","text":"His R disables your turret and shields him while his stacked HP eats your poke — at 2+ items he Q-runs in unstoppable and dives the instant your W is down, so close the lane before then."}],"wants":{"you":["Open the poke war at level 2-3 with Q curse plus E blast while his W bite is on cooldown and Spirit Abjuration heals the chip","Save W to dodge his Q unstoppable run-in so his stun whiffs, then recast Q to pull the curse back for a second hit","All-in at 6 with Between Worlds zoning him — a takedown resets your W and snowballs the lane before he scales"],"foe":["Land his Q empowered run for the unstoppable stun, then W-bite to heal through your poke and flip the trade while your leap is down","Drop Sky Splitter (E) on you from 1200 range for the slow, standing in it himself for the shield","Drag the game past two items where his R tower-disable dive and stacked HP shrug off your burst"]},"early":"Volibear's only early commit is the Q empowered run — he charges in unstoppable and the run ends in a stun when he reaches you; if that lands while your W is down you eat his W-bite combo. So don't burn your leap on poke — hold Across the Veil to dodge the Q run-in and his stun whiffs. Level 1 is a wash since you're a single-spell mage with no escape and he has no empowered Q yet, but from 2-3 you get Q and E online and the poke war begins: curse him with Q, recast to pull it back for the second hit, and let Spirit Abjuration heal you through whatever chip his bite gets in return. He can't win a poke war at melee range when your passive refunds the trade.","mid":"This is your window. Through 4-6 your Q cooldown drops, your passive healing stacks, and your W is up to dodge his one gap-closer — you control every trade. Bait his Q run, leap it so the stun whiffs, and poke him off the wave; his W bite heal can't out-pace your range. At 6 your R is the lane-winner: drop Between Worlds to zone his all-in, walk through walls untargetable if he commits, and remember a takedown on him resets your W so a kill snowballs straight into the next play.","late":"Respect the clock. Once Volibear hits 2+ items his stacked HP eats your poke and he becomes the unkillable brawler he's built to be — and his R disables your turret while shielding him, so a dive lands the moment your W leap is on cooldown. You don't out-DPS a fed Voli in a sustained fight. Use the lead you built early: take plates, roam with your R untargetability, and end the game before his scaling and tower-dive ult flip the matchup.","whys":["You're both weak at level 1 — you're a single-spell mage with no escape and he has no empowered Q yet, so neither side can commit.","Q and E come online and you open a poke war Voli can't answer at range, with Spirit Abjuration healing the chip his W bite can't out-trade.","Your Q-curse-and-pull out-pokes him and you W-leap his Q run so the unstoppable stun whiffs — he can't sustain the trade.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all line up, so you control trades and zone him before ultimates land.","Between Worlds zones his all-in, your R untargetability dodges his dive, and a takedown resets your W to snowball the lane.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-pull burst — keep forcing trades before his HP and resists stack up.","He out-scales hard: stacked HP shrugs off your poke and his R disables your turret to dive you the second your W is down."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"warwick","win":["Aurora","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Aurora","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q out then recast it back through Warwick for the double hit, layer the E slow, and let your Spirit Abjuration spirits heal the trade — he only has autos and Jaws of the Beast to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Both ult together: Between Worlds lets you become untargetable to him and walk a wall to dodge his Infinite Duress, but if he lands the suppress first you are stunned out of your own W and R."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's or a sheen/Malignance line sharpens your Q-recast burst so you can drop him while he's still above 50% — before Eternal Hunger's low-HP lifesteal even turns on."},{"when":"Late","text":"His window: Blood Hunt gives permanent move speed hunting you below half HP, so the moment Across the Veil is on cooldown he runs you down and Infinite Duress suppresses you for the team."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level 2-3 poke war: Q-curse, recast it back through him, stack E slows, and heal the trade with your three Spirit Abjuration spirits","Burst him from above 50% with the Q-recast combo plus first-item AP, before Eternal Hunger's low-HP lifesteal ramps to full","Hold Across the Veil and Between Worlds so Infinite Duress can never catch you with no dodge or untargetable window up"],"foe":["Hunt you with Blood Hunt move speed and chain Infinite Duress while your Across the Veil is down","Drag every trade past your spirit-heal window so his ramping Eternal Hunger lifesteal out-sustains your poke","Catch you below half HP where Blood Hunt frenzies him onto you and his lifesteal wins the drawn-out duel"]},"early":"Early is your window, but a tight one. Land Q, recast it back through Warwick for the second hit, stack the E slow on top, and your Spirit Abjuration spirits drift back to heal whatever he chips with autos and Jaws of the Beast — neither of you threatens a kill at level 1, so trade for last-hit priority. Don't let trades drag, though: the longer he fights the more his Eternal Hunger lifesteal feeds him, so chip-and-reset beats committing. Keep the E backward hop ready — it both pokes and pulls you out before he can close the gap.","mid":"At 6 it's an ultimate mind-game. Between Worlds zones him off you and turns you untargetable to anyone outside the rift, letting you walk a wall to break his angle, and Across the Veil resets on a takedown for the snowball. But respect Infinite Duress: a landed suppress stuns you out of your own W and R entirely, so never burn your leap proactively into a Warwick holding ult. Bait his all-in, E-slow him as he commits, dodge the suppress channel with W, then dump your Q-recast burst — trade his ult cooldown for your full combo and you win the exchange.","late":"This is where he reclaims the lane. Full-build Warwick gets permanent Blood Hunt move speed hunting any target below half HP, so he chases you across the map, and his ramping Eternal Hunger lifesteal turns every extended fight into a sustain war you lose. The instant Across the Veil is down you're a squishy with no escape and a guaranteed Infinite Duress waiting to suppress you for his team. Close on your early-mid leads and your first-item burst window; if it goes long, group, keep peel around you, and never get caught alone where Blood Hunt can run you down.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — you're a single-spell mage, he has autos plus Jaws of the Beast self-heal and no gap-close — so neither threatens a kill; set up the lane and last-hit.","With Q and E online you out-poke him: curse, recast back through him for the double hit, slow, and your Spirit Abjuration spirits heal the trade faster than his Q can answer.","Your poke owns this window — chip-and-reset so his Eternal Hunger low-HP lifesteal never ramps and his Q sustain can't cover the deficit.","Trades are even at 4-5: your poke is strong but going long feeds his lifesteal, so it's a wash decided by who over-commits first.","Your level-6 edge: Between Worlds makes you untargetable through a wall to dodge Infinite Duress, and W resets on takedowns — if you don't pre-burn your leap, you win the ult exchange.","First-item burst can drop him before Eternal Hunger's low-HP lifesteal turns on, but his sustain keeps the all-in honest — an even, mistake-punishing window.","Full-build Blood Hunt move speed runs you down and Infinite Duress suppresses you whenever Across the Veil is on cooldown, and his lifesteal out-duels you — play safe and let your team peel."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"wukong","win":["Aurora","Skill","Wukong","Wukong","Aurora","Wukong","Wukong"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Wukong's Crushing Blow (Q) hits harder than your single Q start and his passive armor blunts your autos — concede the level, last-hit at max Q-missile range, and don't walk into Nimbus Strike (E) range."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Your poke window opens: throw Twofold Hex (Q), recast to drag the curse back for the second hit, and use The Weirding (E) to slow-and-hop when he dashes — your passive heals the chip his armor-shred can't match against AP."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds (R) zones his Cyclone (R) all-in — walk the rift untargetable or bait his Warrior Trickster (W) clone, then Across the Veil (W) leap untargetable as the spin starts."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"Wukong's E-W-R chain is his kill window — if Across the Veil is down when he Nimbus Strikes in, the clone burst plus Cyclone knockup can lock you up and kill you outright."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the poke war with Twofold Hex curse-recall and The Weirding chip, healing it back through Spirit Abjuration stacks while his bonus armor sits useless against your magic","Hold Across the Veil for his Nimbus Strike dash-in so you can leap untargetable as Cyclone starts, then re-engage with the takedown reset","Use Between Worlds to walk the rift and zone his W-clone-into-R engage entirely, denying his one reliable lockdown on you"],"foe":["Land Nimbus Strike plus a Warrior Trickster clone to bait your Across the Veil leap, then commit Cyclone while your dodge is on cooldown","Stack passive armor and ride the clone juke to survive your poke until his bruiser items come online and the lane flips to all-ins","Catch you with the Cyclone knockup the instant your W is down — his only reliable hard lockdown on a slippery untargetable mage"]},"early":"Wukong's level-1 is the stronger one — Crushing Blow (Q) out-damages your single-spell start and his passive armor blunts your autos, so concede the level and last-hit at the tip of your Q missile. Once you have Q and E online around 3 it evens out: throw Twofold Hex, recast to drag the curse back for the second hit, and use The Weirding to slow-and-hop backward if he Nimbus-Strikes at you. His armor and Q armor-shred do nothing against your AP, so don't fear extended pokes — your passive heals the chip back. Just respect his E dash, because pre-6 you have no Across the Veil escape from a level-3 all-in.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are your window — your Q cooldown drops, your Spirit Abjuration sustain is rolling, and his armor stacks are wasted against your magic, so you out-poke him cleanly with curse-recall and E chip. At 6 it gets honest: Cyclone is a real knockup all-in, and his Warrior Trickster clone is built to bait your Across the Veil leap. Hold W for his Nimbus Strike commitment, then leap untargetable as the spin starts, or use Between Worlds to walk the rift and zone his engage entirely. Watch the clone — chase the wrong one and you eat his real burst plus a free Cyclone.","late":"This stays a coin-flip skirmish lane into the mid-game — you're a real poke-and-burst threat with your first item, but Wukong scales into a brutal teamfight diver whose Cyclone can knock up your whole backline. Your edge is the 1v1 picks: catch him alone, land the Q curse-recall burst, and use Between Worlds untargetability to deny his clone-and-spin all-in. Don't facecheck for his Warrior Trickster clone near objectives, and keep Across the Veil up — once your leap is on cooldown his E-W-R chain is the one combo that locks you down and kills you.","whys":["Wukong's Crushing Blow out-damages your single-spell level-1 and his passive armor blunts your autos — you have no Across the Veil escape yet, so concede it.","Your Q-plus-E poke comes online but his Nimbus Strike dash all-in still threatens — neither side owns levels 3-5 cleanly, so trade carefully at Q-missile range.","With Twofold Hex curse-recall and The Weirding slow you start the poke war his armor-shred can't answer, and Spirit Abjuration heals the chip back.","Your Q cooldown, passive healing, and W reset line up before ultimates while his stacked armor is dead weight against your AP.","His Cyclone knockup all-in arrives but Between Worlds zones it and Across the Veil leaps you untargetable through the clone bait — a genuine even all-in window.","Your Luden's/Malignance first-item spike sharpens the curse-recall burst and out-paces his bruiser item curve, so you win the mid-game skirmish picks.","Wukong scales into a teamfight diver whose Cyclone catches your whole backline, and outside the 1v1 his armor and tankiness outvalue your picks — close games before he groups."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"yasuo","win":["Aurora","Skill","Yasuo","Yasuo","Aurora","Yasuo","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Your Q missile and E-slow come online before his trade loop matures — but bait Windwall with the first Q, because a naked Q-recast into a held wall does nothing and wastes your only ranged tool."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds makes you untargetable to him from outside the rift, so it blanks his R (he can only ult an airborne target anyway) and lets you all-in without eating his Q3 knockup."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance Q-E-Q rotation spikes the same time his first crit item (IE/Shieldbow) does — even window where whoever lands their full combo first wins the trade."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With two crit items Yasuo Windwalls your key cast every fight and out-DPS-duels you — your poke gets walled and your W hop is your only safe exit. Don't be even here, be ahead."}],"wants":{"you":["Throw Twofold Hex first to draw out Wind Wall, then trade through the 25-second dead window with The Weirding and your recast","Hop with W to dodge his Q3 knockup or his R, and chain the W reset off any takedown to keep your exit up","Drop Between Worlds at 6 and all-in from inside the rift before his second crit item comes online"],"foe":["Hold Wind Wall (25s at rank 1) to eat your Twofold Hex missile, then walk you down","Stack Q tornado off minion dashes and land the Q3 knockup to enable his R follow-up","Scale to two crit items and turn every Windwall'd trade into a won crit duel"]},"early":"Yasuo's Windwall is the whole early game — it eats your Q missile, your curse-pull recast and your E blast outright, so never throw a naked Q into a held wall. Bait it: fire the first Q to draw the wall, then recast the curse-pull and E-slow him once it's down, chipping him while your passive spirits drift back and heal the trade. Respect his Q tornado range and don't feed him flow shield off free pokes; level 1 is a wash, then you start favoring as your Q-E poke and passive sustain come online at 2-3.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your window. Your Q-E poke, passive spirit healing and W hop all line up, and he can't Windwall forever — once it's on its long cooldown, E-slow him and recast Q for a real chunk. At 6, Between Worlds answers his whole kit: stepping into the rift makes you untargetable to him from outside, so his Q3 knockup and R can't catch you, and a W reset off the takedown snowballs the lane. Force the all-in here, before his crit items come online.","late":"Once Yasuo has two crit items (IE plus a Shieldbow or Bloodthirster), he out-scales you outright. He saves Windwall for your key cast every fight, walls your burst, then crit-autos through you — your W hop is your only out and your poke gets eaten. You must already be ahead from the 4-6 window; an even late game is a losing one, so close the lane or pivot to picking him off the side with your rift before teamfights start.","whys":["Yasuo holds Windwall to eat your Q missile and your level-1 Q does nothing into it — but he has the same weak, low-range start, so it nets out even.","His flow shield and Q tornado contest your trades while neither side's pattern is complete — your W exit isn't up yet either, so it's a coin-flip skirmish.","By 3 your Q-recast and E-slow let you bait the wall and pull the curse back through the dead window — you out-poke a no-Windwall trade and your spirits heal it back.","Your passive spirit sustain out-lasts his poke and your W dodges his Q3 knockup, so you control the trade tempo before either ultimate is online.","Between Worlds makes you untargetable to him from outside the rift, blanking his R follow-up while W-reset takedowns snowball — this is your clearest spike of the lane.","Your Luden's/Malignance poke spike lands the same time as his first crit item — an even item window where whoever lands their full combo first takes the trade.","Two crit items plus a saved Windwall on every key cast lets him wall your burst and crit-duel through you — he out-scales hard, so you must already be ahead."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"yone","win":["Aurora","Skill","Yone","Yone","Aurora","Yone","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q out-then-pull comes online for the double-hit, and each spell exorcises a spirit that drifts back to heal you — so you out-sustain his Q-strike pokes."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds drops a rift on his E body-return spot; pull him in with Q while he's locked out of his snap-back, and W resets on the takedown to snowball."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Luden's/Malignance sharpens the Q-pull burst window — cash the lead in before his first crit item turns even trades in his favor."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Yone's window: full crit plus his E body-snap escape and R dash-knockup let him close, all-in, and reset fights you can't pin him in."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q out, recast to pull the curse back through him for the double-hit poke, and let each spirit that drifts back top you off through the trade","Hit 6 and drop Between Worlds onto his E body-return spot, pull him in while he's denied the snap-back, then W-leap the takedown for the reset","Win the early-mid poke window before his 2+ item crit spike, where his Q-strike DPS and R knockup out-duel you"],"foe":["Land all three Q casts for the knockup-dash gap-close and ride the W cleave onto you while your W leap is down","Bait your W leap or E hop, then end Soul Unbound to body-snap back to safety and reset the trade on his terms","Stall to 2+ items where crit, the W double-hit, and the R dash-knockup make him a mobile carry you can no longer kite"]},"early":"Level 1 is a real toss-up — you're a one-spell mage with a clunky escape and his Q-strike trades just as hard, so last-hit and don't walk into his Q range to throw a hex he can dash through and stat-check. From Level 2-3 you take over: fire Q out, recast to pull the curse back through him for the double-hit, and let each spirit Spirit Abjuration exorcises drift back to heal you through whatever he pokes back. Hold W — it's your reposition tool, not a chase button — and keep it for dodging his triple-Q knockup-dash, not for poking.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your control window. Your Q double-hit poke, the passive heal stacks, and your W cooldown line up so you win every short trade, and his E (Soul Unbound) is the tell — he snaps back to the body he left behind when it ends, so plant your Q-pull on that return spot. At 6 drop Between Worlds on the snap-back point: pull him in while the rift slows him and he's locked out of escaping cleanly, then W-leap a low Yone for the takedown reset. Don't extend into his Q3 + W cleave with your W on cooldown.","late":"This flips hard once Yone hits 2+ items. Full crit plus his E body-snap escape and R dash-knockup turn him into a mobile carry who out-duels you in extended fights and shrugs off your poke between his dashes. Your favor was the early-mid poke window, so close the game before that crit spike lands — take plates off the Q poke, roam with your R wall-walk to make picks elsewhere, and refuse the drawn-out 1v1 you no longer win.","whys":["You're a single-spell mage with a clunky escape at level 1 and his Q-strike trades even — last-hit and set up rather than throwing a hex he dashes through.","Q-out-then-pull double-hit comes online and every spell exorcises a spirit that heals you, so you out-trade his Q-strike pokes.","Your full Q-pull double-hit out-pokes him while Spirit Abjuration's heal stacks sustain you through his return damage.","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all line up — you control short trades before either ultimate matters.","Between Worlds zones his E body-return spot and the W-reset-on-takedown lets one pull snowball the lane.","Your Luden's/Malignance spike sharpens the Q-pull burst — keep forcing trades on his E snap-back point.","He out-scales you: full-crit Yone with the E body-snap and R dash-knockup out-duels you once his crit items come online."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"yorick","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-curse-then-recast-pull plus The Weirding chip him faster than Last Rites (Q, 6s) heals it back — that heal is why anti-heal is core."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds crosses Dark Procession (W, 20s) so his cage cannot hold you, instead of being slowed by Mourning Mist and ground out by his ghouls."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Q burst spike races his Maiden timing — your last clean window to kill him before four graves make every trade a 2v1."},{"when":"Late","text":"Maiden plus the ghoul swarm and his W wall own the side-lane 1v1 — Yorick splitpushes you off the map once he hits two items."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Q-pull and E spirit blasts before Yorick banks four graves for Maiden","Use Across the Veil and Between Worlds to cross Dark Procession's cage and leave the ghoul swarm","Burst him in the early-mid window and roam — never duel him 1v1 in the side-lane late"],"foe":["Cage you with Dark Procession (W) so Mourning Mist ghouls and autos free-hit you","Stack four graves to raise Maiden and turn every trade into a 2v1","Drop W wall to cut your escape and out-splitpush you off the map late"]},"early":"\"Yorick at levels 1-2 is a melee with a couple of ghouls and no gap-closer, so start the poke war the instant you have Q. Curse him with Twofold Hex, recast to pull the curse back for the second hit, and weave E spirit blasts to chip him while your passive heals you off the spirits you exorcise. Respect two spells: Dark Procession (W, 20s) is the destructible cage that boxes you in, and Mourning Mist (E, 12s, 700 range) shreds armour, slows and marks you so his ghouls sprint at you.\"","mid":"\"Levels 4-6 are your window — your Q cooldown and passive healing line up so you out-trade a Yorick who can't chase your W leap. At 6, Between Worlds answers his cage: the rift crosses Dark Procession's wall instead of you being slowed by Mourning Mist and chewed up by ghouls inside it, and a W reset off a takedown snowballs you ahead of his graves. Bait Mourning Mist, leap out with W when ghouls swarm, and try to burst him down before Maiden is ever a factor.\"","late":"\"This is Yorick's lane and you can't fight him straight. With Maiden up and his W wall boxing you in, the side-lane 1v1 is his — the ghoul swarm and Maiden's sustained DPS out-grind your poke the moment your burst stops one-shotting him. Don't try to splitpush against him: group, use R untargetability and W mobility to roam and pick squishies, and make the map matter before his splitpush ends the game. Close it before he has two items or you lose the macro war.\"","whys":["Yorick has ghouls and a strong base kit at level 1 but no gap-close, and you're a one-spell mage with no W escape yet — neither side wins it, so set up the wave.","With Q online you curse-and-pull for two hits while he can only shuffle up behind ghouls — your poke out-paces his sustain before Maiden exists.","Q plus E chips him off CS and your W dodges his ghoul autos; he can't punish your spacing without burning Dark Procession (W, 20s).","Your poke, passive healing, and W cooldown all align — you control trades and zoning while he's still banking graves toward Maiden.","Between Worlds crosses Dark Procession's wall to all-in or escape, so you own the level-6 window before his four graves finish stacking toward Maiden.","Your first-item Q burst spike still races his Maiden timing, so a clean combo can kill him — but it's the last clean window before the lane goes 2v1.","Yorick out-scales hard: Maiden, the ghoul swarm and his W wall win the side-lane 1v1 and his splitpush ends games — play safe and roam instead of dueling."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"zac","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Zac"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q (Twofold Hex) plus E (The Weirding) online — open the poke war and chip his health bar before his passive blobs (dropped off cast/minion kills) let him scoop sustain back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R (Between Worlds, 140s) drops a slowing zone you can teleport across, so his Elastic Slingshot knock-up and Q/W chain miss, then Q-burst and the W-takedown reset close it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Luden's Companion / Malignance spike sharpens the Q recast double-hit so each poke pattern chunks more than his blob-pickup heals back."},{"when":"Lvl 3+ (his)","text":"His threat is E (Elastic Slingshot, 21s) catching you when your W is on cooldown, then Q (Stretching Strikes) knock-up into W (Unstable Matter, flat 5s) to hold you for a gank."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q (Twofold Hex) then recast to pull the curse back through him for the second hit, doubling your poke before his blobs heal his bar","Save W (Across the Veil) to blink his E (Elastic Slingshot) engage instead of burning it offensively, so he can never pin you for a gank","At 6 drop R to slow and zone, teleport across the rift out of his CC, then Q-burst and leap on the takedown for the W reset"],"foe":["Land Elastic Slingshot (21s) the moment your 22s blink is down — its knock-up also cancels the leap if you react late","Soak your poke and refill his health by walking over the passive blobs his casts and minion kills drop","Knock you up with Q (Stretching Strikes) into W and hold you in CC for his jungler while you can't blink out"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — you're a single-spell mage with no escape yet, and Zac is a slow blob with no gap-closer until E at level 2-3, so neither of you can force a kill; just last-hit and stack passive spirits. From level 2 you take over: throw Q (Twofold Hex), recast to drag the curse back through him for the second hit, and weave E (The Weirding) to slow-and-hop backward so his short-range Q/W CC never lands. His passive lets him heal by walking over the blobs his casts and kills drop, so poke him while he's last-hitting before he scoops them, and never linger in E (Elastic Slingshot) range with your W already spent.","mid":"This is your window. Your poke, passive spirit healing, and W cooldown all line up, so you out-chip a tank who only trades evenly and can't chase your blink. At 6 your R (Between Worlds) is the haymaker — drop the rift to slow and zone, then teleport across the rift away from his E engage and Q/W chain, then Q-burst and W-leap on the takedown for the cooldown reset. Keep him low enough that one Q recast finishes him before his blob pickups heal the bar back, and bait his E before committing so he can't slingshot away or onto you.","late":"You hold the 1v1 here too — Zac is an off-meta top tank who trades evenly and gives no solo kill pressure, so your poke-and-blink keeps winning lane. The danger isn't his dueling, it's his roam: his long E (Elastic Slingshot) is a flank and engage tool for his team, so respect that he can leave lane to start fights or peel a gank elsewhere. Convert your lane lead into towers and grouped picks before the game turns into a teamfight where his frontline tankiness and engage matter more than your lane edge.","whys":["Both are weak at level 1 — you have one spell and no escape, he's a slow blob with no gap-closer until E, so it's a wash; just last-hit and stack spirits.","Q and E come online and you open the poke war — recast-pull the curse through him while your E-hop keeps you out of his short-range Q/W CC.","Your passive spirit healing sustains a trade his even-trading blob can't win, and he can't chase your W leap to punish you back.","Your poke, spirit healing, and W cooldown all line up, letting you control trades and zoning against an immobile tank before ults.","Between Worlds (140s) teleports you across its own zone away from his Elastic Slingshot knock-up, then Q-burst plus the W reset closes the all-in.","Your first-item spike sharpens the Q recast, but a tank stacking health and blob pickups closes it back to even here.","He's even-trading and easy to isolate, but as a tank he scales into teamfight frontline and engage value — close the lane and group before that matters."]},
  {"a":"aurora","b":"ziggs","win":["Ziggs","Skill","Aurora","Ziggs","Aurora","Ziggs","Ziggs"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Ziggs opens the poke war the moment you step up — Bouncing Bomb (Q) is 6s at rank 1 to your 9s, so concede the first few CS and let Spirit Abjuration top you off the wave instead of trading."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Across the Veil (22s) finally jumps his bomb range — but Satchel Charge is 20s and Hexplosive Minefield a flat 16s, so bait both, leap, Q and recast for the pull-back, and E away before the mines re-arm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Between Worlds (140s) is your one clean window — the rift crosses terrain to reach him through his mines and a takedown resets W so you exit clean. If you don't kill here, the lane slides to his scaling."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Ziggs's peak — Liandry's plus Rylai's turns his Q into a slowing artillery zone, and Satchel Charge's percent-health knockback cancels your W approach before you ever close the gap."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Satchel Charge (W) and Hexplosive Minefield (E), then W-leap across his bomb range to land a Q-and-recast curse combo before the mines re-arm to slow you","Reach Level 6 with summoners up so Between Worlds crosses terrain and forces the one all-in his poke can't answer, with W reset on the takedown to escape","Stack Spirit Abjuration off the wave to heal the Q chip and stay even, so you never have to recall behind and surrender the lane to his shove"],"foe":["Throw Bouncing Bomb (Q) from max range every time you walk up to last-hit, denying CS while never stepping into your Q or W range","Drop Hexplosive Minefield (16s) and Satchel Charge (20s) on your leap path so your 22s W lands into a slow or gets knocked straight back","Shove with bombs to siege the turret and scale into a 2+ item Liandry's/Rylai's artillery zone your blink-and-poke kit can't walk through"]},"early":"Ziggs out-ranges you from the first wave — Bouncing Bomb (Q) chips you every time you step up to last-hit, and nothing in your kit reaches back, so don't contest the Level 1 poke war. Lean on Spirit Abjuration to heal the chip off minions and stay topped instead of trading into his range. Your real opening is Levels 2-3: once Across the Veil (W) is up you can leap his bomb range, land Q and recast it for the second curse hit, then hop out with The Weirding (E) before his Satchel Charge knocks you back. Bait his Satchel and Hexplosive Minefield first — the only time your gap-close is safe is when both are on cooldown.","mid":"Levels 4-5 swing back to him: his bombs cool down faster, he out-pushes you to siege, and every step toward the wave eats Q poke you can't trade back evenly. Hold a freeze on your side so he has to walk into your W range to do anything. Level 6 is your window — Between Worlds crosses the rift through his mines and bombs, so save it for a committed all-in, not a panic escape. Land the rift, W onto him, Q-recast for the burst, and the takedown resets W to get out. If you don't kill at 6, the lane tilts back toward his scaling.","late":"This is where Ziggs reclaims it for good. With Liandry's and Rylai's online his artillery poke zones whole sections of the map — Q chunks you on cooldown, Satchel Charge (W) knocks you off any engage, and Hexplosive Minefield (E) walls your W and R approach with slows. Your poke-and-blink pattern has to get into range, and a fed Ziggs simply never lets you. Don't solo him in the open; group with vision, fight near walls where Between Worlds' wall-crossing matters most, and let your frontline eat the bombs so you can W-flank his backline instead of facetanking the siege.","whys":["Bouncing Bomb (Q) is 6s at rank 1 against your 9s — he pokes you off CS for free while your only answer is Spirit Abjuration sustain.","The lane is even only in your Level 2-3 window and only while his Satchel and Minefield are down — whoever times the cooldowns better takes the trade, so it comes down to skill.","Across the Veil lets you leap his bomb range and land a Q-recast curse combo — bait his Satchel and Minefield, jump in, and disengage with E before the mines re-arm.","Satchel Charge (20s) and Hexplosive Minefield (16s) both beat your 22s leap, so every step to the wave eats Q poke — freeze and farm safe through 4-5.","Between Worlds (140s) crosses terrain straight onto him past his mines — your one clean all-in, and the takedown resets W so you escape even if you don't finish.","His first-item artillery (Liandry's) out-pokes your Riftmaker spike — he zones the wave and chips you down faster than you can ever close the gap.","Full Liandry's/Rylai's artillery zones you out completely — his siege and Satchel knockback shut down your W approach, so group and let your team soak the bombs."]}
