window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"aurora","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Your full spirit-poke pattern settles in — the chip war begins in earnest, and W discipline decides who wins it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Base ults and totems roughly trade — an even stage until someone's ultimate actually connects."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Purgatory grounds you, so the W escape cannot fire inside it and the execute lands. Step out of the zone before you ever need the hop."},{"when":"Late","text":"A bursty coinflip — whoever lands their combo first deletes the other, so open from fog and keep the exit pre-planned."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke without burning W","W held for his commit","HP above execute range"],"foe":["Bait out your W hop","Chip you toward totem range","R timed on your escape"]},"early":"An even chip war through 1-5. Your spirit poke matches his on-hit trades, so keep the damage flowing but treat W as sacred — it's your only real out, and every trade he wins starts with your hop being down. Poke, reposition, and let the lane stay farm-heavy while you scale.","mid":"Level 6 stays even until someone's ult connects, but his first item is the stage to fear: Purgatory can execute you before the W escape even fires. Keep your HP out of totem range, hold the hop exclusively for his engage, and if his R is up, simply refuse to fight anywhere near even health.","late":"Two-plus items it's a bursty coinflip — whoever lands their combo first deletes the other. Fight off your own vision, open from fog or max range, and always keep the W exit pre-planned. In teamfights your zone control beats his pick pattern, so force the messy fight, not the duel.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your poke and his on-hit trades cancel out, with neither side able to force anything more.","Level 2 stays a skill lane: your W hop is your only real out, so trades stay honest as long as you keep it in reserve.","Level 3 is a wash between your spirit poke and his walk-up pressure — whoever spaces better wins each exchange.","Levels 4-5 stay even and revolve around your W timing: hop too early and you eat the loss, hold it and every trade is fair.","Level 6 opens even — base ults and totems roughly trade, and neither of you can guarantee the kill yet.","First item is Locke's: Purgatory executes you before the W escape resolves. Stay above threshold health and save the hop strictly for his commit.","Late settles into a bursty coinflip — even on paper, decided by who lands the opening combo and who kept their escape."]});
