window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"aurora","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Aurora","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Aurora","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"Twofold Hex starts chipping a melee bruiser who has no answer at 900 — the bullying begins at level 2."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Across the Veil is 22s and Aureate Rush 10s — you cannot dodge them all."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your AP spike out-ranges his bruiser build, but buy anti-heal or The Darkin Glaive refunds it."},{"when":"Late","text":"A high-value mage he cannot reach while W is up — but Dreaded Return pulls from 850 and Determination revives him."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke every last hit","W saved for his E","Scale into range control"],"foe":["Catch your blink down","Sustain through the chip","Force melee at 4-5"]},"early":"Level 1 is mutual farming, then the poke war starts: at 2 Twofold Hex chips a melee from 900 who can't answer. Level 3 is not free — Aureate Rush (E) is 10s and Dreaded Return (W) pulls from 850 on 14s, against one 22s Across the Veil. Hold W for his commit. At 4-5 The Darkin Glaive's heal thickens him, so buy anti-heal.","mid":"Level 6 is his: Grim Deliverance is 110s and heals him off the damage he deals, and Determination can revive him, so your burst does not close. At first item you pull back ahead — AP Aurora out-ranges his build, so poke him below all-in range and blink out the moment he steps up with Aureate Rush.","late":"You've scaled into what he hates: a mage he cannot reach while W is up. Track both engages — Aureate Rush 10s, Dreaded Return 14s — and W only after one is spent, because you cannot beat both. In teamfights Between Worlds dictates the space and he walks all of it to reach you.","whys":["Level 1 is even — both of you just farm out of each other's effective range, with nothing worth forcing.","Aurora takes level 2: your ranged Q poke chips a melee bruiser who has no answer at that distance.","Level 3 is even — Aureate Rush is 10s and Dreaded Return 14s against one 22s blink, so you cannot beat both.","Levels 4-5 go to Zaahen: The Darkin Glaive heals him every 6-10s while Determination stacks bonus AD, so chip trades refund him and one caught blink ends you.","At 6 Zaahen is ahead — Grim Deliverance is 110s and heals off the damage it deals, and Determination can revive him, so Between Worlds' zone does not convert into a kill.","First item is Aurora's: the AP spike out-ranges and out-bursts his bruiser build, so he can no longer afford the walk-up.","Two-plus items are even — you out-range him, but Dreaded Return pulls from 850 and two gap-closers beat one 22s blink."]});
