window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"aurora","b":"masteryi","win":["Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Master Yi","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Full kiting poke plus the W blink — your untouchable phase peaks, and he still can't punish any of it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Little changes in the duel — Highlander ignores slows, so your R zones his team, not him — the lane stays a skill matchup."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His true-damage DPS spike: your squishy frame melts if he ever sticks. W becomes strictly an escape from here on."},{"when":"Late","text":"His resets take over the 1v1 and Highlander ignores your slows — win with walls and teammates."}],"wants":{"you":["Chip him every wave","Blink his Alpha Strike jump","Zone fights, never duels"],"foe":["Farm quietly to first item","Highlander past your slows","Resets in extended fights"]},"early":"Own the early lane. Your Q pokes him at 1 with zero reply, passive spirit damage stacks the level 2 trades your way, and level 3 completes the kite: poke, reposition, W away from anything he tries. Shove when he's low, deny CS, and bank the lead — his items are coming.","mid":"By 4 his Wuju points make trades honest and 6 changes little in the duel — your ult is a teamfight tool, not a dueling cheat — so the mid phase is a skill lane at range. The real alarm is his first item: from there his true damage melts your frame if he ever sticks, so hold W strictly to break his Alpha Strike.","late":"Do not duel him. Highlander is 85s and makes him immune to every slow you own, so your E and rift stop kiting him the moment he presses it. Play the map: waveclear from range, blink over walls when he commits, and fight only with teammates peeling. You outscale as a teamfighter; he outscales as your personal assassin.","whys":["Aurora owns level 1 — your Q pokes him freely and he has no tool to trade back with.","Level 2 stays yours: passive spirit damage stacks onto every exchange and keeps him bleeding.","Level 3 is yours outright — full kiting poke plus the W blink, and he still can't punish any of it.","By 4 his Wuju Style points bring the lane even, and Alpha Strike is untargetable mid-jump — hold burst.","Level 6 stays a skill stage: Highlander is immune to slows, so your R zones his team and not him — nothing shifts the 1v1 yet.","Master Yi takes first item: Wuju true damage out-DPSes your squishy frame the moment he sticks. Kite or leave.","Late is his in any duel — Highlander ignores every slow you have and resets on kills. Zone his team in fights and never sidelane alone."]});
